1
00:00:00,601 --> 00:00:03,069
(Their third morning in Thailand)

2
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:09,341
(Their lodging in Bangkok, 9:00 a.m.)

3
00:00:09,977 --> 00:00:10,843
Hello.

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:11,878
(Won Ji wakes up first.)

5
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,112
Good morning.

6
00:00:13,981 --> 00:00:16,449
I'm wearing the clothes
my Secret Santa got me yesterday.

7
00:00:16,717 --> 00:00:18,651
They were too long,

8
00:00:18,986 --> 00:00:21,054
so I cut off about a hand's length.

9
00:00:22,623 --> 00:00:23,423
It looks good, right?

10
00:00:23,424 --> 00:00:24,624
(Ta-da)

11
00:00:24,925 --> 00:00:27,793
I'm wearing pink today.

12
00:00:28,462 --> 00:00:30,830
Everyone is passed out right now.

13
00:00:30,831 --> 00:00:32,031
I should go wake them up.

14
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:32,965
They're up!

15
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:34,867
Hello.

16
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:35,769
Hi. Good morning.

17
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:36,869
Good morning.

18
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:38,871
(The queen shows up looking groggy.)

19
00:00:38,872 --> 00:00:39,672
She's up.

20
00:00:40,855 --> 00:00:41,774
What about upstairs?

21
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:43,109
I was about to check.

22
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:43,776
Peek-a-boo.

23
00:00:44,111 --> 00:00:45,044
Are you up?

24
00:00:45,145 --> 00:00:46,312
Good morning!

25
00:00:46,313 --> 00:00:47,646
Good morning.

26
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:49,215
Good morning.

27
00:00:49,416 --> 00:00:51,784
- You're wearing the pants I got you.
- I am.

28
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,387
I shortened them. What do you think?

29
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:55,822
You did! Good job.

30
00:00:55,823 --> 00:00:57,758
- It looks good, right?
- Nice.

31
00:00:57,759 --> 00:00:58,725
Cut what?

32
00:00:58,726 --> 00:00:59,592
The pants.

33
00:01:00,093 --> 00:01:01,326
(Impressed)

34
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:02,962
That's cute!

35
00:01:03,831 --> 00:01:06,065
(She's in a good mood as always.)

36
00:01:06,633 --> 00:01:08,934
I have nothing to do in the morning.

37
00:01:09,469 --> 00:01:11,437
I got bored, so I altered my pants.

38
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:12,738
I showered too.

39
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,039
(Fitting)

40
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,407
I'm hungry.

41
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:16,942
Should I use it as a headband?

42
00:01:17,811 --> 00:01:19,645
What if you wear it as a top?

43
00:01:19,646 --> 00:01:20,446
This?

44
00:01:21,782 --> 00:01:24,851
(The it girl is creative.)

45
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:26,853
This could be a headband.

46
00:01:26,854 --> 00:01:28,621
(This might be good as a headband.)

47
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,689
(Exclaiming)

48
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:32,118
Doesn't it look
like an actual headband like this?

49
00:01:32,226 --> 00:01:33,293
Yes, like a set.

50
00:01:34,395 --> 00:01:36,028
It really looks like a headband.

51
00:01:36,029 --> 00:01:36,862
(Loving it)

52
00:01:37,165 --> 00:01:40,433
This seems like it would
tear pretty easily.

53
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:41,234
(Giggling)

54
00:01:41,235 --> 00:01:42,135
It's really breathable.

55
00:01:43,136 --> 00:01:44,736
Do you want me to read your fortune today?

56
00:01:44,872 --> 00:01:46,072
- Sounds good.
- I do.

57
00:01:46,306 --> 00:01:48,240
There's a website that I like.

58
00:01:48,809 --> 00:01:49,642
What is it?

59
00:01:50,076 --> 00:01:51,310
- Naver fortune.
- Naver fortune?

60
00:01:51,311 --> 00:01:52,178
Really?

61
00:01:52,413 --> 00:01:53,612
What should I tell you?

62
00:01:54,281 --> 00:01:55,235
Your birthday and birth year.

63
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:57,150
(Typing)

64
00:01:57,151 --> 00:01:58,918
Today's overall fortune!

65
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,454
"Joyful!"

66
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:04,223
<i>Knock knocking a door</i>

67
00:02:04,424 --> 00:02:05,124
(Overwhelmed)

68
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,760
- Joyful.
- That's good.

69
00:02:07,761 --> 00:02:09,261
Today is the day...

70
00:02:09,262 --> 00:02:10,362
(Knocking)

71
00:02:10,531 --> 00:02:12,131
Sim Cheong meets the Dragon King.

72
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:13,032
Oh, my goodness!

73
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:17,036
"Things keep getting in the way..."

74
00:02:18,839 --> 00:02:21,573
"Things keep getting in the way
more than expected,"

75
00:02:21,574 --> 00:02:23,276
"and you keep messing up
because you're all over the place."

76
00:02:23,277 --> 00:02:24,410
What is that?

77
00:02:24,945 --> 00:02:26,379
You said it was joyful.

78
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,847
Did it mean "discouraged"
instead of "joyful?"

79
00:02:30,017 --> 00:02:32,585
I like that. I'm excited to start my day.

80
00:02:32,654 --> 00:02:36,255
Hye Rim's overall fortune today.

81
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:37,923
"Prepare ahead."

82
00:02:38,258 --> 00:02:39,792
- "Prepare ahead."
- "Prepare ahead."

83
00:02:39,793 --> 00:02:42,995
- Liu Bei and Zhang Fei.
- Liu Bei and Zhang Fei.

84
00:02:43,630 --> 00:02:45,998
Let's go, "Romance of the Three Kingdoms."

85
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,499
(Flustered)

86
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,101
Yours is "Prepare ahead."

87
00:02:49,469 --> 00:02:50,869
Gabee too.

88
00:02:50,870 --> 00:02:52,070
"Prepare ahead" for me too.

89
00:02:52,071 --> 00:02:53,839
(Cheering)

90
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:56,775
We're Liu Bei and Zhang Fei!

91
00:02:56,776 --> 00:02:59,678
We're the "Romance
of the Three Kingdoms" girls.

92
00:03:00,114 --> 00:03:02,648
By the way, I did some research.

93
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:03,484
On what?

94
00:03:03,784 --> 00:03:04,651
In Thailand...

95
00:03:04,652 --> 00:03:05,718
No way!

96
00:03:06,386 --> 00:03:07,186
Saju?

97
00:03:07,821 --> 00:03:10,356
It's like astrology.

98
00:03:10,357 --> 00:03:11,490
(It's like astrology.)

99
00:03:11,491 --> 00:03:12,424
I love that!

100
00:03:12,425 --> 00:03:13,692
There's a really famous place here.

101
00:03:14,428 --> 00:03:16,429
It's super famous.

102
00:03:16,563 --> 00:03:19,632
Thailand has its own form
of fortune-telling like saju.

103
00:03:19,633 --> 00:03:20,833
(She looked
up traditional Thai astrology.)

104
00:03:20,834 --> 00:03:22,235
It's a really famous place.

105
00:03:22,236 --> 00:03:23,369
- Do you want to check it out?
- Let's go!

106
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:24,303
I love that idea.

107
00:03:24,304 --> 00:03:25,804
Isn't it great?

108
00:03:25,805 --> 00:03:27,873
Let's see how compatible we are!

109
00:03:27,975 --> 00:03:29,229
There are a lot of ghosts in Thailand too.

110
00:03:29,977 --> 00:03:32,378
- That's fascinating.
- Their readings might be accurate.

111
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:33,379
I know.

112
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,414
And nearby,

113
00:03:35,415 --> 00:03:36,649
there's a talisman market.

114
00:03:37,184 --> 00:03:38,818
- Talisman?
- A talisman market?

115
00:03:38,819 --> 00:03:40,953
They sell...

116
00:03:41,355 --> 00:03:43,556
- Superstitious items?
- little superstitious items there.

117
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:45,592
- I like that.
- I love that!

118
00:03:45,793 --> 00:03:47,326
Let's have some fun there!

119
00:03:47,327 --> 00:03:49,061
- Let's have fun!
- Let's have fun!

120
00:03:49,296 --> 00:03:50,529
It's going to be so much fun!

121
00:03:51,365 --> 00:03:52,197
Let's have fun!

122
00:03:52,198 --> 00:03:53,966
(Promising to have fun)

123
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:54,901
Let's have a lot of fun.

124
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,970
I think we've gotten pretty close.

125
00:03:58,271 --> 00:04:00,373
Sian is less shy now.

126
00:04:00,875 --> 00:04:02,541
You don't have to worry about those two.

127
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:04,776
I've changed a lot too.

128
00:04:06,146 --> 00:04:07,246
I'm excited about today.

129
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:09,748
I'm looking forward to it.

130
00:04:11,152 --> 00:04:13,319
- I'll go change.
- Take your time.

131
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:14,820
I'll bring some pants.

132
00:04:15,722 --> 00:04:17,556
If this pair rips, I'll wear this.

133
00:04:17,557 --> 00:04:20,660
This? I need some hiking pants.

134
00:04:21,628 --> 00:04:23,262
Can I put in our towels?

135
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:26,899
Yes. If you have some towels
on the third floor, bring them with you.

136
00:04:27,067 --> 00:04:28,567
Let me look up a laundromat.

137
00:04:29,536 --> 00:04:30,436
There's one.

138
00:04:30,737 --> 00:04:31,570
Three minutes away on foot.

139
00:04:31,571 --> 00:04:32,604
(Finds where the laundromat is)

140
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:33,405
It's super close.

141
00:04:34,741 --> 00:04:35,908
Why is your bag so big?

142
00:04:35,909 --> 00:04:37,409
It's a laundry basket.

143
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:38,977
A laundry basket.

144
00:04:38,978 --> 00:04:40,712
(The laundry basket was in the lodging.)

145
00:04:41,381 --> 00:04:42,381
We have 2,160 baht left.

146
00:04:42,716 --> 00:04:43,983
- Our shared money?
- Yes.

147
00:04:43,984 --> 00:04:45,051
(They have about 100 dollars left.)

148
00:04:45,052 --> 00:04:46,819
We spent a lot yesterday...

149
00:04:47,053 --> 00:04:49,288
- We did.
- since we went pretty far.

150
00:04:49,923 --> 00:04:52,525
(Cheering)

151
00:04:52,693 --> 00:04:53,826
(The brush appears today too.)

152
00:04:53,827 --> 00:04:56,663
Come on.

153
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:58,531
Thank you.

154
00:04:59,166 --> 00:05:02,034
That's 4,000, 5,000, 6,000.

155
00:05:02,235 --> 00:05:04,403
Shall we contribute 1,000 baht each?

156
00:05:04,404 --> 00:05:05,337
Okay.

157
00:05:05,338 --> 00:05:06,338
It's 1,000 each.

158
00:05:06,606 --> 00:05:07,606
Okay.

159
00:05:07,941 --> 00:05:09,875
Let's do the laundry and go eat.

160
00:05:09,876 --> 00:05:11,510
- Let's get something to drink too.
- Okay.

161
00:05:12,045 --> 00:05:12,845
Let's go.

162
00:05:12,846 --> 00:05:14,346
Let's go.

163
00:05:14,447 --> 00:05:17,082
We just go straight. Hello.

164
00:05:17,083 --> 00:05:18,117
Hello.

165
00:05:18,385 --> 00:05:19,424
(Starting their day with greetings)

166
00:05:19,425 --> 00:05:20,586
Good morning.

167
00:05:21,621 --> 00:05:23,055
- It's nice.
- It's really nice.

168
00:05:23,557 --> 00:05:24,657
The weather is nice today.

169
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:25,758
It's pretty nice.

170
00:05:25,759 --> 00:05:26,893
(The perfect weather to do laundry)

171
00:05:27,994 --> 00:05:31,229
And we turn left here.

172
00:05:32,866 --> 00:05:33,866
Look at that.

173
00:05:34,734 --> 00:05:35,634
Hello.

174
00:05:36,236 --> 00:05:37,837
He has a lot of flowers on him.

175
00:05:38,606 --> 00:05:40,439
Did you notice...

176
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,975
that they all have shrines
in front of their houses?

177
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:45,344
- Did you see that?
- I did.

178
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:46,846
- There are so many.
- I know.

179
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:48,814
Every house has one.

180
00:05:50,083 --> 00:05:52,851
There it is. "Enjoy Laundry."

181
00:05:53,854 --> 00:05:56,222
- It looks nice.
- It's hip.

182
00:05:56,323 --> 00:05:58,925
This one is for 18kg,
and this one is for 13kg.

183
00:05:59,392 --> 00:06:01,559
We could split the laundry
between two 13kg machines...

184
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,162
and one 18-kg machine.

185
00:06:04,831 --> 00:06:07,099
How much would it be?

186
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,567
It's 60 baht.

187
00:06:08,568 --> 00:06:11,103
- It's 60 baht.
- It's 100 baht.

188
00:06:11,104 --> 00:06:14,072
- It's about 300 baht.
- That should be more than enough.

189
00:06:14,474 --> 00:06:17,209
If you put them in,
it will recognize them automatically.

190
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,076
Is that so?

191
00:06:18,077 --> 00:06:18,944
(Inserting)

192
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:22,068
- I'll take them out.
- Okay.

193
00:06:22,069 --> 00:06:22,882
(Exchanging for coins)

194
00:06:23,216 --> 00:06:25,717
These 2 are detergent,
and these 2 are fabric softener.

195
00:06:26,086 --> 00:06:27,987
- We need three, at least.
- Right.

196
00:06:27,988 --> 00:06:29,922
Our laundry is pretty dirty.

197
00:06:31,458 --> 00:06:33,726
And let's buy enough fabric softener.

198
00:06:33,727 --> 00:06:35,261
- This!
- This?

199
00:06:35,495 --> 00:06:37,129
(Buying what Sian wants)

200
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:37,763
One.

201
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:39,531
Let's wash...

202
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:41,901
towels and underwear first.

203
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:43,736
Then, let's wash the clothes together.

204
00:06:44,504 --> 00:06:45,671
Let me put some here too.

205
00:06:45,672 --> 00:06:48,207
(While Won Ji and Sian are putting
their laundry in the washers,)

206
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:51,377
(Gabee puts the coins in.)

207
00:06:51,711 --> 00:06:54,212
(Inserting)

208
00:06:54,781 --> 00:06:56,115
It's going smoothly.

209
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:57,850
It says "36 minutes."

210
00:06:58,318 --> 00:07:00,119
Shall we eat after putting them
in the dryers?

211
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,688
- We forgot about this! Wait!
- We forgot about this.

212
00:07:03,223 --> 00:07:05,191
(Left on the table)

213
00:07:05,992 --> 00:07:07,225
Hold on.

214
00:07:07,727 --> 00:07:10,696
(Rushing)

215
00:07:10,697 --> 00:07:11,863
Which one has more laundry?

216
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:14,266
Let's put it in the one for outerwear.

217
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:16,201
I can't open it.

218
00:07:16,202 --> 00:07:17,669
(The treasurer with long nails
is also on it.)

219
00:07:18,738 --> 00:07:21,807
(They managed to take care of it!)

220
00:07:21,808 --> 00:07:22,741
Okay!

221
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:24,076
Done.

222
00:07:24,311 --> 00:07:25,478
- Okay.
- We got it.

223
00:07:26,447 --> 00:07:29,748
There's a five-star place.

224
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:31,751
There's a good place 300m away.

225
00:07:31,752 --> 00:07:32,684
Let's go there.

226
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,155
There's a noodle place this way.

227
00:07:36,156 --> 00:07:37,256
I love noodles.

228
00:07:37,591 --> 00:07:38,391
Here!

229
00:07:38,925 --> 00:07:39,658
We're here.

230
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:42,127
This one is open.

231
00:07:42,495 --> 00:07:43,528
It's a Michelin restaurant.

232
00:07:43,897 --> 00:07:45,397
A Michelin restaurant?

233
00:07:45,732 --> 00:07:46,699
A Michelin-starred restaurant.

234
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,067
(Just down the alley,)

235
00:07:50,203 --> 00:07:51,804
(there's a Michelin-star restaurant.)

236
00:07:53,874 --> 00:07:56,709
(A lot of locals come here too.)

237
00:07:57,177 --> 00:08:00,212
(Just seeing the ingredients
at the entrance gets you excited.)

238
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:03,582
It's been a Michelin restaurant
since 2019.

239
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:04,550
That's true.

240
00:08:04,551 --> 00:08:05,551
(Thumbs-up)

241
00:08:05,552 --> 00:08:06,752
So in total,

242
00:08:06,753 --> 00:08:08,287
- Amazing!
- it's been eight years.

243
00:08:09,556 --> 00:08:11,357
It smells so good.

244
00:08:11,358 --> 00:08:13,392
(Taking their seats, feeling excited)

245
00:08:13,794 --> 00:08:16,628
This looks good. I love this one.

246
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:18,497
Meat soup?

247
00:08:18,498 --> 00:08:19,731
(Different kinds of Thai meat soups)

248
00:08:19,732 --> 00:08:20,765
A soup?

249
00:08:20,766 --> 00:08:21,566
This one?

250
00:08:22,035 --> 00:08:23,936
I want this with soup.

251
00:08:23,937 --> 00:08:24,903
I want this too.

252
00:08:25,105 --> 00:08:26,539
One beef noodles without soup.

253
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,474
Two beef soups.

254
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:31,010
One meatball soup.

255
00:08:31,544 --> 00:08:32,878
I have a feeling this place will be good.

256
00:08:32,879 --> 00:08:34,045
- I agree.
- I know.

257
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:39,718
(Pouring the hot broth over the meat
to warm it through)

258
00:08:42,255 --> 00:08:44,189
(Topping it
with a variety of garnishes...)

259
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:48,193
(and finishing it with their secret sauce)

260
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,931
It came out quickly!

261
00:08:51,932 --> 00:08:54,133
- My goodness.
- That looks so good.

262
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:57,136
- It reminds me of bun cha.
- It does.

263
00:08:58,705 --> 00:08:59,805
That looks good.

264
00:09:00,074 --> 00:09:01,273
It looks really good.

265
00:09:01,274 --> 00:09:03,075
(Gabee and Harimu's beef soup)

266
00:09:03,176 --> 00:09:04,677
It's like cold noodles
and spicy cold noodles.

267
00:09:04,678 --> 00:09:06,512
(Beef soup and beef noodles)

268
00:09:06,646 --> 00:09:07,913
Won Ji!

269
00:09:08,982 --> 00:09:10,649
My favorite.

270
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:11,650
(Won Ji's meatball soup)

271
00:09:12,619 --> 00:09:13,519
It looks delicious.

272
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,053
Nice!

273
00:09:16,656 --> 00:09:18,790
- Okay!
- Yes!

274
00:09:19,492 --> 00:09:20,592
Let's eat.

275
00:09:20,593 --> 00:09:22,661
- Let's eat.
- It looks tasty.

276
00:09:22,662 --> 00:09:23,829
Let me give it a taste.

277
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:25,130
Oh, my gosh.

278
00:09:25,131 --> 00:09:26,231
Do you guys have noodles?

279
00:09:27,334 --> 00:09:30,703
- You don't?
- I don't have noodles.

280
00:09:31,104 --> 00:09:32,671
- What?
- You don't have noodles?

281
00:09:33,106 --> 00:09:34,673
You guys don't have noodles either?

282
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:35,908
- Why don't we?
- You're right.

283
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,276
(Sian is the only one who has noodles.)

284
00:09:37,277 --> 00:09:38,510
- Shall we ask for noodles?
- Yes.

285
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:40,079
Excuse me.

286
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:42,714
Could you please add noodles?

287
00:09:42,715 --> 00:09:44,282
- Noodles?
- Yes.

288
00:09:45,051 --> 00:09:46,618
No noodles?

289
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,253
Really?

290
00:09:48,321 --> 00:09:51,089
Then can I...

291
00:09:51,992 --> 00:09:53,225
Can I order this?

292
00:09:53,493 --> 00:09:54,693
One more of this.

293
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:56,562
Like this?

294
00:09:56,563 --> 00:09:58,397
There's no meat.

295
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:00,832
Why did she just give you noodles?

296
00:10:01,214 --> 00:10:04,049
I kept asking for noodles,
so that's all I got.

297
00:10:04,745 --> 00:10:06,605
(Starting with a spoonful of broth)

298
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:07,572
What's this?

299
00:10:08,039 --> 00:10:10,252
Bulgogi soup?

300
00:10:10,845 --> 00:10:14,005
- This is a lot like short rib soup.
- It's exactly like short rib soup.

301
00:10:14,006 --> 00:10:17,083
(Rich, meaty, short rib soup-like broth)

302
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:18,916
(Straight to a bite of meat)

303
00:10:18,917 --> 00:10:22,490
(One bite after another)

304
00:10:22,596 --> 00:10:24,188
(Savoring the flavor)

305
00:10:24,755 --> 00:10:27,225
This meat is like...

306
00:10:27,889 --> 00:10:31,596
short rib soup meat with the bone removed.

307
00:10:32,522 --> 00:10:33,664
- The bone.
- So it's tender.

308
00:10:34,295 --> 00:10:36,234
It's so tender it practically melts.

309
00:10:36,235 --> 00:10:37,935
Agreed. The meat is delicious.

310
00:10:38,535 --> 00:10:39,908
Let's try it. Try this.

311
00:10:39,909 --> 00:10:40,909
(Sliding it over)

312
00:10:41,822 --> 00:10:44,502
(She's giving her meat.)

313
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:47,962
- Aren't you giving me all of it?
- Giving Won Ji all her love.

314
00:10:48,379 --> 00:10:50,248
Then you should try this.

315
00:10:51,212 --> 00:10:53,384
It's kind of like a fish cake with meat.

316
00:10:54,466 --> 00:10:56,679
(Big bite)

317
00:10:57,488 --> 00:10:59,524
- Isn't it incredibly bouncy?
- Totally.

318
00:11:00,372 --> 00:11:04,171
This one's very bouncy and a bit salty.

319
00:11:04,172 --> 00:11:05,663
- Try them together.
- Okay.

320
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:08,168
(Big bite)

321
00:11:08,262 --> 00:11:09,967
(Savoring the flavor)

322
00:11:09,968 --> 00:11:12,035
- It tastes completely packed with meat.
- Right?

323
00:11:12,355 --> 00:11:14,005
The umami builds as you chew.

324
00:11:14,135 --> 00:11:15,540
It's an interesting flavor.

325
00:11:16,602 --> 00:11:17,774
(Slurping)

326
00:11:17,815 --> 00:11:19,577
But it's really good.

327
00:11:19,578 --> 00:11:20,742
(Now a bite of beef noodles)

328
00:11:21,988 --> 00:11:23,114
(Savoring the flavor)

329
00:11:23,322 --> 00:11:24,482
(Puzzled by the flavor)

330
00:11:26,052 --> 00:11:27,885
(Won Ji takes a bite too.)

331
00:11:27,932 --> 00:11:29,654
How are the noodles? Interesting, right?

332
00:11:29,825 --> 00:11:32,652
- You like firm noodles.
- Totally.

333
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:34,525
These noodles are extremely firm.

334
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:37,195
They're very firm and chewy.

335
00:11:38,062 --> 00:11:39,197
Firm and chewy.

336
00:11:40,189 --> 00:11:41,299
This place is good.

337
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,070
(Dipping)

338
00:11:43,016 --> 00:11:45,163
(Now dipping it in the sauce)

339
00:11:46,410 --> 00:11:48,272
This sauce is good.

340
00:11:48,876 --> 00:11:50,341
How is it? The sauce is the star.

341
00:11:50,342 --> 00:11:52,342
- The sauce makes the dish.
- It really does.

342
00:11:52,343 --> 00:11:53,044
Exactly.

343
00:11:53,163 --> 00:11:55,313
Southeast Asian food uses
lots of fish sauce.

344
00:11:55,476 --> 00:11:58,483
- That's why it all has this tangy flavor.
- Yes, right.

345
00:11:58,536 --> 00:12:00,718
- You like Thai food now, don't you?
- Absolutely.

346
00:12:00,923 --> 00:12:02,923
Let's eat at Thai restaurants
back in Korea.

347
00:12:02,924 --> 00:12:04,555
- Sounds great.
- Right?

348
00:12:05,311 --> 00:12:07,425
Let's plan what to ask
at the fortune reading too.

349
00:12:07,471 --> 00:12:09,160
(Questions before the astrology reading)

350
00:12:09,694 --> 00:12:11,896
What's everyone's biggest concern lately?

351
00:12:12,144 --> 00:12:13,264
My biggest concern?

352
00:12:13,564 --> 00:12:15,233
First, whether this show will
work out well.

353
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:16,767
Health.

354
00:12:16,834 --> 00:12:19,270
Maybe they're best at predicting marriage.

355
00:12:19,570 --> 00:12:21,706
Or what kind of work suits you.

356
00:12:21,707 --> 00:12:23,040
- Good.
- I'm curious.

357
00:12:23,041 --> 00:12:24,008
(Strongly agrees)

358
00:12:24,009 --> 00:12:25,462
Should I ask which job suits me?

359
00:12:25,463 --> 00:12:27,778
I've been worried about my future lately.

360
00:12:28,321 --> 00:12:31,627
Have you all had your fortune told
or had a saju reading before?

361
00:12:31,628 --> 00:12:32,617
Of course.

362
00:12:33,135 --> 00:12:36,520
I've never gone for a proper saju reading,

363
00:12:36,988 --> 00:12:40,925
but a close friend of mine became
a shaman.

364
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:41,792
(Intrigued and shocked)

365
00:12:41,793 --> 00:12:43,227
That's fascinating.

366
00:12:43,853 --> 00:12:46,520
Almost everything she tells me comes true.

367
00:12:46,521 --> 00:12:47,632
What did she say?

368
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:51,435
She said I'd want more
than just college...

369
00:12:51,587 --> 00:12:53,953
and would start working very early.

370
00:12:53,954 --> 00:12:55,306
She told me things like that.

371
00:12:55,346 --> 00:12:56,186
What about you?

372
00:12:56,187 --> 00:12:57,939
I've had several readings.

373
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:00,966
I said I want to lead
a fairly ordinary life.

374
00:13:00,986 --> 00:13:02,013
They say I can't.

375
00:13:03,597 --> 00:13:05,149
(A born star)

376
00:13:05,150 --> 00:13:06,717
I'm not a star. It's more like...

377
00:13:06,718 --> 00:13:08,912
You can think of it
all as hits of dopamine.

378
00:13:09,045 --> 00:13:12,156
Deep down, our highs and lows are intense.

379
00:13:12,590 --> 00:13:16,227
What if we end up sobbing at the reading?

380
00:13:16,726 --> 00:13:17,894
I'm finished.

381
00:13:17,895 --> 00:13:20,894
It's 760 baht.

382
00:13:21,367 --> 00:13:22,327
That was good.

383
00:13:22,328 --> 00:13:25,574
(Thank you for the meal.)

384
00:13:25,801 --> 00:13:27,488
There's a cafe over there too.

385
00:13:27,489 --> 00:13:28,739
There's a cafe?

386
00:13:28,821 --> 00:13:30,241
Let's run the dryer and go.

387
00:13:30,388 --> 00:13:31,208
Sounds good.

388
00:13:31,542 --> 00:13:32,443
We're here.

389
00:13:32,548 --> 00:13:34,578
- We made it.
- We made it.

390
00:13:35,308 --> 00:13:38,992
(Back at the laundromat)

391
00:13:40,217 --> 00:13:41,485
It smells good.

392
00:13:42,592 --> 00:13:43,854
(The clothes are clean now.)

393
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:45,956
(Checking the dryer)

394
00:13:45,957 --> 00:13:47,091
It's clean in here.

395
00:13:47,624 --> 00:13:48,826
They maintain it well.

396
00:13:49,237 --> 00:13:51,923
(Loading the dryer)

397
00:13:51,924 --> 00:13:53,030
That's plenty.

398
00:13:53,531 --> 00:13:56,000
This seems like the high heat setting.

399
00:13:56,084 --> 00:13:57,268
- High heat?
- Sure.

400
00:13:57,275 --> 00:13:59,191
(Paying 60 baht,
about 2 dollars and 80 cents)

401
00:13:59,297 --> 00:14:01,297
We're a great team.

402
00:14:01,639 --> 00:14:03,407
How many minutes will it take?

403
00:14:03,818 --> 00:14:04,575
It will take 40 minutes.

404
00:14:04,576 --> 00:14:06,410
- Great.
- That's perfect.

405
00:14:06,451 --> 00:14:07,311
Let's find a cafe.

406
00:14:08,198 --> 00:14:11,818
There's one down this alley.

407
00:14:12,864 --> 00:14:13,951
It looks cool in there.

408
00:14:14,164 --> 00:14:16,164
- That looks good.
- Coffee.

409
00:14:16,484 --> 00:14:17,655
It's pretty.

410
00:14:17,844 --> 00:14:19,623
- Shall we go?
- Let's go.

411
00:14:20,404 --> 00:14:21,558
Nice.

412
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:24,462
I'm going to buy two drinks.
Nice!

413
00:14:24,659 --> 00:14:26,659
Ostrich! Ostrich!

414
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:27,732
Ostrich!

415
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:30,453
- Go straight!
- Straight ahead.

416
00:14:30,454 --> 00:14:31,902
Go straight!

417
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,637
Is this a convex mirror?

418
00:14:34,472 --> 00:14:37,108
Let's take a picture here.

419
00:14:37,246 --> 00:14:38,209
A picture!

420
00:14:38,719 --> 00:14:41,285
(A feel-good selfie)

421
00:14:42,272 --> 00:14:43,881
We look so cute!

422
00:14:43,950 --> 00:14:44,782
Okay.

423
00:14:44,843 --> 00:14:46,183
(Cute even when distorted)

424
00:14:46,517 --> 00:14:47,518
Let's go.

425
00:14:47,663 --> 00:14:49,663
Are we almost there?

426
00:14:50,321 --> 00:14:51,689
- Turn left here.
- It's so hot.

427
00:14:52,323 --> 00:14:53,758
I like this alley.

428
00:14:53,759 --> 00:14:55,155
(Entering a charming cafe alley)

429
00:14:55,156 --> 00:14:55,960
Over there.

430
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:56,961
- I see.
- Okay.

431
00:14:57,002 --> 00:14:59,497
There seem to be lots of travelers here.

432
00:15:01,799 --> 00:15:03,402
They sell matcha too.

433
00:15:03,403 --> 00:15:05,269
- Great.
- Matcha.

434
00:15:05,337 --> 00:15:06,450
I'll have three drinks.

435
00:15:06,451 --> 00:15:08,672
You clearly found a great cafe.

436
00:15:08,673 --> 00:15:11,442
The air conditioning looks really strong.

437
00:15:11,490 --> 00:15:13,477
- This place has a Seongsu vibe.
- It does.

438
00:15:13,870 --> 00:15:15,946
- Hello.
- Hello.

439
00:15:16,057 --> 00:15:17,248
Let's order.

440
00:15:18,203 --> 00:15:20,257
Should I pay for this with my own money?

441
00:15:20,323 --> 00:15:22,153
- You're having two drinks, right?
- Yes.

442
00:15:22,670 --> 00:15:25,923
I can't buy two with our shared money.

443
00:15:25,963 --> 00:15:27,158
We caught you.

444
00:15:27,237 --> 00:15:30,428
One Thai tea and one iced Americano.

445
00:15:30,731 --> 00:15:32,930
Only two, please.

446
00:15:33,464 --> 00:15:34,865
Strawberry matcha sounds good too.

447
00:15:34,866 --> 00:15:36,391
The mixed berry smoothie looks good.

448
00:15:36,392 --> 00:15:38,035
The chocolate milkshake looks good.

449
00:15:38,244 --> 00:15:39,410
- These two?
- Yes.

450
00:15:39,411 --> 00:15:40,471
Then I'll order this one.

451
00:15:40,758 --> 00:15:43,641
One strawberry matcha
and one long black iced coffee.

452
00:15:43,724 --> 00:15:47,882
One mixed berry smoothie
and one chocolate milkshake.

453
00:15:47,984 --> 00:15:50,114
And a strawberry cream croissant.

454
00:15:50,981 --> 00:15:53,617
I always need dessert after a meal.

455
00:15:53,618 --> 00:15:55,250
(Their huge cafe order is complete.)

456
00:15:56,554 --> 00:15:59,156
- Many people retire and move here.
- Right.

457
00:15:59,157 --> 00:16:01,175
(Hopping)

458
00:16:01,535 --> 00:16:02,493
Look at you.

459
00:16:02,588 --> 00:16:04,315
(The neighborhood boss appears.)

460
00:16:04,316 --> 00:16:06,030
Hi, kitty.

461
00:16:07,148 --> 00:16:09,148
- This cat is so friendly.
- Its paws are tiny.

462
00:16:09,149 --> 00:16:10,334
It looks like a baby.

463
00:16:10,335 --> 00:16:11,747
(Clacking)

464
00:16:11,748 --> 00:16:17,395
(Harimu's multipurpose nails)

465
00:16:18,128 --> 00:16:19,210
What is this?

466
00:16:19,543 --> 00:16:20,911
No, you can't have this.

467
00:16:21,412 --> 00:16:22,546
You can't have this.

468
00:16:23,314 --> 00:16:24,648
Look, it's settled in.

469
00:16:25,288 --> 00:16:28,128
(A seat fit for the local boss)

470
00:16:28,129 --> 00:16:30,154
What's with you?

471
00:16:30,334 --> 00:16:33,357
We meet so many animals.

472
00:16:33,624 --> 00:16:34,985
We have good luck with animals.

473
00:16:34,986 --> 00:16:37,528
A dog yesterday and a cat today.

474
00:16:38,185 --> 00:16:39,959
(Who's next?)

475
00:16:40,152 --> 00:16:42,967
I think 40 minutes will pass quickly.

476
00:16:42,968 --> 00:16:43,901
We're in trouble.

477
00:16:43,957 --> 00:16:45,330
It's probably been 15 minutes.

478
00:16:45,477 --> 00:16:47,137
Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

479
00:16:47,243 --> 00:16:48,339
One person does it all.

480
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:49,540
- Sure.
- Great.

481
00:16:49,677 --> 00:16:51,008
It's seriously hot.

482
00:16:51,281 --> 00:16:52,676
This might be the hottest day.

483
00:16:52,677 --> 00:16:54,712
Day Three is the hottest so far.

484
00:16:55,597 --> 00:16:56,614
It's too hot.

485
00:16:57,481 --> 00:16:58,749
- Now?
- Yes.

486
00:16:59,149 --> 00:17:01,218
The loser takes this and goes back.

487
00:17:01,819 --> 00:17:03,287
The loser has to run there after we play.

488
00:17:04,112 --> 00:17:05,789
We need time to prepare ourselves.

489
00:17:05,825 --> 00:17:07,925
Okay, rock-paper-scissors.

490
00:17:08,458 --> 00:17:09,612
Rock-paper-scissors.

491
00:17:09,912 --> 00:17:10,919
Rock-paper-scissors.

492
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:12,062
Nice! Rock-paper-scissors.

493
00:17:12,063 --> 00:17:13,130
Rock-paper-scissors.

494
00:17:15,813 --> 00:17:17,973
(Joy and sorrow)

495
00:17:18,013 --> 00:17:20,204
Thank you! Thank you!

496
00:17:20,386 --> 00:17:22,373
You love me! I love you, too!

497
00:17:22,374 --> 00:17:23,886
(A sudden profession of faith)

498
00:17:24,166 --> 00:17:25,472
(Impressive)

499
00:17:26,377 --> 00:17:28,412
Rock-paper-scissors, shoot!

500
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:32,504
(Sian is going to the laundromat.)

501
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:36,331
Thank you! You see me. I see you.

502
00:17:36,332 --> 00:17:37,944
(A successful conversion)

503
00:17:38,231 --> 00:17:39,018
(Springing up)

504
00:17:39,324 --> 00:17:40,824
Her true feelings? That's amazing!

505
00:17:40,825 --> 00:17:42,126
She's going. She's off.

506
00:17:42,291 --> 00:17:45,095
It's insanely hot.

507
00:17:45,596 --> 00:17:48,144
I just ordered three desserts,

508
00:17:48,145 --> 00:17:49,733
so we could all share them.

509
00:17:49,910 --> 00:17:51,976
(Feeling wronged)

510
00:17:52,043 --> 00:17:53,404
I honestly didn't think I'd lose.

511
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:54,772
(You should've won.)

512
00:17:54,923 --> 00:17:56,307
What were the chances it'd be me?

513
00:17:57,490 --> 00:17:59,677
(The drinks are ready in the meantime.)

514
00:18:00,244 --> 00:18:01,845
(We each ordered two drinks.)

515
00:18:03,349 --> 00:18:07,316
(Four people and seven cups)

516
00:18:07,363 --> 00:18:08,189
I'm so happy.

517
00:18:08,190 --> 00:18:10,487
I'm usually the only one ordering
two drinks.

518
00:18:10,596 --> 00:18:12,723
I'm excited that you're matching
my energy.

519
00:18:12,949 --> 00:18:15,640
I ordered the strawberry matcha.

520
00:18:15,641 --> 00:18:17,268
Strawberry matcha.

521
00:18:17,269 --> 00:18:19,930
You can see the strawberry down there.

522
00:18:19,931 --> 00:18:21,165
Right?

523
00:18:21,488 --> 00:18:23,100
Try a sip.

524
00:18:24,148 --> 00:18:26,021
<i>Matcha, matcha, ya-ya</i>

525
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:26,928
(Eyes widening)

526
00:18:28,339 --> 00:18:30,474
She's really trying.

527
00:18:30,774 --> 00:18:33,611
You sang, "Matcha, matcha, ya ya."

528
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:34,712
We have to play along.

529
00:18:34,713 --> 00:18:37,481
<i>Gitchi gitchi ya ya da da</i>

530
00:18:39,792 --> 00:18:40,918
Try this too.

531
00:18:41,452 --> 00:18:42,886
Did you order it for us to share?

532
00:18:42,887 --> 00:18:44,421
I did. Help yourself.

533
00:18:44,571 --> 00:18:46,323
- Want me to cut it?
- Yes, please.

534
00:18:47,684 --> 00:18:49,991
(Slicing)

535
00:18:50,527 --> 00:18:52,396
Now it's a mess.

536
00:18:53,597 --> 00:18:55,566
Go ahead. It all looks the same
in your stomach.

537
00:18:56,602 --> 00:18:57,953
(Nibbling)

538
00:18:57,954 --> 00:19:00,237
Good choice. This makes me happy.

539
00:19:01,438 --> 00:19:02,706
The cream is delicious.

540
00:19:04,295 --> 00:19:06,666
(Whirring)

541
00:19:08,053 --> 00:19:11,119
(Suddenly imitating a blender)

542
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:13,120
She's doing an astrology reading now.

543
00:19:13,817 --> 00:19:15,319
She's reading our fortunes.

544
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,460
(Playing coy)

545
00:19:16,461 --> 00:19:19,111
How does today look?

546
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:20,991
It looks promising.

547
00:19:22,004 --> 00:19:23,727
(Dying of laughter)

548
00:19:23,764 --> 00:19:25,496
I think it'll go smoothly.

549
00:19:25,864 --> 00:19:26,630
That's all I need.

550
00:19:28,097 --> 00:19:31,114
I thought I took this out of my suitcase.

551
00:19:31,115 --> 00:19:32,296
- Really?
- Who put it back?

552
00:19:32,770 --> 00:19:33,804
- You're wearing it?
- Who did?

553
00:19:33,805 --> 00:19:35,755
- I took it out.
- I didn't put it back.

554
00:19:36,142 --> 00:19:37,182
- You too?
- Her?

555
00:19:38,108 --> 00:19:39,710
I put it in.

556
00:19:40,467 --> 00:19:41,128
I did.

557
00:19:41,508 --> 00:19:42,958
I put it in, but...

558
00:19:43,112 --> 00:19:44,388
This is why I packed it.

559
00:19:44,389 --> 00:19:47,284
We might have a military experience.

560
00:19:48,385 --> 00:19:50,947
I could wear it while crawling
on the ground.

561
00:19:50,948 --> 00:19:52,423
A top while crawling on the ground?

562
00:19:52,424 --> 00:19:54,358
It'd probably fall apart while you crawl.

563
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:55,325
A combat-crawling top.

564
00:19:55,446 --> 00:19:57,628
The military top has returned alive.

565
00:19:58,112 --> 00:20:00,464
On a two-week trip,

566
00:20:00,552 --> 00:20:01,865
not exaggerating,

567
00:20:01,866 --> 00:20:04,297
I literally bring 40 to 50 tops,

568
00:20:04,404 --> 00:20:07,974
then buy ten more on the trip.

569
00:20:07,975 --> 00:20:10,376
For me, tops are
more important than bottoms.

570
00:20:10,477 --> 00:20:13,078
Yes, you've been wearing the same pants
for three days in a row.

571
00:20:13,079 --> 00:20:14,713
I'm keeping these pants on for two weeks.

572
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:18,284
Time flies. It's already been 46 minutes.

573
00:20:18,351 --> 00:20:20,018
We have four minutes left.

574
00:20:20,754 --> 00:20:23,122
(Oh right.)

575
00:20:23,123 --> 00:20:24,290
I forgot about that.

576
00:20:24,958 --> 00:20:26,325
Let's go get our laundry.

577
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,793
- Okay.
- Good luck!

578
00:20:27,894 --> 00:20:29,127
- Good luck!
- You got this!

579
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:30,563
(Wait)

580
00:20:31,065 --> 00:20:34,100
I'll go with Sian.

581
00:20:34,101 --> 00:20:35,968
I'll go with Sian.

582
00:20:35,969 --> 00:20:38,104
It's going to be a date.

583
00:20:38,105 --> 00:20:38,905
Wow.

584
00:20:38,906 --> 00:20:39,939
Are you going together?

585
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:40,640
Yes.

586
00:20:40,641 --> 00:20:41,741
- The two of you?
- Yes.

587
00:20:41,742 --> 00:20:42,775
We'll be back.

588
00:20:42,776 --> 00:20:44,377
(Harimu joins in.)

589
00:20:45,212 --> 00:20:47,246
We'll be quick.

590
00:20:47,247 --> 00:20:48,848
Good luck!

591
00:20:49,583 --> 00:20:50,917
Cover yourself.

592
00:20:51,485 --> 00:20:55,689
(Singing)

593
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:57,924
What if it rains?

594
00:20:58,391 --> 00:20:59,191
Oh my!

595
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:02,829
(Singing)

596
00:21:02,830 --> 00:21:03,796
(Sound effects)

597
00:21:06,566 --> 00:21:07,566
Music brings us together.

598
00:21:08,535 --> 00:21:09,568
I think it's done, right?

599
00:21:10,937 --> 00:21:12,104
I think so.

600
00:21:12,105 --> 00:21:14,039
(Third time visiting the laundromat)

601
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:14,907
It's finished.

602
00:21:15,442 --> 00:21:16,542
Let's open it.

603
00:21:17,611 --> 00:21:18,444
Is it fluffy?

604
00:21:18,445 --> 00:21:20,046
Very!

605
00:21:20,914 --> 00:21:22,248
It smells so good.

606
00:21:23,117 --> 00:21:26,652
- Thanks for coming with me.
- No problem, roommate.

607
00:21:26,653 --> 00:21:29,222
Best friends forever.

608
00:21:29,223 --> 00:21:30,456
We were each other's Secret Santas.

609
00:21:30,757 --> 00:21:31,824
Off we go.

610
00:21:32,626 --> 00:21:34,293
What do you think of our friendship?

611
00:21:34,294 --> 00:21:35,761
(We're best friends.)

612
00:21:35,762 --> 00:21:36,562
Let's go.

613
00:21:37,230 --> 00:21:38,830
This would have been
too heavy for one person.

614
00:21:38,831 --> 00:21:40,766
Yes, this is a bit heavy.

615
00:21:40,767 --> 00:21:42,701
Why is it heavier after laundry?

616
00:21:43,537 --> 00:21:45,271
It wasn't this heavy in the morning.

617
00:21:45,939 --> 00:21:48,274
Okay guys, we're back.

618
00:21:48,608 --> 00:21:50,042
(Back at the hotel)

619
00:21:51,444 --> 00:21:52,511
Hi!

620
00:21:52,512 --> 00:21:54,546
Oh, it's so cool and nice.

621
00:21:54,547 --> 00:21:56,214
Thank you.

622
00:21:56,416 --> 00:21:57,516
We still have to take them out,

623
00:21:57,517 --> 00:21:59,084
otherwise it's going to get all damp.

624
00:21:59,252 --> 00:22:00,253
They're really warm.

625
00:22:00,254 --> 00:22:02,622
They're so clean.
Let's do it again.

626
00:22:02,623 --> 00:22:03,756
All right.

627
00:22:04,224 --> 00:22:06,492
Let's spread them out a bit
before leaving.

628
00:22:06,493 --> 00:22:07,259
Okay.

629
00:22:07,561 --> 00:22:08,961
I'll call the taxi.

630
00:22:08,962 --> 00:22:10,129
All right.

631
00:22:10,864 --> 00:22:13,365
Let's get the taxi and go.

632
00:22:13,366 --> 00:22:14,634
Let's go!

633
00:22:14,635 --> 00:22:16,274
- It's only 10 minutes away.
- Yes!

634
00:22:16,275 --> 00:22:17,369
(10 minutes to the fortune teller)

635
00:22:17,771 --> 00:22:19,139
Oh, the taxi's here.

636
00:22:19,140 --> 00:22:20,840
- Okay, let's go!
- The taxi is here.

637
00:22:20,841 --> 00:22:21,707
I'm so excited.

638
00:22:23,109 --> 00:22:24,843
Let's go, Day Three!

639
00:22:24,844 --> 00:22:25,777
(Day 3 officially begins.)

640
00:22:25,778 --> 00:22:27,312
Is that it?

641
00:22:27,313 --> 00:22:28,947
- Is that our taxi, Gabee?
- That's it.

642
00:22:28,948 --> 00:22:31,116
Yes, it's that one.

643
00:22:31,819 --> 00:22:33,719
I'll sit in the middle, Harimu.

644
00:22:33,720 --> 00:22:35,420
No, I will.

645
00:22:35,522 --> 00:22:37,156
- I'll sit in the middle.
- Get in the middle.

646
00:22:37,157 --> 00:22:38,023
(Being considerate)

647
00:22:38,024 --> 00:22:39,557
Hello!

648
00:22:39,558 --> 00:22:41,826
Hello.

649
00:22:41,995 --> 00:22:44,330
Are you okay back there?

650
00:22:45,065 --> 00:22:47,500
It's only a short ride.

651
00:22:47,501 --> 00:22:48,834
(Heading off to the fortune teller)

652
00:22:49,002 --> 00:22:50,970
(Singing)

653
00:22:51,171 --> 00:22:52,838
(Singing)

654
00:22:56,944 --> 00:22:59,511
Let's ride a taxi...

655
00:22:59,512 --> 00:23:01,547
and go over there.

656
00:23:01,548 --> 00:23:05,184
(Not used to the lively vibe)

657
00:23:05,484 --> 00:23:07,952
(Excitedly heading to downtown Bangkok)

658
00:23:08,835 --> 00:23:10,529
Thailand is great.

659
00:23:10,530 --> 00:23:12,524
(Heading to Tha Pra Chan)

660
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:14,700
Oh, an unfamiliar path.

661
00:23:16,002 --> 00:23:17,235
Jewelry?

662
00:23:17,769 --> 00:23:19,338
- Jewelry?
- Jewelry.

663
00:23:22,902 --> 00:23:24,736
They're like a jukebox.

664
00:23:28,641 --> 00:23:30,342
(Singing)

665
00:23:30,343 --> 00:23:31,643
(Dancing)

666
00:23:31,944 --> 00:23:34,045
(An introvert internally screaming)

667
00:23:36,883 --> 00:23:38,784
Check out those details.

668
00:23:39,085 --> 00:23:40,886
This was the first song I performed
on stage.

669
00:23:40,887 --> 00:23:43,322
- Seriously?
- When I was five.

670
00:23:45,124 --> 00:23:48,093
That song gave me a taste of the stage.

671
00:23:49,529 --> 00:23:50,762
You were just five?

672
00:23:51,230 --> 00:23:53,164
You were only five back then?

673
00:23:53,165 --> 00:23:54,799
Thank you, Jewelry!

674
00:23:56,335 --> 00:23:58,002
I also have a first performance story.

675
00:23:58,104 --> 00:23:59,037
Really?

676
00:23:59,172 --> 00:24:00,772
- Can you guess what it was?
- Show me.

677
00:24:00,907 --> 00:24:02,608
<i>I love my boy</i>

678
00:24:02,909 --> 00:24:05,410
(Diva by After School)

679
00:24:09,882 --> 00:24:11,349
(Singing along)

680
00:24:12,351 --> 00:24:13,985
(Clapping)

681
00:24:18,257 --> 00:24:20,692
(Please, send help.)

682
00:24:23,362 --> 00:24:25,196
So you all performed on stage
when you were young.

683
00:24:25,298 --> 00:24:26,265
Mine was when I was in 5th grade...

684
00:24:26,799 --> 00:24:27,672
at a senior center.

685
00:24:27,934 --> 00:24:29,734
- The senior center!
- We went volunteering...

686
00:24:29,735 --> 00:24:31,436
and four of us danced.

687
00:24:31,437 --> 00:24:32,504
What about you, Won Ji?

688
00:24:32,505 --> 00:24:34,673
I've never been on stage before.

689
00:24:34,674 --> 00:24:36,207
(A 100 percent introvert
with no stage experience)

690
00:24:36,208 --> 00:24:38,578
What's going to be your debut song?

691
00:24:38,579 --> 00:24:39,945
What should it be?

692
00:24:39,946 --> 00:24:42,548
I pick "Bromm, Taki."

693
00:24:42,849 --> 00:24:44,349
Your debut stage is going
to be "Bromm, Taki?"

694
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:46,651
- Of course.
- I'm so honored.

695
00:24:47,693 --> 00:24:49,187
<i>Bromm, Taki</i>

696
00:24:50,302 --> 00:24:51,489
(Giggling)

697
00:24:51,904 --> 00:24:53,371
(The world's flattest debut)

698
00:24:53,372 --> 00:24:54,639
Won Ji.

699
00:24:54,973 --> 00:24:55,940
It's like you're meditating.

700
00:24:56,408 --> 00:24:58,209
<i>Bromm, Taki!</i>

701
00:24:58,944 --> 00:25:01,947
(A dance track turned solemn)

702
00:25:02,034 --> 00:25:03,168
Let's do a debut stage!

703
00:25:03,169 --> 00:25:05,737
My debut is today!

704
00:25:06,238 --> 00:25:08,907
- That's funny.
- Yesterday, I heard a toad.

705
00:25:09,842 --> 00:25:11,209
(Gabee's toad?)

706
00:25:11,210 --> 00:25:12,143
Really?

707
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:14,445
It must've been a real toad...

708
00:25:14,446 --> 00:25:15,546
because we didn't use it yesterday.

709
00:25:15,547 --> 00:25:16,380
We didn't.

710
00:25:16,381 --> 00:25:18,015
Really?

711
00:25:18,117 --> 00:25:20,251
- Did you hear it?
- No.

712
00:25:20,552 --> 00:25:21,552
But I heard it.

713
00:25:22,755 --> 00:25:24,823
Thailand has many ghosts.

714
00:25:25,224 --> 00:25:27,125
I never touched it once yesterday.

715
00:25:27,126 --> 00:25:28,326
- No way.
- Seriously.

716
00:25:28,327 --> 00:25:29,561
I definitely heard it.

717
00:25:31,063 --> 00:25:32,997
We left it downstairs.

718
00:25:32,998 --> 00:25:35,566
So we never got to use it.

719
00:25:35,801 --> 00:25:36,701
We left it in the bag.

720
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,905
- They left it downstairs.
- I really heard it.

721
00:25:39,906 --> 00:25:41,940
- It's a ghost toad!
- So I thought...

722
00:25:41,941 --> 00:25:43,775
you were cute for using it...

723
00:25:43,776 --> 00:25:45,443
and that it sounded nice.

724
00:25:45,444 --> 00:25:47,412
That was a ghost.

725
00:25:49,348 --> 00:25:52,583
(What did Sian hear?)

726
00:25:52,851 --> 00:25:54,718
- Here we are.
- Is this the place?

727
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:55,986
(The taxi arrives at the destination.)

728
00:25:56,355 --> 00:25:59,057
They even have fortune-telling merch here.

729
00:25:59,058 --> 00:26:01,125
- Really?
- Wow.

730
00:26:01,327 --> 00:26:02,460
Cool!

731
00:26:02,628 --> 00:26:04,729
Thank you!

732
00:26:05,765 --> 00:26:07,298
Thank you.

733
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,601
Have a nice day.

734
00:26:09,902 --> 00:26:11,102
This is the place.

735
00:26:11,203 --> 00:26:13,137
They're selling frame keychains.

736
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:15,073
They have a lot of photo frame things.

737
00:26:15,074 --> 00:26:16,474
I want something...

738
00:26:16,475 --> 00:26:18,809
- like that.
- That looks like a necklace.

739
00:26:18,945 --> 00:26:21,746
- Is this a fortune teller's street?
- All of these.

740
00:26:22,181 --> 00:26:24,016
The whole street is like that.

741
00:26:24,149 --> 00:26:25,450
I guess so.

742
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:28,285
- They have amulets.
- Right, they have talismans.

743
00:26:28,954 --> 00:26:30,087
They even have herbal inhalers.

744
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:31,289
(Street full of amulets and merch)

745
00:26:31,290 --> 00:26:32,123
There are so many.

746
00:26:33,359 --> 00:26:35,126
Keep going.

747
00:26:35,127 --> 00:26:36,861
Yes, keep going.

748
00:26:37,896 --> 00:26:39,497
This place feels more urban.

749
00:26:39,498 --> 00:26:40,998
Yes, it does.

750
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:43,601
Follow me.

751
00:26:44,903 --> 00:26:48,572
(Peaceful and quiet Tha Phra Chan)

752
00:26:48,909 --> 00:26:52,177
In Thailand, you should never...

753
00:26:52,478 --> 00:26:53,711
touch a monk.

754
00:26:53,712 --> 00:26:55,046
- Really?
- Never.

755
00:26:55,047 --> 00:26:56,047
Never.

756
00:26:56,048 --> 00:26:57,449
This place doesn't have any cars.

757
00:26:57,583 --> 00:26:58,950
The flowers are so pretty.

758
00:26:58,951 --> 00:26:59,817
(Entering a car-free zone)

759
00:26:59,852 --> 00:27:02,120
Let's go slowly, girls.

760
00:27:03,222 --> 00:27:04,022
Slay.

761
00:27:04,156 --> 00:27:07,158
(Slow down and look around.)

762
00:27:07,159 --> 00:27:09,293
- Slow down, girls.
- Slow.

763
00:27:09,728 --> 00:27:13,397
(Taking in the feedback with her body)

764
00:27:14,099 --> 00:27:14,965
Oh, tacos!

765
00:27:15,734 --> 00:27:16,801
They sell tacos.

766
00:27:17,035 --> 00:27:19,637
- The specialty coffee looks nice!
- Right!

767
00:27:19,939 --> 00:27:21,373
That place looks classy, too.

768
00:27:21,374 --> 00:27:22,473
That place looks good.

769
00:27:23,075 --> 00:27:24,175
Is it over there?

770
00:27:24,576 --> 00:27:26,544
Yes, let's keep moving.

771
00:27:26,845 --> 00:27:28,145
Phra Chan.

772
00:27:28,847 --> 00:27:29,847
Tha Phra Chan.

773
00:27:30,149 --> 00:27:31,249
Tha Phra Chan.

774
00:27:31,617 --> 00:27:33,351
Tha Phra Chan.

775
00:27:34,286 --> 00:27:36,082
(A riverside complex filled
with shops and eateries)

776
00:27:36,083 --> 00:27:38,089
(A popular tourist spot known
for astrology and fortune telling)

777
00:27:38,924 --> 00:27:42,260
(A pier located
along the Chao Phraya River)

778
00:27:42,561 --> 00:27:45,496
(Bursting with food, shops,
and fortune tellers)

779
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:53,004
(Connected to a 100-year-old
traditional amulet market)

780
00:27:53,005 --> 00:27:54,105
We're not getting on a boat.

781
00:27:54,106 --> 00:27:55,072
(Entering the building)

782
00:27:55,073 --> 00:27:56,240
Is it inside here?

783
00:27:56,810 --> 00:27:57,976
This looks like a shopping arcade.

784
00:27:58,243 --> 00:28:00,311
It kind of looks like a station.

785
00:28:00,939 --> 00:28:02,373
This place has an interesting vibe.

786
00:28:02,381 --> 00:28:04,015
They sell records there.

787
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:06,784
You can see a river over there.

788
00:28:06,985 --> 00:28:08,852
Finally, we're seeing the river.

789
00:28:09,021 --> 00:28:12,023
This way. Have a look.

790
00:28:12,024 --> 00:28:12,924
(Taking in the view)

791
00:28:12,925 --> 00:28:14,159
Hi.

792
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:17,128
Wow, water hyacinths!

793
00:28:17,129 --> 00:28:20,131
This place has a lot of them.

794
00:28:20,833 --> 00:28:24,135
- This is a fortune-telling zone.
- This way.

795
00:28:24,136 --> 00:28:26,037
So this is the place.

796
00:28:26,672 --> 00:28:28,373
Hello.

797
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:30,842
Hello.

798
00:28:31,009 --> 00:28:33,344
(Arrives at the fortune teller)

799
00:28:33,345 --> 00:28:35,245
- Shall we sit?
- What about chairs?

800
00:28:35,481 --> 00:28:37,282
Hello.

801
00:28:37,650 --> 00:28:39,150
You two can sit here.

802
00:28:39,151 --> 00:28:40,718
(Taking seats right away)

803
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:42,721
Two can sit there.

804
00:28:42,722 --> 00:28:44,755
We need to talk to her, though.

805
00:28:44,756 --> 00:28:45,623
(Taking the innermost seats)

806
00:28:45,624 --> 00:28:46,825
Just a second.

807
00:28:46,826 --> 00:28:48,059
We have a translator app here.

808
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:51,662
I'm on it. "We want..."

809
00:28:52,030 --> 00:28:53,897
"our Thai astrology reading done."

810
00:28:53,898 --> 00:28:56,300
- Hello.
- Hello!

811
00:28:56,535 --> 00:28:58,236
Hello.

812
00:28:58,438 --> 00:29:01,005
Tell her that we want our fortunes told.

813
00:29:01,540 --> 00:29:03,674
(Translator ready)

814
00:29:03,942 --> 00:29:05,809
We're here for Thai fortune telling.

815
00:29:06,011 --> 00:29:09,547
Tell me your birthdate.

816
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:12,516
She wants to know our birthdate.

817
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:14,752
My birthdate is...

818
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:16,553
(First conversation: success)

819
00:29:16,655 --> 00:29:17,888
Let's write it down.

820
00:29:17,889 --> 00:29:19,557
Yes, let's write it down for her.

821
00:29:19,992 --> 00:29:22,427
And let's send the message.

822
00:29:22,428 --> 00:29:24,596
First, second, third, and fourth.

823
00:29:24,597 --> 00:29:26,397
I'm the first one.

824
00:29:26,932 --> 00:29:28,332
Number Won Ji.

825
00:29:29,234 --> 00:29:31,535
(Kindly laughing at the dad joke)

826
00:29:31,536 --> 00:29:33,671
Do tourists get their fortune told...

827
00:29:33,672 --> 00:29:35,306
when they visit Korea?

828
00:29:35,307 --> 00:29:37,474
It might be hard
with the language barrier.

829
00:29:37,475 --> 00:29:40,578
I don't think many would
even think about it.

830
00:29:40,825 --> 00:29:41,879
- Wow.
- Gosh!

831
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:43,848
She's using a book.

832
00:29:44,250 --> 00:29:45,449
What is that?

833
00:29:46,051 --> 00:29:47,885
It's full of numbers.

834
00:29:47,886 --> 00:29:49,286
(Wall of numbers)

835
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:50,654
She looks so serious.

836
00:29:50,655 --> 00:29:51,722
Very serious.

837
00:29:51,890 --> 00:29:54,358
(Focused)

838
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:56,494
She's writing down all the numbers.

839
00:29:57,230 --> 00:29:58,796
She's calculating something.

840
00:29:58,797 --> 00:29:59,764
(She writes something.)

841
00:29:59,789 --> 00:30:02,501
There's one at every interval
like a clock.

842
00:30:02,622 --> 00:30:04,836
Right. I can see the zodiac signs.

843
00:30:05,420 --> 00:30:06,638
In Thai astrology,

844
00:30:06,707 --> 00:30:10,280
there's a guardian deity
for each day of the week,

845
00:30:10,281 --> 00:30:11,495
and not just your birthday and year.

846
00:30:11,496 --> 00:30:14,446
It's kind of like a mix
of saju and astrology.

847
00:30:14,601 --> 00:30:15,647
It's totally different from Korea.

848
00:30:15,648 --> 00:30:18,216
- We use Chinese characters for that.
- That's right.

849
00:30:18,568 --> 00:30:21,386
I guess they even offer yogurt drinks
to the gods.

850
00:30:22,421 --> 00:30:23,255
Seems like it.

851
00:30:23,282 --> 00:30:25,282
I thought it was Korean one.

852
00:30:25,415 --> 00:30:27,626
It's water with a straw in it.

853
00:30:27,627 --> 00:30:29,169
You're right.

854
00:30:29,528 --> 00:30:31,730
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

855
00:30:31,731 --> 00:30:33,298
Nice to meet you.

856
00:30:33,587 --> 00:30:35,968
(Suddenly)

857
00:30:36,321 --> 00:30:38,634
(The fortune teller finishes the reading.)

858
00:30:40,075 --> 00:30:41,106
I'm nervous.

859
00:30:41,107 --> 00:30:42,507
It's making me nervous.

860
00:30:43,141 --> 00:30:45,043
Let's reveal the results!

861
00:30:45,044 --> 00:30:47,044
What if it says that I'm doomed?

862
00:30:47,431 --> 00:30:48,844
No way.

863
00:30:48,938 --> 00:30:51,049
Based on your face reading,
you're not bound to fail.

864
00:30:51,244 --> 00:30:52,438
Because you're a born cutie!

865
00:30:52,439 --> 00:30:53,611
I've never heard of that before.

866
00:30:53,612 --> 00:30:55,087
A born cutie.

867
00:30:55,088 --> 00:30:56,497
(Powered by cuteness)

868
00:30:57,237 --> 00:30:59,503
As for your personality,

869
00:30:59,670 --> 00:31:01,363
you're naturally quiet...

870
00:31:01,364 --> 00:31:04,290
and a bit impatient.

871
00:31:05,664 --> 00:31:06,998
Didn't we agree not to do that?

872
00:31:06,999 --> 00:31:08,233
Oh, right. I forgot.

873
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:10,135
Just kidding. You do what you want.

874
00:31:10,179 --> 00:31:12,437
How did she know I'm impatient?

875
00:31:12,966 --> 00:31:16,079
I'm seriously in the top one percent
when it comes to being impatient.

876
00:31:16,646 --> 00:31:19,485
I may seem calm,
but I'm actually really impatient.

877
00:31:19,579 --> 00:31:21,346
- I need things done quickly.
- You need to do a lot too.

878
00:31:21,347 --> 00:31:22,547
Everything should be done "ASAP."

879
00:31:22,612 --> 00:31:23,715
I think I get what you mean.

880
00:31:25,091 --> 00:31:29,542
You have a knack for business
and making money.

881
00:31:29,795 --> 00:31:30,701
So,

882
00:31:30,702 --> 00:31:32,782
money will keep flowing your way.

883
00:31:32,783 --> 00:31:35,288
- Make money, girl!
- Money, money.

884
00:31:35,289 --> 00:31:37,062
Money!

885
00:31:37,409 --> 00:31:39,233
But never co-sign for anyone.

886
00:31:39,286 --> 00:31:41,800
You'll end up shouldering
all the responsibility.

887
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:43,735
Co-sign!

888
00:31:43,736 --> 00:31:45,697
(Just the fortune teller's
personal opinion.)

889
00:31:45,983 --> 00:31:48,073
- No co-signing.
- Never.

890
00:31:48,369 --> 00:31:49,341
(Never co-sign!)

891
00:31:49,422 --> 00:31:50,942
According to your reading,

892
00:31:51,229 --> 00:31:53,382
(Focused)

893
00:31:53,555 --> 00:31:55,649
you're destined to meet your soulmate.

894
00:31:55,881 --> 00:31:57,468
(Indistinct speech)

895
00:31:57,475 --> 00:31:59,918
I feel like she's saying something huge.

896
00:32:00,652 --> 00:32:02,664
Your friend's friend likes you.

897
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:05,190
My friend's friend has a crush on me?

898
00:32:05,447 --> 00:32:06,324
This is true.

899
00:32:06,625 --> 00:32:08,380
A mutual friend!

900
00:32:08,474 --> 00:32:11,863
- It's true, right?
- A mutual friend.

901
00:32:11,864 --> 00:32:13,071
- That's how you two met!
- That's right.

902
00:32:14,684 --> 00:32:16,768
You're amazing, sis!

903
00:32:17,097 --> 00:32:18,503
You're so good at this!

904
00:32:18,517 --> 00:32:20,295
(This lady knows what she's doing.)

905
00:32:21,044 --> 00:32:25,258
(Next up is Gabee!)

906
00:32:25,702 --> 00:32:32,427
You'll have a lot of expenses
over the next two months.

907
00:32:32,686 --> 00:32:34,052
For the next two?

908
00:32:34,213 --> 00:32:35,787
Guess you'll be spending a lot.

909
00:32:36,894 --> 00:32:38,760
And I see a change in where you live.

910
00:32:39,007 --> 00:32:41,307
It looks like you'll be moving.

911
00:32:42,019 --> 00:32:43,762
Is this true?

912
00:32:43,824 --> 00:32:45,497
- Are you serious?
- This just gave me chills.

913
00:32:46,198 --> 00:32:48,500
- When?
- Next year.

914
00:32:48,940 --> 00:32:51,203
I've already signed the contract
for my new place next year.

915
00:32:52,204 --> 00:32:53,424
Really?

916
00:32:53,425 --> 00:32:56,174
It's basically a done deal.

917
00:32:56,175 --> 00:32:57,576
I'm moving next year.

918
00:32:57,629 --> 00:32:59,077
I signed the contract in advance.

919
00:33:00,655 --> 00:33:04,115
(Spot on.)

920
00:33:04,437 --> 00:33:07,950
First of all,
you have very high self-esteem.

921
00:33:08,197 --> 00:33:09,257
And you're very stubborn.

922
00:33:09,754 --> 00:33:11,243
Stubborn, she says.

923
00:33:11,244 --> 00:33:12,697
Miss. Stubborn.

924
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:14,893
She seems pretty certain.

925
00:33:15,214 --> 00:33:17,629
This is true.

926
00:33:17,707 --> 00:33:18,900
Impatient and stubborn.

927
00:33:18,901 --> 00:33:20,394
But you need to be stubborn sometimes.

928
00:33:20,395 --> 00:33:22,133
It's definitely needed.

929
00:33:22,248 --> 00:33:24,769
It's a dangerous world out there.
You need some stubbornness.

930
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,869
As for your career,

931
00:33:27,870 --> 00:33:30,509
good fortune is coming your way
starting this year.

932
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:33,361
And it'll last for the next ten years.

933
00:33:35,115 --> 00:33:37,508
(Jackpot)

934
00:33:37,555 --> 00:33:39,135
- Ten years.
- Ten years.

935
00:33:39,136 --> 00:33:40,352
Wow, ten years.

936
00:33:40,752 --> 00:33:44,577
- That's good.
- And as for love,

937
00:33:44,677 --> 00:33:46,797
you'll meet your destined partner
this year.

938
00:33:46,926 --> 00:33:49,382
If someone comes along,
you have to open your heart.

939
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:52,430
Three will come. Choose wisely.

940
00:33:52,431 --> 00:33:54,699
- Three?
- Three guys?

941
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:57,364
(Not one, not two, but three men!)

942
00:33:57,372 --> 00:33:59,224
- Meow!
- Meow! Meow!

943
00:33:59,225 --> 00:34:00,912
- Who are you going to choose?
- Catch!

944
00:34:00,913 --> 00:34:02,774
Who's going to be mine?

945
00:34:03,880 --> 00:34:05,911
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

946
00:34:05,912 --> 00:34:06,980
(Much appreciated)

947
00:34:07,533 --> 00:34:09,606
(It's Sian's turn now.)

948
00:34:09,853 --> 00:34:12,179
(Nervous)

949
00:34:12,412 --> 00:34:16,626
You're the one putting gold
on the back of the Buddha statue.

950
00:34:16,731 --> 00:34:19,298
You're someone who does good
behind the scenes without seeking credit.

951
00:34:19,299 --> 00:34:21,896
Even when you do good deeds,
no one knows about them.

952
00:34:22,266 --> 00:34:23,866
(Emotional)

953
00:34:23,892 --> 00:34:28,086
- We'll know.
- For sure. Don't worry.

954
00:34:28,452 --> 00:34:30,072
But that would really suck.

955
00:34:30,073 --> 00:34:31,102
It's not fair.

956
00:34:31,747 --> 00:34:34,259
You're good at making money, too.

957
00:34:34,260 --> 00:34:37,720
You love your family,
and you'd do anything for them.

958
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:39,627
Amazing daughter.

959
00:34:39,893 --> 00:34:42,828
(She will be a rich and nice daughter.)

960
00:34:43,016 --> 00:34:47,435
Right now, you're in a period
where money comes easily.

961
00:34:47,436 --> 00:34:48,456
And that begins...

962
00:34:48,883 --> 00:34:50,656
this year. You're destined
to become very wealthy.

963
00:34:51,803 --> 00:34:54,025
Everything's working out for everyone!

964
00:34:54,026 --> 00:34:55,660
It's really working out
for the three of us!

965
00:34:55,734 --> 00:34:56,654
- Yes.
- I'm so glad.

966
00:34:56,655 --> 00:34:58,830
But even in Korea,

967
00:34:59,061 --> 00:35:00,231
they said my luck is just getting started.

968
00:35:00,232 --> 00:35:01,166
- Really?
- Yeah.

969
00:35:01,167 --> 00:35:04,736
Looks like you picked a winner, Producer.

970
00:35:05,113 --> 00:35:07,672
You really made the perfect choice.

971
00:35:07,747 --> 00:35:14,373
I also see a lot of people
who'll help you.

972
00:35:14,374 --> 00:35:16,618
You'll have supportive coworkers,

973
00:35:16,619 --> 00:35:18,933
and you'll meet a lot of people
who'll help you along the way.

974
00:35:18,973 --> 00:35:20,385
A lot of benefactors, she says!

975
00:35:20,386 --> 00:35:23,688
- Benefactor 1, 2, 3!
- Benefactors!

976
00:35:23,766 --> 00:35:25,399
(I've already met benefactors!)

977
00:35:25,473 --> 00:35:26,758
Benefactors? To queens!

978
00:35:27,446 --> 00:35:28,858
- Queens!
- Queens!

979
00:35:28,859 --> 00:35:30,552
(With benefactors, they are now queens.)

980
00:35:31,078 --> 00:35:33,611
Thank you.

981
00:35:35,599 --> 00:35:38,503
- At last.
- That look of "Finally, it's you."

982
00:35:38,930 --> 00:35:39,965
"Finally it's you?"

983
00:35:40,019 --> 00:35:42,874
Let's get this loud one over with.

984
00:35:43,250 --> 00:35:45,915
People born with this fate...

985
00:35:45,916 --> 00:35:48,503
tend to be very straightforward
with their words.

986
00:35:48,703 --> 00:35:50,936
The moment they know it's not right,
they walk away.

987
00:35:51,036 --> 00:35:52,570
This is true.

988
00:35:52,571 --> 00:35:55,120
It's obvious what you like and don't like.

989
00:35:55,161 --> 00:35:57,022
- That's right.
- You either love it or hate it.

990
00:35:58,288 --> 00:36:00,373
You're a strong and adventurous type.

991
00:36:00,374 --> 00:36:01,914
You're bold, courageous,

992
00:36:02,214 --> 00:36:03,581
and someone people can always rely on.

993
00:36:03,582 --> 00:36:04,996
- She's right.
- Like manly?

994
00:36:04,997 --> 00:36:06,231
Yes.

995
00:36:06,321 --> 00:36:07,465
I'm a warrior at heart!

996
00:36:08,794 --> 00:36:10,135
Yeah, I hear that a lot.

997
00:36:10,814 --> 00:36:15,520
You've probably been making
a lot of money since last February.

998
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:18,274
Your career has a lot of good things
in store for you.

999
00:36:18,426 --> 00:36:19,760
And this will last...

1000
00:36:20,187 --> 00:36:22,240
for the next eleven years.

1001
00:36:22,241 --> 00:36:24,716
Okay.

1002
00:36:24,770 --> 00:36:26,838
- We're all so lucky.
- Yes, sir.

1003
00:36:26,839 --> 00:36:27,929
(All four of them have good luck.)

1004
00:36:28,297 --> 00:36:30,384
(She can't help but dance.)

1005
00:36:30,864 --> 00:36:33,324
Thank you.

1006
00:36:33,404 --> 00:36:35,536
Let's look at our compatibility,

1007
00:36:35,537 --> 00:36:37,062
and do a tarot reading.

1008
00:36:37,276 --> 00:36:40,331
- Compatibility reading. Let's go!
- Let's go.

1009
00:36:40,469 --> 00:36:41,866
It's been forever
since I had a tarot reading.

1010
00:36:42,300 --> 00:36:44,556
I don't even remember when I had one.

1011
00:36:46,387 --> 00:36:49,341
(Pick a card each.)

1012
00:36:49,387 --> 00:36:50,875
- One.
- One.

1013
00:36:51,342 --> 00:36:52,677
- At once.
- Okay.

1014
00:36:52,854 --> 00:36:55,013
- Let's pick together.
- Alright.

1015
00:36:55,513 --> 00:36:56,815
I'm going to pick...

1016
00:36:57,712 --> 00:36:59,284
In 1, 2, 3.

1017
00:36:59,952 --> 00:37:01,820
(Choosing carefully)

1018
00:37:01,821 --> 00:37:02,954
This one.

1019
00:37:04,452 --> 00:37:06,324
I'm so excited!

1020
00:37:06,658 --> 00:37:07,992
Our compatibility!

1021
00:37:09,276 --> 00:37:11,263
(Nervous)

1022
00:37:11,810 --> 00:37:15,876
Even more nerve-racking
than the personal readings.

1023
00:37:18,256 --> 00:37:22,605
(The cards are revealed one by one.)

1024
00:37:22,606 --> 00:37:25,119
(Harimu, Sian, Gabee, Won Ji)

1025
00:37:25,396 --> 00:37:27,689
This person is good at what she does,

1026
00:37:27,690 --> 00:37:31,150
but she's especially good with money.

1027
00:37:31,303 --> 00:37:32,283
You're the money manager!

1028
00:37:32,284 --> 00:37:33,716
(Born to handle the money?)

1029
00:37:33,717 --> 00:37:34,652
You're our money manager.

1030
00:37:34,996 --> 00:37:37,809
The second card represents someone
who gets along with everyone.

1031
00:37:37,810 --> 00:37:41,901
You naturally fit in
and bring harmony to the group.

1032
00:37:41,967 --> 00:37:43,967
Yeah, definitely.

1033
00:37:43,968 --> 00:37:45,864
- A peacemaker.
- The one who holds us together.

1034
00:37:47,042 --> 00:37:49,042
(So far, the four of them are
getting along perfectly.)

1035
00:37:49,043 --> 00:37:50,708
(Expecting good word)

1036
00:37:50,988 --> 00:37:52,488
The third person...

1037
00:37:52,608 --> 00:37:53,938
complains a lot.

1038
00:37:56,375 --> 00:37:57,869
(Oops.)

1039
00:37:58,242 --> 00:37:59,867
She's picking up mine too.

1040
00:37:59,868 --> 00:38:00,935
(Dizzy)

1041
00:38:01,235 --> 00:38:03,948
But this person keeps everyone grounded.

1042
00:38:04,809 --> 00:38:06,551
So I'm the problem.

1043
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:07,685
I'm the problem.

1044
00:38:07,686 --> 00:38:09,187
- Not at all!
- No way.

1045
00:38:09,188 --> 00:38:10,989
- There are zero problems.
- We're just different.

1046
00:38:10,990 --> 00:38:12,724
I'm the problem.

1047
00:38:13,108 --> 00:38:17,315
You may work together,
but you'll grow into close friends.

1048
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:18,880
you'll be loving friends.

1049
00:38:18,881 --> 00:38:21,199
We'll become friends
who truly care about each other.

1050
00:38:22,035 --> 00:38:24,435
This is so true. You're right.

1051
00:38:25,036 --> 00:38:27,305
I just need to keep my mouth shut.

1052
00:38:27,306 --> 00:38:28,353
- No way.
- Come on!

1053
00:38:28,354 --> 00:38:30,074
She's not like that!

1054
00:38:30,899 --> 00:38:32,477
I think it's good advice.

1055
00:38:32,478 --> 00:38:34,813
- Being too straightforward can be...
- No, I'm the impatient one.

1056
00:38:34,814 --> 00:38:36,114
We will keep our mouths shut.

1057
00:38:36,115 --> 00:38:37,148
Zip.

1058
00:38:37,149 --> 00:38:38,341
Then nothing will work.

1059
00:38:39,768 --> 00:38:42,375
You're good.
You can keep traveling together.

1060
00:38:43,808 --> 00:38:45,123
Thank you.

1061
00:38:45,423 --> 00:38:47,759
Alright. We're a good combo!

1062
00:38:47,874 --> 00:38:50,562
We're all good personally.

1063
00:38:50,787 --> 00:38:53,598
But I want to know
if our show's going to go big.

1064
00:38:54,876 --> 00:38:56,067
She said we'll go big.

1065
00:38:57,992 --> 00:39:00,412
Dang! She said it three times!

1066
00:39:00,445 --> 00:39:02,340
- She said "Dang."
- Dang! Dang! Dang!

1067
00:39:02,341 --> 00:39:04,832
It means it will become famous.

1068
00:39:04,899 --> 00:39:07,425
- You mean we'll make it big?
- Fame.

1069
00:39:07,426 --> 00:39:09,814
So we're going to take the world by storm?

1070
00:39:10,440 --> 00:39:11,416
Okay.

1071
00:39:12,100 --> 00:39:14,219
- I'm so happy.
- This is great.

1072
00:39:14,220 --> 00:39:16,220
Thank you.

1073
00:39:16,986 --> 00:39:17,922
We are compatible.

1074
00:39:18,159 --> 00:39:19,992
- I knew we'd be a good team.
- Sure.

1075
00:39:19,993 --> 00:39:20,919
It was so obvious!

1076
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:22,961
Of course. We felt it all along.

1077
00:39:22,962 --> 00:39:23,907
(After the interesting astrology reading)

1078
00:39:24,353 --> 00:39:26,464
Was there anything that felt
especially accurate?

1079
00:39:26,465 --> 00:39:30,869
Wherever I go,
they always tell me I'm impatient.

1080
00:39:30,952 --> 00:39:33,304
I guess it's just the way I am.

1081
00:39:33,305 --> 00:39:36,891
They always say my face gives me away.

1082
00:39:36,892 --> 00:39:38,291
I'm always told that I'm stubborn, too.

1083
00:39:38,292 --> 00:39:39,744
Maybe I look like it?

1084
00:39:39,778 --> 00:39:41,771
They always tell me...

1085
00:39:41,784 --> 00:39:43,014
- You're fickle?
- Yes, fickle.

1086
00:39:43,038 --> 00:39:45,617
I'm so happy she said we're a good match.

1087
00:39:45,618 --> 00:39:47,185
That's all that matters!

1088
00:39:47,186 --> 00:39:48,887
That's what matters most.

1089
00:39:49,191 --> 00:39:50,688
I heard they have...

1090
00:39:50,689 --> 00:39:51,658
a talisman shop here.

1091
00:39:51,659 --> 00:39:53,825
Yeah, they have one here.
It's close by.

1092
00:39:53,872 --> 00:39:56,118
Let me guide you the way to the shop.

1093
00:39:56,119 --> 00:39:57,432
I think this is the entrance.

1094
00:39:57,433 --> 00:39:59,898
That's right. It begins here.

1095
00:39:59,899 --> 00:40:00,958
Here we go.

1096
00:40:00,959 --> 00:40:02,290
(There is a strange vibe in the alley.)

1097
00:40:02,691 --> 00:40:05,092
- But this is kind of scary.
- Exactly.

1098
00:40:05,093 --> 00:40:05,926
Look at this.

1099
00:40:06,128 --> 00:40:07,095
Don't be afraid.

1100
00:40:07,096 --> 00:40:09,831
- These things will protect you.
- Really?

1101
00:40:09,832 --> 00:40:10,965
It's a skull.

1102
00:40:10,966 --> 00:40:12,133
(Such a creepy-looking item)

1103
00:40:12,501 --> 00:40:15,503
There's something
in what looks like blood.

1104
00:40:17,072 --> 00:40:19,440
(An assortment
of creepy objects fills the stall)

1105
00:40:19,441 --> 00:40:21,342
- Is this ginseng?
- There's something.

1106
00:40:23,645 --> 00:40:24,511
It's too...

1107
00:40:25,447 --> 00:40:27,615
Everyone, look at this.
What do you think they are?

1108
00:40:27,616 --> 00:40:29,116
It looks like a goblin.

1109
00:40:29,117 --> 00:40:29,950
(Creepy)

1110
00:40:30,311 --> 00:40:31,813
(In awe)

1111
00:40:32,421 --> 00:40:34,722
(What is this place?)

1112
00:40:34,723 --> 00:40:37,792
I usually buy these kind of things
at a time,

1113
00:40:38,193 --> 00:40:39,827
but this feels way too serious.

1114
00:40:39,828 --> 00:40:42,096
- It feels way too serious, right?
- Exactly.

1115
00:40:42,197 --> 00:40:44,198
I want something I can carry every day.

1116
00:40:44,199 --> 00:40:47,067
- I want something cute.
- I hope they have something cute.

1117
00:40:47,302 --> 00:40:48,269
Like a key ring...

1118
00:40:48,270 --> 00:40:49,570
(Looking for a more
everyday kind of talisman)

1119
00:40:49,705 --> 00:40:51,005
There are so many shops here.

1120
00:40:51,573 --> 00:40:53,575
It's like Dongdaemun Market.

1121
00:40:53,576 --> 00:40:55,576
- There are so many Buddha statues
- Buddha merchandise.

1122
00:40:56,445 --> 00:40:59,147
They sell a lot of things
like necklace pendants.

1123
00:40:59,148 --> 00:41:00,848
Yes, there are so many pendants.

1124
00:41:02,150 --> 00:41:04,885
When I traveled around Thailand,

1125
00:41:05,687 --> 00:41:07,187
I saw so many people wearing pendants,

1126
00:41:07,623 --> 00:41:10,558
- about this size around their necks.
- Exactly.

1127
00:41:10,559 --> 00:41:13,428
(Thailand's amulet necklace culture)

1128
00:41:13,462 --> 00:41:15,263
(Thailand's amulet culture)

1129
00:41:15,264 --> 00:41:17,131
(Amulets are commonly worn as jewelry.)

1130
00:41:17,132 --> 00:41:18,966
(They carry spiritual
and religious significance.)

1131
00:41:18,967 --> 00:41:21,002
I guess you put the pendant in here.

1132
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:23,337
I think so.

1133
00:41:23,338 --> 00:41:25,907
They sell these frame-like key ring cases.

1134
00:41:26,608 --> 00:41:29,043
I guess you can put
whatever you want inside.

1135
00:41:29,044 --> 00:41:31,445
(Customizable amulet necklaces)

1136
00:41:32,047 --> 00:41:34,815
This one is kind of cute.
Is this a Thai person?

1137
00:41:35,017 --> 00:41:37,218
Maybe he's a monk. They're so colorful.

1138
00:41:37,219 --> 00:41:38,987
I guess there are quite
a few famous monks here.

1139
00:41:38,988 --> 00:41:40,721
Yes, well-known monks.

1140
00:41:40,722 --> 00:41:43,491
Exactly.
There are a lot of well-known monks here.

1141
00:41:44,626 --> 00:41:47,064
- This is pretty.
- There are a lot of pretty ones here.

1142
00:41:47,065 --> 00:41:48,229
Is that so?

1143
00:41:48,230 --> 00:41:50,397
Isn't this one cute?
This one is totally my style.

1144
00:41:50,799 --> 00:41:52,200
It looks like Santa Claus.

1145
00:41:52,701 --> 00:41:54,602
You really do like
colorful things, Won Ji.

1146
00:41:54,603 --> 00:41:55,970
I like this too.

1147
00:41:56,204 --> 00:41:58,037
(Searching through the items)

1148
00:41:58,038 --> 00:42:00,174
There are so many
ridiculously suggestive ones.

1149
00:42:00,175 --> 00:42:01,475
It's like a nightlife show.

1150
00:42:01,777 --> 00:42:03,377
There are so many shameless individuals.

1151
00:42:04,145 --> 00:42:07,348
And this lady too.

1152
00:42:07,349 --> 00:42:09,116
(She keeps showing them to everyone.)

1153
00:42:09,318 --> 00:42:10,751
This would be heavy
to wear around your neck.

1154
00:42:10,752 --> 00:42:11,752
Yes.

1155
00:42:12,187 --> 00:42:14,221
I want to buy it,
but it's too heavy to carry.

1156
00:42:15,290 --> 00:42:17,858
- Let's look around a little more.
- Yes, let's go.

1157
00:42:17,859 --> 00:42:19,860
(Street stalls continue
through the maze-like alleys)

1158
00:42:19,861 --> 00:42:21,395
There are so many interesting things.

1159
00:42:21,396 --> 00:42:22,696
There are some here too.

1160
00:42:22,864 --> 00:42:25,265
They have things that look like coins.

1161
00:42:27,703 --> 00:42:28,736
Let's buy one here.

1162
00:42:28,737 --> 00:42:29,570
Okay.

1163
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:32,039
There are so many cute ones.

1164
00:42:32,040 --> 00:42:33,040
Cute, right?

1165
00:42:33,743 --> 00:42:36,277
I like these old coins.

1166
00:42:36,278 --> 00:42:37,011
Me too.

1167
00:42:37,246 --> 00:42:38,412
Pretty good, right?

1168
00:42:39,081 --> 00:42:40,081
How about this one?

1169
00:42:40,615 --> 00:42:41,815
A coin?

1170
00:42:41,816 --> 00:42:44,251
- It feels like money will be flowing in.
- Right.

1171
00:42:44,252 --> 00:42:47,120
It's small enough
to carry around in your wallet.

1172
00:42:47,121 --> 00:42:48,221
Yes, it's small enough.

1173
00:42:48,222 --> 00:42:49,723
What does this coin mean?

1174
00:42:49,724 --> 00:42:51,258
It's 30 baht.

1175
00:42:51,393 --> 00:42:52,526
Does it mean 30 baht?

1176
00:42:53,362 --> 00:42:55,063
She says it means 30 baht.

1177
00:42:55,664 --> 00:42:57,365
It means 30 baht.

1178
00:42:58,034 --> 00:43:01,035
She said it's 30 baht.

1179
00:43:01,503 --> 00:43:05,639
And I think it probably
symbolizes financial luck.

1180
00:43:05,841 --> 00:43:08,409
I'll buy one for each of us four.

1181
00:43:10,112 --> 00:43:14,115
Won Ji is treating
everyone to lucky coins.

1182
00:43:16,218 --> 00:43:19,020
So that's 120 baht in total?

1183
00:43:19,821 --> 00:43:22,957
(They bought 5.6 dollars
worth of good luck)

1184
00:43:25,594 --> 00:43:27,518
The value is whatever we decide it is.

1185
00:43:27,543 --> 00:43:30,430
A talisman gets its power
from what you believe in.

1186
00:43:30,665 --> 00:43:33,233
It all comes from your own mind.

1187
00:43:33,702 --> 00:43:36,326
Let's go a little farther.
I think that's the end.

1188
00:43:36,327 --> 00:43:37,605
Let's go all the way to the end.

1189
00:43:38,007 --> 00:43:39,540
- Wait.
- Hold on.

1190
00:43:39,541 --> 00:43:40,607
There's a QR code here.

1191
00:43:40,608 --> 00:43:42,810
- Suddenly?
- All of a sudden?

1192
00:43:42,835 --> 00:43:45,212
(A suspicious QR code
appears in the amulet market.)

1193
00:43:45,213 --> 00:43:46,943
- This is crazy.
- This elephant plate is cute.

1194
00:43:47,532 --> 00:43:50,518
- Let's scan it right now.
- What's going on?

1195
00:43:53,321 --> 00:43:54,187
- What's this?
- It's a talisman.

1196
00:43:54,990 --> 00:43:55,990
All of a sudden?

1197
00:43:56,591 --> 00:43:57,457
What's this?

1198
00:43:58,693 --> 00:44:00,594
- What's this?
- Something popped up.

1199
00:44:00,595 --> 00:44:01,295
Really?

1200
00:44:04,066 --> 00:44:04,866
This is it.

1201
00:44:04,867 --> 00:44:06,234
It's an abandoned building.

1202
00:44:06,235 --> 00:44:07,668
This is so scary.

1203
00:44:07,936 --> 00:44:08,969
I'm scared.

1204
00:44:09,871 --> 00:44:11,939
(Frozen)

1205
00:44:11,940 --> 00:44:13,440
I really hate scary stuff.

1206
00:44:13,441 --> 00:44:15,943
It looks like a stopped escalator.

1207
00:44:15,944 --> 00:44:17,511
It has this old-fashioned vibe.

1208
00:44:17,512 --> 00:44:19,280
What if it's covered
in blood or something?

1209
00:44:19,482 --> 00:44:21,916
- It says it's a chance to find good luck.
- Seriously?

1210
00:44:22,184 --> 00:44:23,918
It tells us to go to a lucky place.

1211
00:44:23,919 --> 00:44:26,187
Seize your chance for good luck tonight.

1212
00:44:26,521 --> 00:44:30,591
Any luck you find there will be yours.

1213
00:44:30,592 --> 00:44:32,593
Is this some kind of treasure hunt?

1214
00:44:32,994 --> 00:44:35,095
Click here to go to the place of luck.

1215
00:44:35,897 --> 00:44:37,197
Find good luck?

1216
00:44:37,866 --> 00:44:39,100
This is totally high-tech.

1217
00:44:39,101 --> 00:44:41,636
- It says the place is closed down.
- Horror experience all of a sudden?

1218
00:44:41,903 --> 00:44:43,971
- I'm really scared.
- It says it's closed down.

1219
00:44:44,539 --> 00:44:45,372
I'm so scared.

1220
00:44:45,941 --> 00:44:47,275
Is this an abandoned-building experience?

1221
00:44:47,276 --> 00:44:50,044
(A gloomy atmosphere
surrounds this supposedly Lucky Place.)

1222
00:44:53,982 --> 00:44:56,083
It doesn't look very lucky to me.

1223
00:44:56,084 --> 00:44:57,017
(What kind of luck is here?)

1224
00:44:57,252 --> 00:44:58,519
(Not exactly thrilled)

1225
00:44:58,520 --> 00:44:59,420
It's closed down.

1226
00:44:59,421 --> 00:45:00,754
It says it's closed down.

1227
00:45:00,922 --> 00:45:02,256
It's not far from here.

1228
00:45:02,424 --> 00:45:03,324
Let's go check it out.

1229
00:45:05,994 --> 00:45:08,596
I'm a woman who went
to an abandoned building in Hong Kong.

1230
00:45:08,597 --> 00:45:09,363
Really?

1231
00:45:09,364 --> 00:45:11,799
"I'm a woman who went
to an abandoned building in Hong Kong."

1232
00:45:12,968 --> 00:45:15,302
Abandoned building in Hong Kong.

1233
00:45:15,303 --> 00:45:16,536
You went to the Himalayas too, didn't you?

1234
00:45:16,805 --> 00:45:18,873
She's been to the Himalayas and
an abandoned building in Hong Kong.

1235
00:45:19,651 --> 00:45:20,517
Let's check it out.

1236
00:45:21,046 --> 00:45:23,377
No, this is so scary.

1237
00:45:25,547 --> 00:45:27,381
I guess they have it.

1238
00:45:27,516 --> 00:45:29,617
Should I grab some coffee?

1239
00:45:30,063 --> 00:45:33,120
(They said they were going right away,
then suddenly changed course.)

1240
00:45:33,121 --> 00:45:33,988
Matcha and...

1241
00:45:35,090 --> 00:45:37,224
- Crepe.
- I want a crepe.

1242
00:45:38,089 --> 00:45:42,135
Can I have one banana chocolate crepe?

1243
00:45:42,964 --> 00:45:45,266
I need to eat a crepe
and build up my courage.

1244
00:45:45,734 --> 00:45:48,703
(Soothing her anxiety with dessert)

1245
00:45:48,704 --> 00:45:50,671
I'm going to get a Thai tea.

1246
00:45:51,940 --> 00:45:52,806
It looks good.

1247
00:45:52,807 --> 00:45:54,208
(Harimu also buys a cool, sweet dessert.)

1248
00:45:54,543 --> 00:45:55,910
Did they go get coffee?

1249
00:45:57,812 --> 00:46:00,947
(This is mine.)

1250
00:46:01,504 --> 00:46:03,116
(Meanwhile, the sisters are...)

1251
00:46:03,435 --> 00:46:06,921
(lost in their shopping spree.)

1252
00:46:07,722 --> 00:46:08,855
Are you buying all of that?

1253
00:46:08,856 --> 00:46:10,223
No, I'm not.

1254
00:46:10,358 --> 00:46:12,659
Can you help me pick something?

1255
00:46:12,660 --> 00:46:13,560
Sure.

1256
00:46:13,829 --> 00:46:14,695
Number one.

1257
00:46:15,297 --> 00:46:16,063
Number two.

1258
00:46:16,698 --> 00:46:17,498
Number three.

1259
00:46:18,833 --> 00:46:19,799
This one.

1260
00:46:21,202 --> 00:46:23,703
(Going with the blue one
the youngers recommended)

1261
00:46:27,976 --> 00:46:29,644
(Shaking her head)

1262
00:46:30,011 --> 00:46:32,522
(She secretly tries to bargain.)

1263
00:46:32,547 --> 00:46:34,381
Is there no discount?

1264
00:46:35,183 --> 00:46:35,983
I have no choice.

1265
00:46:35,984 --> 00:46:37,918
(When the negotiation fails,
her voice gets louder.)

1266
00:46:38,186 --> 00:46:39,153
I don't have much money.

1267
00:46:39,721 --> 00:46:42,156
(She tries to win sympathy,
even though they can't understand her.)

1268
00:46:42,290 --> 00:46:45,459
It's so pretty. It's totally my style.

1269
00:46:45,560 --> 00:46:48,429
(Spending 250 baht on peacock upkeep)

1270
00:46:48,430 --> 00:46:50,897
Oh, right. I ordered a crepe.

1271
00:46:51,166 --> 00:46:54,668
I need to pick up my crepe.

1272
00:46:55,737 --> 00:46:57,471
This one is cute too.

1273
00:46:59,440 --> 00:47:02,275
(She tends to lose all sense of reason
whenever she sees something cute.)

1274
00:47:02,276 --> 00:47:03,276
This is totally you.

1275
00:47:04,079 --> 00:47:06,347
It's totally mine.

1276
00:47:06,748 --> 00:47:08,849
(She immediately claims ownership.)

1277
00:47:09,384 --> 00:47:11,828
(It's 59 baht for one,
or 100 baht for two.)

1278
00:47:11,853 --> 00:47:14,087
How about 50 baht for one?

1279
00:47:14,723 --> 00:47:15,556
Okay.

1280
00:47:15,724 --> 00:47:17,491
I need to go pick up my crepe.

1281
00:47:17,993 --> 00:47:19,126
(There she came.)

1282
00:47:19,127 --> 00:47:20,027
It's done now.

1283
00:47:20,729 --> 00:47:22,596
- I came at exactly the right time.
- Yes.

1284
00:47:22,764 --> 00:47:24,664
- It took quite a while.
- Let's share this.

1285
00:47:26,134 --> 00:47:27,901
Let's sit down.

1286
00:47:29,537 --> 00:47:30,938
My pants ripped again.

1287
00:47:31,607 --> 00:47:33,841
Do you want to go change?
You brought a spare pair.

1288
00:47:33,842 --> 00:47:34,642
Right.

1289
00:47:34,877 --> 00:47:36,710
I knew this would happen,
so I brought another pair of pants.

1290
00:47:37,245 --> 00:47:40,380
Then I'll show off
the shirt I just bought too.

1291
00:47:40,615 --> 00:47:41,548
I'll be right back.

1292
00:47:42,150 --> 00:47:44,184
Doesn't she keep
twerking behind our backs?

1293
00:47:44,586 --> 00:47:46,954
(Not shaking, just covering)

1294
00:47:47,523 --> 00:47:49,257
(She was supposed to be right back.)

1295
00:47:50,158 --> 00:47:51,291
Buying something.

1296
00:47:52,861 --> 00:47:56,331
Since my pants ripped,

1297
00:47:56,332 --> 00:47:58,299
I changed into the shirt I bought earlier.

1298
00:47:58,300 --> 00:47:59,967
And she really likes this headscarf.

1299
00:47:59,968 --> 00:48:02,236
- Exactly.
- I'm good at getting people into things.

1300
00:48:02,237 --> 00:48:03,571
So I brought her over.

1301
00:48:03,572 --> 00:48:05,706
I want to copy your style.
You're such an it girl.

1302
00:48:05,707 --> 00:48:07,908
- I'm an it girl.
- You're an it girl.

1303
00:48:08,310 --> 00:48:09,377
What did you buy?

1304
00:48:09,378 --> 00:48:11,479
The one you recommended.

1305
00:48:11,480 --> 00:48:12,280
I like that.

1306
00:48:12,580 --> 00:48:14,581
I really wanted to try this.

1307
00:48:14,582 --> 00:48:15,982
Now is the perfect time.

1308
00:48:15,983 --> 00:48:17,017
Now is the time.

1309
00:48:17,018 --> 00:48:18,486
Because your outfit is way too plain.

1310
00:48:18,487 --> 00:48:19,686
It's too plain, right?

1311
00:48:19,687 --> 00:48:21,821
It's so plain that I'm not happy.

1312
00:48:21,822 --> 00:48:23,690
I've always loved scarves, so...

1313
00:48:24,125 --> 00:48:26,560
Isn't this pin so cute? Should I get one?

1314
00:48:26,928 --> 00:48:28,128
Isn't this one so cute?

1315
00:48:28,129 --> 00:48:29,062
It really is.

1316
00:48:29,063 --> 00:48:30,097
They're three for 100 baht.

1317
00:48:30,398 --> 00:48:31,833
It looks like you.

1318
00:48:32,100 --> 00:48:34,034
- It really is.
- Right?

1319
00:48:34,035 --> 00:48:35,569
This is totally me.

1320
00:48:35,671 --> 00:48:37,472
Even the round nose.

1321
00:48:37,473 --> 00:48:39,206
- This is totally you, Won Ji.
- I know.

1322
00:48:39,942 --> 00:48:41,342
But you never wear pins.

1323
00:48:41,343 --> 00:48:43,143
- No, I don't.
- I've never seen you wear one.

1324
00:48:43,144 --> 00:48:44,278
Pins don't suit me.

1325
00:48:44,579 --> 00:48:46,179
Then do you want to get
matching pins with me?

1326
00:48:46,681 --> 00:48:47,481
Matching pins?

1327
00:48:48,516 --> 00:48:49,316
Tempting.

1328
00:48:50,318 --> 00:48:51,952
Because my bangs keep falling down.

1329
00:48:51,953 --> 00:48:53,987
Really? They're three for 100 baht.

1330
00:48:54,589 --> 00:48:56,023
So, should we get this or this?

1331
00:48:56,691 --> 00:48:58,660
- Put it up against your hair.
- This one is ugly.

1332
00:48:59,294 --> 00:49:01,996
- The cherry one looks much better.
- Put this one back.

1333
00:49:03,064 --> 00:49:04,998
How about the strawberry one?

1334
00:49:05,810 --> 00:49:07,568
- But it's similar, right?
- This one is cute.

1335
00:49:07,569 --> 00:49:09,236
- What about this one?
- Which one?

1336
00:49:09,671 --> 00:49:11,772
That's pretty.

1337
00:49:11,773 --> 00:49:12,773
Okay.

1338
00:49:13,041 --> 00:49:15,042
I'm not really into it, but...

1339
00:49:15,043 --> 00:49:16,610
- What else is here?
- Isn't this one better?

1340
00:49:16,811 --> 00:49:18,572
What about this smiley one?

1341
00:49:18,596 --> 00:49:19,847
Isn't this one pretty?

1342
00:49:19,848 --> 00:49:21,048
(Well...)

1343
00:49:21,049 --> 00:49:24,218
- I don't think our tastes match well.
- Absolutely.

1344
00:49:24,219 --> 00:49:25,986
I don't think we can do a group buy.

1345
00:49:26,831 --> 00:49:28,022
Group buying?

1346
00:49:28,890 --> 00:49:30,757
Then how about we pick one for you?

1347
00:49:30,758 --> 00:49:31,825
- Great idea.
- Great idea.

1348
00:49:31,826 --> 00:49:33,303
- Are there any other options?
- This one.

1349
00:49:33,328 --> 00:49:35,896
(The smiley pin
she couldn't quite let go of)

1350
00:49:35,930 --> 00:49:38,698
There's one more. This one too.

1351
00:49:38,699 --> 00:49:40,600
Not a chance.

1352
00:49:40,969 --> 00:49:42,836
I think we're just not compatible at all.

1353
00:49:42,837 --> 00:49:44,905
But that one is the best.

1354
00:49:44,906 --> 00:49:46,006
Is this one the best?

1355
00:49:47,008 --> 00:49:49,143
We've made our final decision.

1356
00:49:49,144 --> 00:49:51,144
The one I wanted...

1357
00:49:51,145 --> 00:49:51,979
Why things...

1358
00:49:51,980 --> 00:49:53,413
Let's smile a lot.

1359
00:49:53,414 --> 00:49:55,482
"Let's smile a lot" pin.

1360
00:49:55,483 --> 00:49:58,485
(Before we change our mind,
let's just pay for it.)

1361
00:49:58,486 --> 00:49:59,953
We bought our pins.

1362
00:50:00,287 --> 00:50:01,887
- Matching pins!
- Cute!

1363
00:50:02,047 --> 00:50:03,367
I'll put it on you.

1364
00:50:03,547 --> 00:50:05,169
- A cute couple!
- Okay.

1365
00:50:05,636 --> 00:50:07,271
- Should we put them on each other?
- Yes.

1366
00:50:08,223 --> 00:50:09,523
I'll put it here.

1367
00:50:09,603 --> 00:50:11,208
- Okay!
- Okay!

1368
00:50:11,609 --> 00:50:13,177
- That's cute.
- It's not bad.

1369
00:50:13,577 --> 00:50:15,079
- It looks good.
- It does?

1370
00:50:15,177 --> 00:50:16,247
Okay!

1371
00:50:16,780 --> 00:50:18,249
We spent money again.

1372
00:50:18,250 --> 00:50:19,729
- Cute!
- Adorable.

1373
00:50:19,730 --> 00:50:22,211
(Their suitcase slowly fills up
today too.)

1374
00:50:23,187 --> 00:50:24,555
I did some research.

1375
00:50:25,289 --> 00:50:27,464
The lucky place that we're visiting today.

1376
00:50:27,465 --> 00:50:30,094
It's a famous filming location
for Thai horror films.

1377
00:50:30,171 --> 00:50:31,262
Let's not do that.

1378
00:50:31,664 --> 00:50:33,364
There are a few ghost stories
about this place.

1379
00:50:33,365 --> 00:50:35,365
One says that after the theater
was abandoned,

1380
00:50:35,555 --> 00:50:38,369
people saw someone sitting alone
in the empty audience.

1381
00:50:39,642 --> 00:50:41,572
(Humming scary music)

1382
00:50:41,573 --> 00:50:43,407
What is she going to do alone?

1383
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:45,241
So it's haunted.

1384
00:50:45,242 --> 00:50:46,744
People also have seen...

1385
00:50:46,893 --> 00:50:48,893
ghostly figures performing on the stage.

1386
00:50:49,446 --> 00:50:50,881
That doesn't make sense.

1387
00:50:51,582 --> 00:50:54,451
At night, the projector starts
playing movies on its own.

1388
00:50:55,920 --> 00:50:57,920
Who's turning that on?

1389
00:50:57,978 --> 00:50:58,889
A ghost!

1390
00:50:58,944 --> 00:51:00,291
(No way.)

1391
00:51:00,358 --> 00:51:02,993
They hear screams
coming from the audience.

1392
00:51:03,231 --> 00:51:04,604
That could be me.

1393
00:51:04,605 --> 00:51:05,629
They can hear someone whimper.

1394
00:51:05,630 --> 00:51:06,430
That's ridiculous.

1395
00:51:06,884 --> 00:51:09,264
- You've been to a haunted house.
- I have.

1396
00:51:09,265 --> 00:51:10,701
- In Hong Kong?
- In Hong Kong?

1397
00:51:10,702 --> 00:51:12,036
An abandoned school in Hong Kong.

1398
00:51:12,037 --> 00:51:12,870
How was it?

1399
00:51:13,145 --> 00:51:15,472
- It was so scary.
- I hate it.

1400
00:51:15,473 --> 00:51:17,575
The aura makes it impossible to go inside.

1401
00:51:17,605 --> 00:51:18,709
Did you see something?

1402
00:51:18,989 --> 00:51:19,932
I did.

1403
00:51:19,933 --> 00:51:21,412
What did you see?

1404
00:51:21,413 --> 00:51:22,380
I'm not sure.

1405
00:51:22,613 --> 00:51:23,547
But I did something.

1406
00:51:23,548 --> 00:51:25,783
- What was it?
- I felt some energy.

1407
00:51:26,317 --> 00:51:27,585
There were bats flying around.

1408
00:51:27,675 --> 00:51:28,552
- What?
- What?

1409
00:51:29,253 --> 00:51:31,655
I promised myself
I'd never go to a haunted place again.

1410
00:51:32,356 --> 00:51:33,657
Never ever.

1411
00:51:34,287 --> 00:51:36,287
Are you afraid of ghosts?

1412
00:51:36,288 --> 00:51:37,455
- I hate them.
- I hate them.

1413
00:51:37,508 --> 00:51:38,929
- All three of you?
- I hate them so much.

1414
00:51:39,797 --> 00:51:41,332
At least one of us shouldn't.

1415
00:51:41,333 --> 00:51:43,122
(What are the four scaredy-cats going
to do there?)

1416
00:51:43,241 --> 00:51:46,249
- We need someone to lead us.
- I'll do it.

1417
00:51:47,620 --> 00:51:49,960
But Sian, it should be someone
who's good at it.

1418
00:51:51,241 --> 00:51:52,910
You said you hated ghosts.

1419
00:51:53,510 --> 00:51:55,346
- No. I'll do it.
- You said you hated them.

1420
00:51:55,347 --> 00:51:56,914
- You want to?
- I'll beat them up.

1421
00:51:56,915 --> 00:51:58,582
- Really?
- I'm quite strong.

1422
00:51:58,681 --> 00:51:59,917
- Okay.
- Are you sure?

1423
00:52:00,417 --> 00:52:01,752
I'll beat them all up.

1424
00:52:01,841 --> 00:52:02,553
That sounds good.

1425
00:52:02,554 --> 00:52:04,587
Sian is also taller than us.

1426
00:52:04,588 --> 00:52:06,208
Let's hide behind her.

1427
00:52:06,209 --> 00:52:08,209
- Yes. We should hide behind her.
- Just hide behind me.

1428
00:52:08,594 --> 00:52:10,280
(Why do I feel like it was a trap?)

1429
00:52:10,281 --> 00:52:11,261
That's good.

1430
00:52:11,374 --> 00:52:12,428
I'm scared.

1431
00:52:12,429 --> 00:52:13,998
I'm sure I'm the strongest among us.

1432
00:52:13,999 --> 00:52:15,399
Okay. Then let's get going.

1433
00:52:15,685 --> 00:52:17,134
Shall we go?

1434
00:52:17,135 --> 00:52:21,085
(Let's go check what our luck is.)

1435
00:52:21,438 --> 00:52:22,740
Which bus are we taking?

1436
00:52:22,892 --> 00:52:25,609
A green bus that says 60.

1437
00:52:26,291 --> 00:52:29,246
We're waiting for our bus.

1438
00:52:29,324 --> 00:52:33,384
There's a bus
that goes to the abandoned theater.

1439
00:52:34,198 --> 00:52:35,853
We don't have much money,

1440
00:52:36,362 --> 00:52:37,921
so we should take a bus.

1441
00:52:38,489 --> 00:52:39,990
Please have your coins ready.

1442
00:52:41,416 --> 00:52:42,793
- The fare...
- My wallet.

1443
00:52:43,321 --> 00:52:44,061
This is my wallet.

1444
00:52:44,062 --> 00:52:45,763
I might need a wallet.

1445
00:52:46,022 --> 00:52:47,731
- You should buy an elephant wallet.
- Yes.

1446
00:52:48,098 --> 00:52:51,301
My butt is getting hot.

1447
00:52:51,602 --> 00:52:53,237
It feels like a sauna.

1448
00:52:53,238 --> 00:52:56,540
- It's like a butt sauna.
- A butt sauna.

1449
00:52:57,174 --> 00:53:00,010
It'll come soon.

1450
00:53:00,298 --> 00:53:02,546
Two minutes to go.

1451
00:53:03,213 --> 00:53:05,349
<i>Arriving in two minutes</i>

1452
00:53:06,436 --> 00:53:08,304
I hope the bus looked like this.

1453
00:53:09,176 --> 00:53:10,821
It's not coming.

1454
00:53:12,483 --> 00:53:15,096
(Everyone got on their buses,
except them.)

1455
00:53:15,689 --> 00:53:17,027
Our bus is not coming.

1456
00:53:17,743 --> 00:53:20,868
A few moments later.

1457
00:53:20,869 --> 00:53:23,375
One hour later.

1458
00:53:23,376 --> 00:53:29,141
(They just keep waiting.)

1459
00:53:29,348 --> 00:53:32,209
- We're waiting and waiting.
- Look here.

1460
00:53:32,588 --> 00:53:34,741
- Try to look like you're forcing a smile.
- Okay.

1461
00:53:36,808 --> 00:53:37,648
Okay.

1462
00:53:37,649 --> 00:53:41,859
(Guys, don't do this.)

1463
00:53:42,453 --> 00:53:44,221
Is traveling always like this?

1464
00:53:44,586 --> 00:53:46,656
I completely checked out.

1465
00:53:46,657 --> 00:53:48,058
Are you losing your mind?

1466
00:53:48,719 --> 00:53:50,830
(A lot of them are losing their minds.)

1467
00:53:50,831 --> 00:53:51,995
What's wrong?

1468
00:53:52,118 --> 00:53:55,432
I want to go home.

1469
00:53:55,433 --> 00:53:56,867
We can't anyway!

1470
00:53:57,134 --> 00:53:58,669
We can't go home anyway!

1471
00:53:58,698 --> 00:54:00,771
- Hey!
- We can't go home anyway.

1472
00:54:01,178 --> 00:54:03,507
We can't go home!

1473
00:54:04,541 --> 00:54:06,110
Let me go ask.

1474
00:54:06,111 --> 00:54:09,546
Someone has been waiting
as long as we have.

1475
00:54:09,671 --> 00:54:10,748
She might be waiting for the same bus.

1476
00:54:10,749 --> 00:54:13,604
- Won Ji!
- Won Ji!

1477
00:54:13,777 --> 00:54:15,986
Hello.

1478
00:54:16,084 --> 00:54:18,622
Which bus are you waiting for?

1479
00:54:19,957 --> 00:54:21,304
No bus?

1480
00:54:21,305 --> 00:54:22,760
Why isn't it coming?

1481
00:54:22,761 --> 00:54:23,961
Oh, my.

1482
00:54:23,962 --> 00:54:26,420
- Traffic jam.
- Traffic jam?

1483
00:54:28,525 --> 00:54:31,172
All other buses came except ours.

1484
00:54:31,173 --> 00:54:32,627
Oh, we've never even seen that bus before.

1485
00:54:32,628 --> 00:54:34,628
- It's 1-92.
- It's good to see it.

1486
00:54:35,402 --> 00:54:37,007
So, I asked her.

1487
00:54:37,941 --> 00:54:40,744
She says it might be
because of traffic jams.

1488
00:54:41,011 --> 00:54:43,614
- But other buses had no problem.
- I know.

1489
00:54:43,615 --> 00:54:46,364
So I was thinking,

1490
00:54:46,365 --> 00:54:47,885
what if we all chip in for a taxi?

1491
00:54:48,124 --> 00:54:49,738
(That's a good idea.)

1492
00:54:49,764 --> 00:54:51,255
Let's just buy one less item.

1493
00:54:51,256 --> 00:54:52,831
Why didn't we think of that?

1494
00:54:52,832 --> 00:54:54,158
Let's call a taxi.

1495
00:54:54,524 --> 00:54:56,026
I'll do it.

1496
00:54:56,771 --> 00:54:59,696
Let's take a taxi.

1497
00:54:59,697 --> 00:55:00,796
What is she doing?

1498
00:55:00,797 --> 00:55:04,837
(Twerking for a taxi
in the middle of Bangkok)

1499
00:55:04,891 --> 00:55:07,229
- Let's go to our lucky place!
- Let's go.

1500
00:55:07,230 --> 00:55:09,907
I wonder how lucky we're going to get.

1501
00:55:09,969 --> 00:55:11,969
It better be some serious good luck.

1502
00:55:12,663 --> 00:55:14,663
It better be worth it when we get there.

1503
00:55:15,550 --> 00:55:18,264
(Setting off
while demanding some good luck)

1504
00:55:19,171 --> 00:55:22,437
(It's almost sunset now.)

1505
00:55:22,484 --> 00:55:23,353
Let's go.

1506
00:55:23,754 --> 00:55:24,655
- Okay!
- Let's go.

1507
00:55:25,088 --> 00:55:28,158
Taxis are indeed convenient!

1508
00:55:28,159 --> 00:55:30,527
- They're the best!
- Taxis!

1509
00:55:30,553 --> 00:55:31,461
Is it this way?

1510
00:55:32,526 --> 00:55:33,897
The map says...

1511
00:55:34,492 --> 00:55:35,465
It's over there.

1512
00:55:36,959 --> 00:55:38,079
We should cross.

1513
00:55:38,080 --> 00:55:40,337
- That does look like a theater.
- It looks so abandoned.

1514
00:55:41,205 --> 00:55:43,507
This neighborhood is really eerie.

1515
00:55:43,807 --> 00:55:45,976
I don't want to get closer.

1516
00:55:46,977 --> 00:55:48,879
I can't believe it.

1517
00:55:49,271 --> 00:55:50,871
(Rumbling)

1518
00:55:52,431 --> 00:55:55,219
(Suddenly, thunder rumbles.)

1519
00:55:55,418 --> 00:55:57,054
Thunder cracked.

1520
00:55:57,103 --> 00:55:59,363
This is not a set, right?

1521
00:55:59,364 --> 00:56:01,225
Did you prepare the weather too?

1522
00:56:01,504 --> 00:56:02,857
Is this an outdoor set?

1523
00:56:02,858 --> 00:56:03,990
This is "The Truman Show," isn't it?

1524
00:56:03,991 --> 00:56:05,729
Thunder rumbled.

1525
00:56:06,078 --> 00:56:09,233
I've never even watched a horror movie.

1526
00:56:09,234 --> 00:56:11,043
- I hate horror movies.
- Me too.

1527
00:56:11,044 --> 00:56:12,803
I even hate the posters.

1528
00:56:14,104 --> 00:56:15,939
I've never been
to a haunted house attraction either.

1529
00:56:16,440 --> 00:56:18,440
I've done that, at least.

1530
00:56:18,544 --> 00:56:20,911
Then does that make you less scared?

1531
00:56:20,912 --> 00:56:22,346
No, I'm still scared.

1532
00:56:22,347 --> 00:56:23,780
You've only done it.

1533
00:56:24,177 --> 00:56:25,549
I'm already scared.

1534
00:56:26,604 --> 00:56:28,785
The thunder really felt staged.

1535
00:56:29,086 --> 00:56:30,988
It came out of nowhere.

1536
00:56:30,989 --> 00:56:34,162
(Something feels off from the start.)

1537
00:56:34,591 --> 00:56:35,826
I can do it.

1538
00:56:36,393 --> 00:56:38,495
- Is that the building?
- I can do this.

1539
00:56:39,515 --> 00:56:42,267
(Despite their determination,)

1540
00:56:43,013 --> 00:56:47,927
(darkness soon fell
on their lucky place too.)

1541
00:56:52,209 --> 00:56:56,444
(Welcome.)

1542
00:56:56,778 --> 00:56:59,750
- This is the place.
- Come on.

1543
00:56:59,798 --> 00:57:00,851
- Here?
- Wait.

1544
00:57:00,870 --> 00:57:01,611
Yes.

1545
00:57:01,684 --> 00:57:03,220
It looks eerie.

1546
00:57:03,221 --> 00:57:04,688
- Is this the theater?
- Yes.

1547
00:57:04,689 --> 00:57:07,287
It does look like a haunted place.

1548
00:57:07,921 --> 00:57:09,626
Look how dark the entrance is.

1549
00:57:09,781 --> 00:57:11,261
Isn't it too dark?

1550
00:57:11,427 --> 00:57:13,096
Don't we need a flashlight?

1551
00:57:13,741 --> 00:57:15,534
(Noticing Harimu's face)

1552
00:57:15,567 --> 00:57:17,034
Harimu, are you all right?

1553
00:57:17,087 --> 00:57:18,568
I'm really not.

1554
00:57:18,569 --> 00:57:20,737
You look really scared.

1555
00:57:21,227 --> 00:57:23,307
Honestly, think about it.

1556
00:57:23,594 --> 00:57:24,775
If we see a ghost,

1557
00:57:25,094 --> 00:57:27,454
that means our show will go viral.

1558
00:57:27,455 --> 00:57:29,314
That's true.

1559
00:57:29,315 --> 00:57:31,615
If we don't, that's still good
because that means we're safe.

1560
00:57:31,616 --> 00:57:33,428
The lightning feels staged.

1561
00:57:33,595 --> 00:57:36,253
My goodness. All of a sudden...

1562
00:57:36,295 --> 00:57:38,867
Won Ji, I...

1563
00:57:38,892 --> 00:57:41,182
Lightning struck behind you.

1564
00:57:41,525 --> 00:57:43,760
I'm not scared of ghosts.

1565
00:57:44,461 --> 00:57:46,964
Ghosts, you die.

1566
00:57:47,746 --> 00:57:49,520
(Threatening ghosts that are already dead)

1567
00:57:49,686 --> 00:57:52,166
- Ghosts!
- Ghosts, come on!

1568
00:57:52,167 --> 00:57:53,507
- Ghosts!
- Ghosts!

1569
00:57:54,181 --> 00:57:56,767
- Come on, ghosts!
- I'm not scared.

1570
00:57:56,768 --> 00:58:00,510
She's doing that
because she's not the leader, right?

1571
00:58:00,687 --> 00:58:01,812
Why did I volunteer?

1572
00:58:02,020 --> 00:58:05,623
(Lightning flashes.)

1573
00:58:07,318 --> 00:58:10,598
(Using the lightning as a light source)

1574
00:58:12,078 --> 00:58:15,144
(At the start of a horror movie,
everyone is excited.)

1575
00:58:15,145 --> 00:58:16,444
It's so funny.

1576
00:58:16,445 --> 00:58:18,445
Harimu, you might be good
at fighting off ghosts.

1577
00:58:18,446 --> 00:58:19,820
Start!

1578
00:58:19,840 --> 00:58:22,733
- Ghosts, come on!
- Ghosts, come on!

1579
00:58:22,734 --> 00:58:23,633
(Cheering)

1580
00:58:24,200 --> 00:58:25,002
Ghosts!

1581
00:58:25,420 --> 00:58:26,403
I...

1582
00:58:26,527 --> 00:58:28,772
I'm getting used to it.

1583
00:58:28,847 --> 00:58:30,674
- I find it fun. It's becoming part of me.
- We can do it!

1584
00:58:30,675 --> 00:58:32,609
Sian! You can do this!

1585
00:58:32,610 --> 00:58:34,311
- You volunteered!
- Right.

1586
00:58:34,385 --> 00:58:36,513
Ghosts might feel drained and run away.

1587
00:58:36,675 --> 00:58:39,216
Ghosts, you're out!

1588
00:58:39,716 --> 00:58:41,885
You're boring.

1589
00:58:42,001 --> 00:58:43,053
Seriously.

1590
00:58:44,867 --> 00:58:45,689
You suck.

1591
00:58:46,490 --> 00:58:48,058
- Suck?
- You really suck.

1592
00:58:49,007 --> 00:58:50,027
You're stinky.

1593
00:58:50,028 --> 00:58:51,288
(You hurt the ghosts' feelings.)

1594
00:58:51,681 --> 00:58:54,034
(Meanwhile)

1595
00:58:56,001 --> 00:58:57,908
(The abandoned theater got even darker.)

1596
00:58:57,909 --> 00:58:59,015
- Let's get going.
- Let's go.

1597
00:58:59,016 --> 00:59:00,295
- Can you do this?
- I can.

1598
00:59:00,296 --> 00:59:01,972
- We can do this.
- Just trust me!

1599
00:59:01,973 --> 00:59:05,509
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1600
00:59:06,476 --> 00:59:07,978
We'll catch ghosts!

1601
00:59:07,979 --> 00:59:09,979
- Link arms.
- Okay!

1602
00:59:10,059 --> 00:59:13,429
- Isn't it really creepy, though?
- It is.

1603
00:59:13,430 --> 00:59:15,059
It has a really bad vibe.

1604
00:59:15,060 --> 00:59:16,753
Why do they leave a place like this?

1605
00:59:17,219 --> 00:59:19,331
Why didn't they remodel the place?

1606
00:59:19,332 --> 00:59:20,357
Remodel the place?

1607
00:59:20,651 --> 00:59:22,559
Now that we're closer...

1608
00:59:22,598 --> 00:59:24,327
I can't. I don't want to.

1609
00:59:24,458 --> 00:59:25,818
The door is tightly shut.

1610
00:59:25,819 --> 00:59:26,963
It's so scary.

1611
00:59:26,964 --> 00:59:28,065
I got goosebumps.

1612
00:59:28,398 --> 00:59:29,566
Did you feel that?

1613
00:59:30,534 --> 00:59:31,802
Wait. What is that?

1614
00:59:32,098 --> 00:59:33,570
- What?
- Isn't that a suitcase?

1615
00:59:33,823 --> 00:59:34,804
Where's our suitcase?

1616
00:59:34,805 --> 00:59:35,972
I don't know!

1617
00:59:35,973 --> 00:59:37,307
I feel like there's something up there.

1618
00:59:37,308 --> 00:59:38,799
That yellow thing over there.

1619
00:59:38,800 --> 00:59:40,077
- I don't see it.
- Isn't that a suitcase?

1620
00:59:40,377 --> 00:59:41,572
- On our right.
- It is.

1621
00:59:41,573 --> 00:59:42,913
It doesn't have a sticker on it.

1622
00:59:42,914 --> 00:59:45,082
- I see it now.
- It scared me!

1623
00:59:45,083 --> 00:59:46,138
(That suitcase looks scarier here.)

1624
00:59:46,193 --> 00:59:49,252
- It looks so scary.
- My gosh! What do I do?

1625
00:59:49,853 --> 00:59:51,021
I'm so scared.

1626
00:59:51,146 --> 00:59:52,531
I'm sorry. I can't.

1627
00:59:52,558 --> 00:59:53,878
- Over there.
- There's nothing there.

1628
00:59:53,879 --> 00:59:56,059
What was that just now? A bird flew by.

1629
00:59:56,060 --> 00:59:57,427
It's okay.

1630
00:59:57,573 --> 00:59:58,835
- I see the suitcase.
- I've had it.

1631
00:59:59,573 --> 01:00:01,693
- Good idea. Grab some weapon.
- Yes.

1632
01:00:02,365 --> 01:00:04,766
But the sticker isn't on it.

1633
01:00:05,035 --> 01:00:06,836
Maybe it's a new suitcase?

1634
01:00:06,970 --> 01:00:08,971
Maybe it's not our original one.

1635
01:00:09,473 --> 01:00:11,641
Oh, no. I really don't want to go.

1636
01:00:11,975 --> 01:00:13,375
Do we have to go in here?

1637
01:00:13,376 --> 01:00:14,243
(Pitch-black darkness)

1638
01:00:14,244 --> 01:00:15,577
Who's there?

1639
01:00:15,846 --> 01:00:17,747
This is terrifying.

1640
01:00:18,648 --> 01:00:19,582
Terrifying.

1641
01:00:19,583 --> 01:00:21,617
No, I don't want to do this.

1642
01:00:21,885 --> 01:00:24,353
This is actually my first time.

1643
01:00:24,607 --> 01:00:26,107
Let's open the suitcase.

1644
01:00:26,823 --> 01:00:28,758
I think something's inside.

1645
01:00:28,759 --> 01:00:30,059
I don't think this is ours.

1646
01:00:30,060 --> 01:00:30,893
Yes.

1647
01:00:30,961 --> 01:00:32,437
Is this the reward
they were talking about?

1648
01:00:32,462 --> 01:00:33,596
Something before we go back?

1649
01:00:34,264 --> 01:00:35,998
I think we need to equip this.

1650
01:00:36,266 --> 01:00:37,066
What is it?

1651
01:00:38,035 --> 01:00:40,703
I think they want us to wear this
and film ourselves.

1652
01:00:41,038 --> 01:00:42,004
What?

1653
01:00:42,005 --> 01:00:42,938
(There's no one around but them.)

1654
01:00:42,939 --> 01:00:45,174
I don't like this!

1655
01:00:45,175 --> 01:00:46,676
Was that thunder and lightning?

1656
01:00:47,177 --> 01:00:48,445
What's over there?

1657
01:00:48,779 --> 01:00:50,647
This can't be real.
I'm going to wet myself.

1658
01:00:50,847 --> 01:00:52,281
There's nothing here.

1659
01:00:52,282 --> 01:00:54,149
- What's this?
- What's that?

1660
01:00:54,251 --> 01:00:55,518
I know what this is.

1661
01:00:55,519 --> 01:00:56,385
A noise meter?

1662
01:00:56,386 --> 01:00:58,788
It's a ghost detector.

1663
01:00:58,789 --> 01:01:01,190
If a ghost is nearby, it'll start moving.

1664
01:01:01,191 --> 01:01:01,991
Really?

1665
01:01:01,992 --> 01:01:04,036
- They have some kind of frequency.
- Wait, what's this?

1666
01:01:04,061 --> 01:01:06,063
What's this? Look.

1667
01:01:06,064 --> 01:01:06,963
What is that?

1668
01:01:08,198 --> 01:01:10,032
- What is it?
- I think we have to go somewhere.

1669
01:01:10,033 --> 01:01:11,367
I think we have to go watch a movie.

1670
01:01:11,368 --> 01:01:12,301
(A movie ticket dated today)

1671
01:01:13,570 --> 01:01:15,304
Abra-ca-Empty?

1672
01:01:17,174 --> 01:01:18,908
<i>Abracadabra</i>

1673
01:01:19,309 --> 01:01:20,676
Stop! Don't!

1674
01:01:20,677 --> 01:01:22,087
(Just a camera)

1675
01:01:22,112 --> 01:01:23,312
Stop that!

1676
01:01:23,313 --> 01:01:24,113
Don't.

1677
01:01:24,915 --> 01:01:25,882
(Harimu hits the deck mid-song)

1678
01:01:25,883 --> 01:01:26,616
Stop.

1679
01:01:27,043 --> 01:01:28,744
Twerk! Twerk!

1680
01:01:29,419 --> 01:01:32,388
(Might as well twerk)

1681
01:01:32,924 --> 01:01:34,590
That was so scary.

1682
01:01:34,969 --> 01:01:36,358
I almost had a heart attack.

1683
01:01:36,359 --> 01:01:37,359
There's this too.

1684
01:01:38,261 --> 01:01:39,027
A flashlight.

1685
01:01:39,028 --> 01:01:41,630
Four headlamps and one flashlight.

1686
01:01:41,631 --> 01:01:43,599
The person in the front can hold this.

1687
01:01:44,301 --> 01:01:45,703
(A must-have for the person in front)

1688
01:01:45,704 --> 01:01:47,770
I hate it!

1689
01:01:48,405 --> 01:01:49,339
(Silence)

1690
01:01:49,340 --> 01:01:51,073
Abracadabra!

1691
01:01:53,243 --> 01:01:54,743
- Okay.
- Let me go.

1692
01:01:55,145 --> 01:01:55,978
Come on.

1693
01:01:56,379 --> 01:01:58,046
We have to rely on each other.

1694
01:01:58,047 --> 01:01:59,683
This is what you call a girls' night.

1695
01:02:00,117 --> 01:02:01,451
I'll grab your shoulder from behind.

1696
01:02:01,452 --> 01:02:03,352
- Okay.
- I hope nothing grabs my ankles.

1697
01:02:03,353 --> 01:02:04,487
Can you just stick with me?

1698
01:02:04,488 --> 01:02:05,422
- Stick to you?
- Yes.

1699
01:02:05,423 --> 01:02:06,289
Hold me.

1700
01:02:06,423 --> 01:02:07,424
- Hold you?
- Yes.

1701
01:02:07,449 --> 01:02:08,325
That's cute.

1702
01:02:08,925 --> 01:02:09,725
I'm going in.

1703
01:02:09,726 --> 01:02:10,692
(Agh!)

1704
01:02:10,693 --> 01:02:12,294
Hold this and let's go.

1705
01:02:12,295 --> 01:02:13,495
- I'll hold it.
- You hold it.

1706
01:02:13,496 --> 01:02:14,363
I'll hold this...

1707
01:02:14,364 --> 01:02:16,031
- and grab you.
- If we don't make it out in 30 minutes,

1708
01:02:16,032 --> 01:02:17,032
- please save us!
- I can't keep up.

1709
01:02:17,033 --> 01:02:17,933
Someone has to hold you.

1710
01:02:17,934 --> 01:02:19,268
- Shall we?
- Okay.

1711
01:02:19,269 --> 01:02:20,002
Let's go.

1712
01:02:20,203 --> 01:02:22,037
- It's okay.
- It's okay, girls.

1713
01:02:22,038 --> 01:02:23,539
- This is nothing.
- It's going to be fine.

1714
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:24,740
- It's nothing.
- Okay.

1715
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:27,109
Do we go left or right?

1716
01:02:27,110 --> 01:02:28,212
Let's see. Left or right.

1717
01:02:28,213 --> 01:02:30,079
Do we have to go up the stairs?

1718
01:02:30,914 --> 01:02:32,014
It should be left, right?

1719
01:02:32,015 --> 01:02:33,048
(First, a quick peek to the left)

1720
01:02:33,049 --> 01:02:33,849
Here we go.

1721
01:02:35,385 --> 01:02:37,653
- Huh?
- This is so wrong.

1722
01:02:37,654 --> 01:02:39,521
(A dark and humid corridor)

1723
01:02:40,357 --> 01:02:41,257
What the hell?

1724
01:02:41,658 --> 01:02:42,524
Oh, come on.

1725
01:02:42,525 --> 01:02:43,394
(Slowly moving forward)

1726
01:02:43,395 --> 01:02:45,194
- Please.
- The windows are all broken.

1727
01:02:45,195 --> 01:02:48,797
I think they were praying here.

1728
01:02:48,798 --> 01:02:50,400
Please don't jump scare us.

1729
01:02:50,401 --> 01:02:51,233
I'm begging you.

1730
01:02:51,234 --> 01:02:53,902
Watch your step.

1731
01:02:54,137 --> 01:02:55,604
We can do this.

1732
01:02:55,605 --> 01:02:57,239
I really hate this.

1733
01:02:57,607 --> 01:02:59,108
Please... Twerk.

1734
01:02:59,576 --> 01:03:00,342
Twerk.

1735
01:03:00,343 --> 01:03:01,510
(I twerk when I'm scared.)

1736
01:03:01,511 --> 01:03:02,211
Wait. We're good.

1737
01:03:02,212 --> 01:03:03,880
- Can you please grab me here?
- Sure.

1738
01:03:05,715 --> 01:03:06,682
(The biggest scaredy-cat takes the lead.)

1739
01:03:06,683 --> 01:03:07,616
This is crazy.

1740
01:03:07,617 --> 01:03:08,684
It won't be dangerous.

1741
01:03:09,487 --> 01:03:13,055
It says to keep out.
Are we going in there?

1742
01:03:13,290 --> 01:03:14,523
Do we go over this?

1743
01:03:14,524 --> 01:03:16,459
(Dead end)

1744
01:03:16,460 --> 01:03:17,560
I don't think this is it.

1745
01:03:17,561 --> 01:03:20,029
- It's not?
- Something's closed over here.

1746
01:03:20,597 --> 01:03:22,231
Wow, I can't see anything up ahead.

1747
01:03:22,232 --> 01:03:24,166
This flashlight isn't that great.

1748
01:03:24,167 --> 01:03:25,034
(Can't see anything behind them)

1749
01:03:25,035 --> 01:03:25,968
Seriously?

1750
01:03:26,236 --> 01:03:27,970
- Oh, crap.
- This is really scary.

1751
01:03:27,971 --> 01:03:28,904
It's okay.

1752
01:03:29,239 --> 01:03:30,272
Be careful.

1753
01:03:30,473 --> 01:03:31,340
Please be careful.

1754
01:03:31,341 --> 01:03:33,008
Watch your step.

1755
01:03:33,677 --> 01:03:35,111
Look at the shattered glass.

1756
01:03:35,779 --> 01:03:37,480
- Who broke it?
- We're in trouble.

1757
01:03:37,481 --> 01:03:40,049
(Shattered mirror)

1758
01:03:40,483 --> 01:03:41,583
(Pause)

1759
01:03:41,584 --> 01:03:42,417
Oh, my.

1760
01:03:42,686 --> 01:03:44,053
- Wow.
- Is that a haechi?

1761
01:03:44,921 --> 01:03:45,721
What is that?

1762
01:03:47,157 --> 01:03:48,023
It's a toad.

1763
01:03:48,024 --> 01:03:49,492
(Who broke that?)

1764
01:03:49,493 --> 01:03:51,460
This is crazy. You must be joking.

1765
01:03:51,561 --> 01:03:52,729
Wow.

1766
01:03:53,396 --> 01:03:55,330
(Too scared to go in, just peeking)

1767
01:03:55,331 --> 01:03:56,198
This place is...

1768
01:03:56,633 --> 01:03:58,434
- Where do we go?
- What do we do?

1769
01:03:59,102 --> 01:04:01,003
We need some signs at least.

1770
01:04:01,004 --> 01:04:02,137
(Complete darkness)

1771
01:04:02,138 --> 01:04:03,606
- Why is this place so big?
- I think it's this way.

1772
01:04:03,607 --> 01:04:04,940
- Left?
- Let me head this way.

1773
01:04:04,941 --> 01:04:07,076
- I don't think it's upstairs.
- We can't go up the stairs.

1774
01:04:07,077 --> 01:04:10,479
(Heading to the big space on the left)

1775
01:04:11,014 --> 01:04:12,381
It's okay.

1776
01:04:12,850 --> 01:04:14,684
- Stay calm.
- We have four people.

1777
01:04:15,019 --> 01:04:16,118
Wow, it's here.

1778
01:04:16,386 --> 01:04:18,654
This is the place we saw in the photo.

1779
01:04:19,155 --> 01:04:21,523
This is it. That escalator is here.

1780
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:23,692
The place we saw in the photo.

1781
01:04:23,693 --> 01:04:24,493
(The escalator they saw in the QR code)

1782
01:04:24,661 --> 01:04:26,462
(Singing)

1783
01:04:26,764 --> 01:04:27,963
What is it?

1784
01:04:29,132 --> 01:04:30,199
It's nothing.

1785
01:04:30,200 --> 01:04:31,233
Don't do that.

1786
01:04:31,234 --> 01:04:32,134
(It's just the staff.)

1787
01:04:32,301 --> 01:04:34,003
We are looking for our reward.

1788
01:04:34,004 --> 01:04:36,405
We came a long way.

1789
01:04:36,406 --> 01:04:37,372
(Forcing each step,
thinking about the reward)

1790
01:04:37,373 --> 01:04:38,740
Don't do that.

1791
01:04:38,976 --> 01:04:40,743
I'm pretty sure we have to go up.

1792
01:04:40,744 --> 01:04:41,677
We go up?

1793
01:04:41,944 --> 01:04:42,945
I think this is it.

1794
01:04:42,946 --> 01:04:45,480
Yes, this is what we saw in the photo.

1795
01:04:46,683 --> 01:04:47,784
Do we have to go up?

1796
01:04:49,986 --> 01:04:51,853
- We have...
- Are you sure this isn't going to break?

1797
01:04:51,854 --> 01:04:52,654
no choice.

1798
01:04:52,857 --> 01:04:55,190
Wow, look at all that dust.

1799
01:04:55,792 --> 01:04:56,926
Are you sure we can go up?

1800
01:04:56,927 --> 01:04:58,627
I'm so scared.

1801
01:04:58,628 --> 01:04:59,963
(It looks like it's never been used.)

1802
01:04:59,964 --> 01:05:01,830
Did someone send the dragon of fear?

1803
01:05:01,831 --> 01:05:03,665
Who sent us the dragon of fear?

1804
01:05:04,601 --> 01:05:06,236
- Hold on!
- What is it?

1805
01:05:06,237 --> 01:05:07,469
- Why?
- What is fear?

1806
01:05:07,570 --> 01:05:08,937
Fear...

1807
01:05:09,306 --> 01:05:10,140
is an illusion.

1808
01:05:10,608 --> 01:05:11,941
Fear is an illusion!

1809
01:05:12,208 --> 01:05:13,975
- Fear is an illusion!
- Fear is an illusion!

1810
01:05:13,976 --> 01:05:15,777
(Dropping quotes to hide the fear)

1811
01:05:15,912 --> 01:05:17,613
It's all in my head!

1812
01:05:17,614 --> 01:05:19,748
- True.
- It's all in my head!

1813
01:05:19,749 --> 01:05:21,250
- It's just the dark.
- That's right.

1814
01:05:21,251 --> 01:05:23,418
We sleep in the dark.

1815
01:05:23,419 --> 01:05:24,319
- Oh, yes.
- Right?

1816
01:05:24,956 --> 01:05:26,088
Every day...

1817
01:05:26,456 --> 01:05:27,756
we have at least 8 hours of darkness.

1818
01:05:27,757 --> 01:05:28,824
- Yes.
- Let's go.

1819
01:05:28,825 --> 01:05:30,225
Pass me the flashlight.

1820
01:05:30,226 --> 01:05:31,361
Flashlight for the lead.

1821
01:05:31,628 --> 01:05:33,629
Let's go.

1822
01:05:33,630 --> 01:05:35,664
- Wow, there are dead feathers.
- Wow, look.

1823
01:05:35,832 --> 01:05:37,834
There are spiderwebs here.

1824
01:05:38,435 --> 01:05:40,103
- There are feathers everywhere.
- Wow, spiderwebs.

1825
01:05:41,204 --> 01:05:41,903
(Jingle)

1826
01:05:41,904 --> 01:05:43,438
What was that? Did you hear that?

1827
01:05:43,439 --> 01:05:44,739
I heard a jingling sound from above.

1828
01:05:44,740 --> 01:05:46,509
You heard that, right?
It sounded like a toad.

1829
01:05:46,810 --> 01:05:48,511
Like yesterday?

1830
01:05:48,512 --> 01:05:49,678
We heard toads yesterday.

1831
01:05:49,679 --> 01:05:51,680
- Yes.
- Watch your step.

1832
01:05:52,082 --> 01:05:54,717
Let's try not to freak out on the stairs.

1833
01:05:55,185 --> 01:05:56,952
- Yes.
- If we jump here, it's going to be bad.

1834
01:05:56,953 --> 01:05:58,053
(Jingle)

1835
01:05:58,054 --> 01:05:58,887
It's very...

1836
01:05:58,888 --> 01:06:00,989
- I knew it. It was a jingle!
- You're right.

1837
01:06:00,990 --> 01:06:02,491
- I heard it too.
- Yes.

1838
01:06:02,492 --> 01:06:04,560
- It jingled.
- But we're on the stairs!

1839
01:06:06,096 --> 01:06:07,830
Wasn't this supposed to be
a suitcase trip?

1840
01:06:08,733 --> 01:06:10,442
I know, right?
What do they think they're doing?

1841
01:06:10,467 --> 01:06:11,901
Why are there so many feathers?

1842
01:06:12,469 --> 01:06:13,668
Agh!

1843
01:06:13,669 --> 01:06:14,403
What?

1844
01:06:14,404 --> 01:06:16,439
We're still on the stairs!

1845
01:06:16,440 --> 01:06:17,606
The stairs!

1846
01:06:18,041 --> 01:06:20,175
A bird!

1847
01:06:20,643 --> 01:06:21,676
We made it!

1848
01:06:21,677 --> 01:06:23,278
- We came a long way.
- That's right.

1849
01:06:23,279 --> 01:06:24,079
- Totally.
- Totally.

1850
01:06:24,080 --> 01:06:25,647
But where's the reward?

1851
01:06:25,648 --> 01:06:27,248
What's that?

1852
01:06:27,249 --> 01:06:29,985
(Multiple doors with mirrors on them)

1853
01:06:30,186 --> 01:06:31,052
Let's go find out.

1854
01:06:31,053 --> 01:06:31,787
(Scouting the place)

1855
01:06:31,788 --> 01:06:33,756
- I think this will break if I step on it.
- This is crazy.

1856
01:06:34,457 --> 01:06:36,158
This is insane.

1857
01:06:36,460 --> 01:06:38,227
My underwear is soaked with sweat.

1858
01:06:38,461 --> 01:06:39,696
This really is insane.

1859
01:06:39,963 --> 01:06:41,130
Unbelievable.

1860
01:06:41,155 --> 01:06:42,484
(An insane situation)

1861
01:06:42,532 --> 01:06:44,833
- Where do we go now?
- This is beyond scary.

1862
01:06:44,834 --> 01:06:46,668
I think...

1863
01:06:47,170 --> 01:06:49,204
Shouldn't we use this ticket?

1864
01:06:49,205 --> 01:06:51,073
That's exactly what I was going to say.

1865
01:06:51,074 --> 01:06:52,774
I get it. Let's look for a box office.

1866
01:06:52,976 --> 01:06:53,776
I get it now.

1867
01:06:53,777 --> 01:06:55,244
Is the box office normally upstairs?

1868
01:06:57,947 --> 01:07:01,149
(Chaos)

1869
01:07:01,150 --> 01:07:03,118
Oh, come on!

1870
01:07:03,486 --> 01:07:04,586
What was it?

1871
01:07:04,587 --> 01:07:06,122
(Sian gets startled by the camera again.)

1872
01:07:06,123 --> 01:07:07,355
- Where's the theater?
- Hold on.

1873
01:07:07,490 --> 01:07:08,657
Hold on a second.

1874
01:07:08,658 --> 01:07:10,592
There was nothing there, right?

1875
01:07:10,593 --> 01:07:12,561
Please don't scream.

1876
01:07:12,562 --> 01:07:13,963
- My nose is sweating.
- I'm so scared.

1877
01:07:14,657 --> 01:07:16,658
I'm dripping in sweat.

1878
01:07:17,367 --> 01:07:19,635
Okay. Let's go again.

1879
01:07:19,903 --> 01:07:21,271
There was nothing there.

1880
01:07:21,604 --> 01:07:22,437
(Hands held tight)

1881
01:07:22,438 --> 01:07:23,738
- Calm down.
- Don't cry.

1882
01:07:23,739 --> 01:07:24,973
- There's nothing there.
- Don't cry.

1883
01:07:25,308 --> 01:07:28,010
- I think we have to go into the theater.
- No way.

1884
01:07:28,344 --> 01:07:31,279
No jump scares, please.

1885
01:07:31,414 --> 01:07:33,615
- You're the scariest right now.
- No one did anything.

1886
01:07:33,616 --> 01:07:35,351
You're our biggest fear, Sian.

1887
01:07:35,352 --> 01:07:36,618
It's true, Sian.

1888
01:07:36,619 --> 01:07:37,720
I'm so overwhelmed.

1889
01:07:37,721 --> 01:07:39,355
No one jump-scared us.

1890
01:07:42,592 --> 01:07:43,759
(Jingle)

1891
01:07:44,260 --> 01:07:45,794
You must be freaking kidding me.

1892
01:07:47,163 --> 01:07:49,932
(It's so scary a curse word slipped out.)

1893
01:07:49,933 --> 01:07:51,266
Do we have to go there?

1894
01:07:51,267 --> 01:07:52,901
(Where the jingle came from)

1895
01:07:52,902 --> 01:07:54,504
Do we have to follow the jingle?

1896
01:07:54,972 --> 01:07:55,972
- It came from there.
- I think so.

1897
01:07:55,973 --> 01:07:58,273
I think we'll have to go toward the sound.

1898
01:07:59,008 --> 01:07:59,774
Dang it!

1899
01:07:59,775 --> 01:08:00,942
(Jingle)

1900
01:08:00,943 --> 01:08:02,010
Stay back!

1901
01:08:03,046 --> 01:08:05,180
- Oh, come on!
- Wait.

1902
01:08:05,582 --> 01:08:07,850
(The fact is, no one went near them.)

1903
01:08:07,851 --> 01:08:08,817
Is there something there?

1904
01:08:09,452 --> 01:08:10,886
Look over there.

1905
01:08:10,887 --> 01:08:11,887
(They found the door
where the jingle came from.)

1906
01:08:11,888 --> 01:08:13,221
- Let's go over there.
- Why is it so close?

1907
01:08:13,222 --> 01:08:14,490
I'm pretty sure it's that room.

1908
01:08:14,958 --> 01:08:15,958
You're lying.

1909
01:08:15,959 --> 01:08:17,559
- I'm sweating.
- We have to go in there?

1910
01:08:17,560 --> 01:08:18,928
Seriously?

1911
01:08:19,329 --> 01:08:20,629
We have to cross that river?

1912
01:08:21,464 --> 01:08:24,466
(Crossing the hall to find the reward)

1913
01:08:25,101 --> 01:08:26,669
My feet are sweating.

1914
01:08:26,670 --> 01:08:29,171
- This is insane.
- It's crazy.

1915
01:08:29,472 --> 01:08:31,973
I don't think I can go in there.
I'm serious.

1916
01:08:31,974 --> 01:08:32,841
(Come in.)

1917
01:08:33,943 --> 01:08:35,277
(Turn)

1918
01:08:35,378 --> 01:08:36,946
(Glancing)

1919
01:08:36,947 --> 01:08:37,946
Crap.

1920
01:08:38,615 --> 01:08:41,216
I'm sweating like crazy.

1921
01:08:41,217 --> 01:08:43,052
Let's just use the flashlight
at the entrance.

1922
01:08:43,053 --> 01:08:44,020
(One step closer to the door)

1923
01:08:44,021 --> 01:08:44,887
Let's test the water.

1924
01:08:45,088 --> 01:08:46,021
- Come here.
- Dear God.

1925
01:08:46,022 --> 01:08:47,622
There's something written here.

1926
01:08:47,647 --> 01:08:49,415
It's not for us,

1927
01:08:50,093 --> 01:08:51,694
is it?

1928
01:08:51,695 --> 01:08:52,528
I'm sure it's not.

1929
01:08:52,529 --> 01:08:53,763
(Suspicious red writing)

1930
01:08:54,931 --> 01:08:56,598
The sound is coming from there.

1931
01:08:57,634 --> 01:08:59,668
And it's pissing me off.

1932
01:09:00,036 --> 01:09:01,070
It's so annoying.

1933
01:09:01,203 --> 01:09:03,039
Wait. Where do we head from here?

1934
01:09:03,064 --> 01:09:04,039
- So scary.
- Left?

1935
01:09:05,041 --> 01:09:06,541
What are we looking for?

1936
01:09:07,277 --> 01:09:09,077
- Let's just go in!
- My legs won't move.

1937
01:09:09,078 --> 01:09:09,811
Okay.

1938
01:09:10,680 --> 01:09:11,948
This place is crazy.

1939
01:09:12,382 --> 01:09:14,083
I've never seen anything like this.

1940
01:09:14,984 --> 01:09:15,817
(A pitch-black hallway)

1941
01:09:15,818 --> 01:09:17,353
It's going to jingle again soon.

1942
01:09:17,520 --> 01:09:18,655
Come here and hold my hand.

1943
01:09:18,821 --> 01:09:20,088
I'll hold your hand.

1944
01:09:20,290 --> 01:09:21,490
Yes, hold my hand.

1945
01:09:22,125 --> 01:09:22,891
Perfect.

1946
01:09:23,626 --> 01:09:25,160
It's so scary.

1947
01:09:25,628 --> 01:09:27,062
- There's nothing over here.
- Is this it?

1948
01:09:27,063 --> 01:09:28,997
- Wait. I'm so scared.
- Shh.

1949
01:09:28,998 --> 01:09:29,864
(Pause)

1950
01:09:29,865 --> 01:09:30,966
It's over there.

1951
01:09:32,468 --> 01:09:33,568
There.

1952
01:09:33,670 --> 01:09:34,937
(Where the jingle is coming from)

1953
01:09:34,938 --> 01:09:37,373
- It's open here.
- Why do I even have to do this?

1954
01:09:37,374 --> 01:09:38,440
I know, right?

1955
01:09:40,810 --> 01:09:42,043
- You hear that, right?
- Yes.

1956
01:09:44,614 --> 01:09:46,615
- I can hear the jingle.
- It's getting louder.

1957
01:09:46,616 --> 01:09:47,583
(Getting louder as they approach)

1958
01:09:47,884 --> 01:09:49,985
- I'm way too scared.
- There's nothing on the right.

1959
01:09:49,986 --> 01:09:52,198
- Nothing on the right or left, right?
- What's in front?

1960
01:09:52,223 --> 01:09:53,756
It's a theater.

1961
01:09:53,757 --> 01:09:54,857
Oh, the stairs go down.

1962
01:09:54,858 --> 01:09:56,375
Unbelievable.

1963
01:09:56,400 --> 01:09:59,194
What on earth is this?

1964
01:09:59,195 --> 01:10:00,129
It's complete darkness.

1965
01:10:00,619 --> 01:10:02,063
It's pitch black.

1966
01:10:02,725 --> 01:10:04,901
I'm usually terrified
of looking under chairs.

1967
01:10:05,190 --> 01:10:06,069
Seriously.

1968
01:10:07,303 --> 01:10:09,083
- Her accent is slipping out.
- Seriously.

1969
01:10:09,230 --> 01:10:10,673
I'm not kidding.

1970
01:10:10,756 --> 01:10:12,208
Don't do it.

1971
01:10:12,209 --> 01:10:14,711
- I'm dying of heat.
- Don't grab my ankle or anything.

1972
01:10:14,712 --> 01:10:17,113
I'm going to get mad. I'm going home.

1973
01:10:17,114 --> 01:10:19,449
I'm a travel YouTuber.
I'll straight-up buy a ticket and leave.

1974
01:10:19,558 --> 01:10:20,583
Just a little bit.

1975
01:10:22,018 --> 01:10:24,320
At least the sides look okay.
There's nothing there.

1976
01:10:24,721 --> 01:10:26,389
Nothing's going to fall from above, right?

1977
01:10:26,904 --> 01:10:30,291
(How did she know?)

1978
01:10:30,577 --> 01:10:32,431
(Terrified)

1979
01:10:33,464 --> 01:10:36,762
(The sisters immediately bolt.)

1980
01:10:37,175 --> 01:10:39,235
(Gabee turns around
and bursts out laughing.)

1981
01:10:40,255 --> 01:10:45,182
(Harimu freezes in place like a scorpion.)

1982
01:10:45,835 --> 01:10:49,586
(One by one, they return
to check on the scorpion.)

1983
01:10:50,440 --> 01:10:53,916
(They belatedly reach out to pet her.)

1984
01:10:54,174 --> 01:10:56,440
(Sweat glands back in overdrive)

1985
01:10:56,560 --> 01:10:58,054
- I'm scared.
- I'm sweating.

1986
01:10:58,055 --> 01:10:59,222
Look at all this sweat.

1987
01:10:59,455 --> 01:11:01,648
I guess it was just a wig.

1988
01:11:02,115 --> 01:11:03,960
Where did it come from?

1989
01:11:03,961 --> 01:11:06,062
I think there are seats upstairs too.

1990
01:11:06,821 --> 01:11:08,199
We totally overreacted.

1991
01:11:08,698 --> 01:11:10,959
- That was it?
- Yes.

1992
01:11:10,960 --> 01:11:12,774
- Let's put it on and keep moving.
- Okay.

1993
01:11:12,914 --> 01:11:14,640
Look at her. She's drenched in sweat.

1994
01:11:14,641 --> 01:11:16,600
(Putting on the wig
with pure determination)

1995
01:11:16,601 --> 01:11:18,048
I think you can pull this off.

1996
01:11:18,049 --> 01:11:19,876
(After one big jump scare,
she's dark and fearless.)

1997
01:11:20,034 --> 01:11:21,468
You're amazing.

1998
01:11:22,701 --> 01:11:25,448
- Did someone throw it?
- I don't know. It just fell.

1999
01:11:25,473 --> 01:11:26,315
(Heading back inside)

2000
01:11:27,049 --> 01:11:28,751
Don't do it.

2001
01:11:29,081 --> 01:11:31,254
- Seriously, don't.
- I said don't do it.

2002
01:11:31,356 --> 01:11:32,288
Please don't.

2003
01:11:32,722 --> 01:11:33,756
Don't do it.

2004
01:11:33,803 --> 01:11:35,691
Is there something in here?

2005
01:11:37,493 --> 01:11:40,603
How old are these chairs, anyway?

2006
01:11:42,161 --> 01:11:44,000
I'm actually fine with creepy things.

2007
01:11:44,001 --> 01:11:46,265
- It's being startled that I hate.
- I know. Just...

2008
01:11:46,290 --> 01:11:47,039
(Bump)

2009
01:11:47,064 --> 01:11:49,505
I just hate jump scares.

2010
01:11:49,897 --> 01:11:50,972
I'm not scared at all.

2011
01:11:50,973 --> 01:11:52,525
(The camera accidentally bumps into them.)

2012
01:11:52,550 --> 01:11:54,043
I don't like horror movies.

2013
01:11:54,111 --> 01:11:56,412
- I guess we should go downstairs, right?
- Okay.

2014
01:11:56,437 --> 01:11:58,835
(Clinging tightly
to each other's hands again)

2015
01:11:58,860 --> 01:12:01,684
- Why are there so many chairs?
- I know, right?

2016
01:12:02,051 --> 01:12:04,534
- This place must be huge.
- It had to be a massive theater.

2017
01:12:04,535 --> 01:12:06,455
Looks like it could seat 300 people.

2018
01:12:06,960 --> 01:12:08,057
Hold on.

2019
01:12:08,140 --> 01:12:10,693
- Why are there so many chairs?
- Wait.

2020
01:12:11,227 --> 01:12:14,564
Doesn't that look
like something black over there?

2021
01:12:17,266 --> 01:12:19,969
- Looks like only that spot is black.
- I think so too.

2022
01:12:20,006 --> 01:12:21,103
There's something over there.

2023
01:12:22,393 --> 01:12:24,707
- Is that the lucky item?
- Are my eyes playing tricks on me?

2024
01:12:24,708 --> 01:12:26,609
No, you're right. There's something black.

2025
01:12:26,740 --> 01:12:28,077
Let's do it this way.

2026
01:12:28,102 --> 01:12:31,089
(Checking both sides row by row
as they advance)

2027
01:12:31,114 --> 01:12:32,815
Next, row 2.

2028
01:12:33,088 --> 01:12:34,962
Row 2 is clear.

2029
01:12:34,987 --> 01:12:35,714
Okay.

2030
01:12:36,052 --> 01:12:38,354
- Row 3.
- Row 3 is clear, right?

2031
01:12:39,184 --> 01:12:41,591
- We got this.
- I'm sweating bullets.

2032
01:12:41,592 --> 01:12:44,464
(Slowly making their way down)

2033
01:12:44,644 --> 01:12:46,229
I don't think that's a person.

2034
01:12:46,704 --> 01:12:48,497
Then what is it?

2035
01:12:48,898 --> 01:12:50,099
That's...

2036
01:12:51,149 --> 01:12:52,802
- Your voice...
- Are you okay?

2037
01:12:54,570 --> 01:12:57,473
It looks like someone
hanging their head down.

2038
01:12:59,162 --> 01:13:00,776
I really can't go any further.

2039
01:13:01,707 --> 01:13:04,647
Inching closer row by row
makes it even creepier.

2040
01:13:05,214 --> 01:13:06,282
- I'll go.
- Okay.

2041
01:13:06,453 --> 01:13:07,450
I'm going.

2042
01:13:07,817 --> 01:13:09,685
That hair is really long.

2043
01:13:09,893 --> 01:13:11,053
It's just a wig.

2044
01:13:13,356 --> 01:13:14,423
It doesn't have a body.

2045
01:13:14,424 --> 01:13:16,459
If that weren't a wig,
I would've passed out.

2046
01:13:16,960 --> 01:13:18,327
We fell for it.

2047
01:13:19,262 --> 01:13:21,262
But I think we need to go over there.

2048
01:13:21,263 --> 01:13:22,665
- Near that head?
- Yes.

2049
01:13:23,169 --> 01:13:25,701
Don't you think there might be
a clue over there?

2050
01:13:26,656 --> 01:13:29,470
(Could the lucky item be inside the wig?)

2051
01:13:29,495 --> 01:13:30,273
I'm going.

2052
01:13:31,009 --> 01:13:33,404
(Won Ji cautiously approaches.)

2053
01:13:35,275 --> 01:13:36,012
Hey!

2054
01:13:36,437 --> 01:13:37,380
It's a balloon.

2055
01:13:37,947 --> 01:13:38,636
A balloon?

2056
01:13:38,660 --> 01:13:40,183
If we pop it, something has to be inside.

2057
01:13:40,210 --> 01:13:41,751
I'm scared of popping balloons.

2058
01:13:42,750 --> 01:13:44,197
(Pop)

2059
01:13:45,758 --> 01:13:46,923
There's nothing.

2060
01:13:47,323 --> 01:13:49,525
(Venting her anger after finding nothing)

2061
01:13:49,774 --> 01:13:51,542
At times like this,

2062
01:13:51,543 --> 01:13:52,908
we can't break formation.

2063
01:13:52,909 --> 01:13:55,039
- Is something written there?
- We need to stick together.

2064
01:13:55,064 --> 01:13:56,399
(Like a terrified bodyguard)

2065
01:13:57,002 --> 01:13:58,029
(Jingle)

2066
01:13:59,363 --> 01:14:00,476
(Not there.)

2067
01:14:02,804 --> 01:14:04,173
(The bell rings again.)

2068
01:14:04,473 --> 01:14:05,808
I hear a bell.

2069
01:14:06,142 --> 01:14:07,209
I hear a bell.

2070
01:14:07,510 --> 01:14:08,210
Behind us.

2071
01:14:08,517 --> 01:14:09,723
- Behind us?
- This way.

2072
01:14:09,724 --> 01:14:10,513
In front?

2073
01:14:11,710 --> 01:14:13,784
(Following the chime,
they venture deeper inside.)

2074
01:14:13,785 --> 01:14:14,784
This is the right way.

2075
01:14:15,084 --> 01:14:16,285
- Is this right?
- Yes.

2076
01:14:17,920 --> 01:14:18,917
Seriously, where is it?

2077
01:14:18,918 --> 01:14:20,389
We've come way too far in.

2078
01:14:20,817 --> 01:14:22,007
Getting back out is going to be a pain.

2079
01:14:22,008 --> 01:14:23,492
I'm sweating so much.

2080
01:14:24,668 --> 01:14:25,761
There's something here.

2081
01:14:27,296 --> 01:14:29,265
- It's a suitcase.
- A suitcase.

2082
01:14:29,508 --> 01:14:30,599
It's a suitcase.

2083
01:14:30,641 --> 01:14:32,335
This is seriously creepy.

2084
01:14:32,431 --> 01:14:33,536
I'll bring it over.

2085
01:14:33,736 --> 01:14:34,513
Good idea.

2086
01:14:34,605 --> 01:14:36,138
Rimu Queen, you can do it.

2087
01:14:37,516 --> 01:14:38,316
Why?

2088
01:14:38,411 --> 01:14:40,609
Did they give us another suitcase?

2089
01:14:40,610 --> 01:14:43,212
- It's a lucky suitcase, it says.
- Really?

2090
01:14:43,662 --> 01:14:44,413
For real?

2091
01:14:44,814 --> 01:14:45,681
Finally?

2092
01:14:45,829 --> 01:14:46,582
It's...

2093
01:14:46,762 --> 01:14:48,762
It's a bigger suitcase!

2094
01:14:49,994 --> 01:14:51,048
- It's much bigger.
- Great.

2095
01:14:51,817 --> 01:14:53,723
"This is your reward."

2096
01:14:53,724 --> 01:14:57,326
"Exchange your original suitcase
for this larger one."

2097
01:14:57,425 --> 01:14:58,494
Okay.

2098
01:15:00,091 --> 01:15:01,223
Okay.

2099
01:15:01,248 --> 01:15:02,795
So we just take this with us now?

2100
01:15:02,796 --> 01:15:04,100
Is this bigger than ours?

2101
01:15:04,101 --> 01:15:06,274
- Way bigger.
- Right.

2102
01:15:06,299 --> 01:15:07,208
Thank goodness.

2103
01:15:07,209 --> 01:15:08,471
I have no idea where we are.

2104
01:15:08,472 --> 01:15:10,172
Let's get out.

2105
01:15:10,252 --> 01:15:11,273
We should go back.

2106
01:15:12,187 --> 01:15:14,110
It's scary.

2107
01:15:14,605 --> 01:15:16,925
(The bell rings even louder.)

2108
01:15:17,538 --> 01:15:19,311
(Pure panic)

2109
01:15:19,795 --> 01:15:22,631
(Ensuring the walk back isn't too quiet)

2110
01:15:22,986 --> 01:15:26,489
I can't lead,
but I can't be in the back either!

2111
01:15:26,490 --> 01:15:29,303
(Quickly rushing back toward the entrance)

2112
01:15:29,416 --> 01:15:32,710
Don't even try dropping anything.
I see right through you.

2113
01:15:33,002 --> 01:15:34,790
(Keeping their eyes glued to the ceiling)

2114
01:15:35,596 --> 01:15:36,665
This is seriously terrifying.

2115
01:15:38,349 --> 01:15:39,335
This is seriously terrifying.

2116
01:15:39,342 --> 01:15:40,736
Yes, this is so scary.

2117
01:15:42,829 --> 01:15:43,649
(What on earth did she see?)

2118
01:15:43,650 --> 01:15:45,742
That's so creepy.

2119
01:15:45,743 --> 01:15:46,675
- Why?
- What's that?

2120
01:15:46,729 --> 01:15:48,129
(Won Ji suddenly completely freezes up.)

2121
01:15:48,229 --> 01:15:49,178
It's a real ghost.

2122
01:15:49,445 --> 01:15:50,613
It really is.

2123
01:15:50,702 --> 01:15:52,281
Did you see a ghost?

2124
01:15:55,502 --> 01:15:57,186
Let's go.

2125
01:15:59,264 --> 01:16:02,792
Hang in there till the end.
There are stairs here too.

2126
01:16:03,999 --> 01:16:04,827
Okay.

2127
01:16:05,077 --> 01:16:06,899
- It's raining.
- It's raining.

2128
01:16:06,951 --> 01:16:08,631
- No way.
- This happened to me last time too.

2129
01:16:08,632 --> 01:16:11,200
Why does it always rain
right after we finish?

2130
01:16:11,201 --> 01:16:13,201
It's insane.

2131
01:16:13,568 --> 01:16:15,037
It always pours when we're done.

2132
01:16:15,638 --> 01:16:16,806
I'm completely drained.

2133
01:16:16,841 --> 01:16:19,542
How can someone
just stand there alone like that?

2134
01:16:20,176 --> 01:16:22,578
Someone was up on the balcony.

2135
01:16:24,213 --> 01:16:26,877
They were just standing there
staring blankly.

2136
01:16:26,878 --> 01:16:28,374
That was one of the crew, right?

2137
01:16:28,507 --> 01:16:30,019
- Wait, they're not there?
- Are they gone now?

2138
01:16:30,044 --> 01:16:32,688
(The expressionless figure
they all supposedly saw)

2139
01:16:32,689 --> 01:16:33,722
Wasn't that a producer?

2140
01:16:34,023 --> 01:16:36,726
(The crew couldn't have
accessed that area.)

2141
01:16:37,593 --> 01:16:39,195
Wait, so it really was a ghost?

2142
01:16:39,728 --> 01:16:41,831
When we were leaving the theater,

2143
01:16:42,131 --> 01:16:46,435
I said I was scared, and they just
stood there staring like this.

2144
01:16:46,460 --> 01:16:49,095
- Yes, with zero expression.
- Completely blank.

2145
01:16:49,195 --> 01:16:50,540
- Really?
- Yes.

2146
01:16:52,143 --> 01:16:57,202
(The footage shows nothing
at that moment.)

2147
01:16:57,646 --> 01:16:59,482
Stop lying. I saw it too.

2148
01:16:59,483 --> 01:17:00,850
(A darkened face)

2149
01:17:01,216 --> 01:17:03,686
I was sweating so much.

2150
01:17:04,620 --> 01:17:05,914
I keep thinking about it.

2151
01:17:05,915 --> 01:17:09,859
I was walking while holding
Harimu's hand so tightly.

2152
01:17:09,881 --> 01:17:11,781
Then the second the wig dropped,

2153
01:17:11,782 --> 01:17:13,782
I let go of her hand and flew backward.

2154
01:17:14,259 --> 01:17:15,998
I had no clue what was happening.

2155
01:17:16,023 --> 01:17:17,254
(The fastest movement
since arriving in Thailand)

2156
01:17:17,279 --> 01:17:20,936
And then Hye Rim was
in this full scorpion pose.

2157
01:17:21,706 --> 01:17:22,979
She was literally like this.

2158
01:17:22,992 --> 01:17:24,379
(Transformed into a scorpion)

2159
01:17:24,546 --> 01:17:28,010
That's my desperate survival pose.

2160
01:17:29,809 --> 01:17:31,747
I was like this.

2161
01:17:32,081 --> 01:17:34,083
- Exactly like that.
- She really was.

2162
01:17:34,084 --> 01:17:36,118
It's a desperate pose for survival.

2163
01:17:36,700 --> 01:17:38,420
It was so funny.

2164
01:17:39,553 --> 01:17:42,024
We can use this tomorrow.

2165
01:17:43,900 --> 01:17:45,995
I didn't realize
there'd be such a difference.

2166
01:17:45,996 --> 01:17:47,363
There really is a huge difference.

2167
01:17:47,647 --> 01:17:48,764
There really is.

2168
01:17:48,840 --> 01:17:51,700
Because we trusted each other,
we were able to pull this off.

2169
01:17:51,867 --> 01:17:54,270
Our teamwork was great.

2170
01:17:54,271 --> 01:17:55,037
High five.

2171
01:17:57,817 --> 01:17:59,909
We beat the ghost.

2172
01:18:00,337 --> 01:18:02,337
Get out of here, ghost!

2173
01:18:02,397 --> 01:18:04,171
We got a big suitcase.

2174
01:18:04,172 --> 01:18:05,714
I'm so happy.

2175
01:18:06,648 --> 01:18:08,217
We have way more room now.

2176
01:18:11,392 --> 01:18:13,622
(The ghost detector suddenly goes wild.)

2177
01:18:13,623 --> 01:18:14,924
The light turned red.

2178
01:18:15,206 --> 01:18:16,292
Let me out.

2179
01:18:16,453 --> 01:18:17,993
Let's pack up and go.

2180
01:18:17,994 --> 01:18:21,054
(Fleeing the scene)

2181
01:18:21,055 --> 01:18:23,799
- Let's get out before it attaches to us.
- Let's go.

2182
01:18:23,874 --> 01:18:27,336
- Don't attach to us.
- Don't follow us.

2183
01:18:27,337 --> 01:18:29,638
- Let me go get some salt.
- Good idea.

2184
01:18:31,377 --> 01:18:34,490
(The abandoned theater
falls silent once again.)

2185
01:18:36,017 --> 01:18:43,710
(What did they actually see that night?)

2186
01:18:44,363 --> 01:18:48,921
(Heading back to the lodge
before the night grows deeper)

2187
01:18:49,858 --> 01:18:52,494
I seriously need to use the bathroom.

2188
01:18:52,602 --> 01:18:55,515
(B-lining straight for the bathroom
upon arrival)

2189
01:18:56,089 --> 01:18:58,615
(Just how urgent was it?)

2190
01:18:58,635 --> 01:19:00,002
I'm dying.

2191
01:19:00,382 --> 01:19:02,571
Oh, I'm dying.

2192
01:19:02,572 --> 01:19:04,173
I should've used this
to beat up the ghost.

2193
01:19:04,602 --> 01:19:05,255
(Whack)

2194
01:19:05,782 --> 01:19:08,222
(Now that it's over,
her confidence is back.)

2195
01:19:09,829 --> 01:19:11,834
(Rejoining the crew completely refreshed)

2196
01:19:11,835 --> 01:19:13,215
I feel so much better.

2197
01:19:13,315 --> 01:19:14,583
Laundry time.

2198
01:19:14,584 --> 01:19:17,553
These are towels, so take one each.

2199
01:19:17,702 --> 01:19:18,921
And this one is Harimu's.

2200
01:19:18,922 --> 01:19:20,256
(Elephant pants returning
to their rightful owner)

2201
01:19:20,257 --> 01:19:21,490
The red ones.

2202
01:19:23,077 --> 01:19:24,893
There's a hole right here.

2203
01:19:27,099 --> 01:19:27,796
It's sexy.

2204
01:19:27,797 --> 01:19:29,665
Mine got a hole in them too.

2205
01:19:30,232 --> 01:19:31,615
Sexy.

2206
01:19:31,967 --> 01:19:33,702
I had no idea mine ended up like this.

2207
01:19:33,703 --> 01:19:35,304
Mine did too.

2208
01:19:36,939 --> 01:19:39,108
I feel like I sweated out two kilos today.

2209
01:19:40,170 --> 01:19:42,645
- Let's meet up after showering.
- Sounds good.

2210
01:19:42,806 --> 01:19:43,846
Okay.

2211
01:19:45,676 --> 01:19:47,116
(Gabee finishes showering first)

2212
01:19:47,362 --> 01:19:49,116
(Rummaging around)

2213
01:19:49,117 --> 01:19:50,286
Yesterday,

2214
01:19:51,287 --> 01:19:53,076
I felt bad about the Secret Santa gift
I gave you.

2215
01:19:53,077 --> 01:19:54,523
Did you buy something else?

2216
01:19:55,030 --> 01:19:56,325
What's that?

2217
01:19:56,357 --> 01:19:58,060
You said you wanted a headscarf.

2218
01:20:00,462 --> 01:20:01,996
When did you buy this?

2219
01:20:01,997 --> 01:20:04,065
(Before leaving for the lucky spot)

2220
01:20:04,066 --> 01:20:04,932
Thank you.

2221
01:20:05,334 --> 01:20:08,202
I feel like I didn't do
Secret Santa properly.

2222
01:20:08,537 --> 01:20:10,605
So I bought something for Won Ji.

2223
01:20:10,606 --> 01:20:11,940
This looks perfect for her.

2224
01:20:12,708 --> 01:20:14,676
- It looks so cute.
- This is awesome.

2225
01:20:15,878 --> 01:20:17,011
(Cuteness score up)

2226
01:20:17,012 --> 01:20:18,580
I'm going to put this on tomorrow.

2227
01:20:18,581 --> 01:20:19,347
Right away.

2228
01:20:19,348 --> 01:20:22,083
It just screamed Won Ji.

2229
01:20:22,518 --> 01:20:23,752
I'm wearing it tomorrow.

2230
01:20:26,422 --> 01:20:28,790
Gabee's so considerate.

2231
01:20:28,791 --> 01:20:29,891
Yes.

2232
01:20:29,892 --> 01:20:31,626
Are you still doing
your Secret Santa stuff?

2233
01:20:31,627 --> 01:20:33,695
This is so wholesome.

2234
01:20:34,797 --> 01:20:36,263
It looks perfect for you.

2235
01:20:36,264 --> 01:20:37,598
(Appreciating)

2236
01:20:37,900 --> 01:20:39,067
Thanks so much.

2237
01:20:39,068 --> 01:20:40,401
You're welcome.

2238
01:20:41,537 --> 01:20:43,405
The bandana is so pretty.

2239
01:20:44,540 --> 01:20:45,407
It was a good buy.

2240
01:20:46,175 --> 01:20:48,910
I'm going to unbox my gift too.

2241
01:20:49,945 --> 01:20:51,312
It's just so cute.

2242
01:20:52,382 --> 01:20:54,482
(Muhaha)

2243
01:20:54,684 --> 01:20:56,317
Elephants are so cute.

2244
01:20:56,318 --> 01:20:58,019
(Elephant-obsessed)

2245
01:20:58,420 --> 01:20:59,587
The colors are just so pretty.

2246
01:20:59,588 --> 01:21:00,988
I just think the blue one is so pretty.

2247
01:21:00,989 --> 01:21:02,323
(Relaxing after a shower)

2248
01:21:02,992 --> 01:21:06,328
(After recuperating)

2249
01:21:09,431 --> 01:21:10,531
That's cute.

2250
01:21:11,334 --> 01:21:14,335
Toadie, golden toadie.

2251
01:21:15,170 --> 01:21:16,904
You lost three today?

2252
01:21:17,040 --> 01:21:17,972
Your nails?

2253
01:21:18,107 --> 01:21:21,342
They're falling off one by one.

2254
01:21:21,577 --> 01:21:23,711
Harimu's pedicures are cute too.

2255
01:21:23,712 --> 01:21:24,546
(Demure)

2256
01:21:24,681 --> 01:21:25,647
By the way,

2257
01:21:27,850 --> 01:21:29,584
the person in the projection room...

2258
01:21:29,885 --> 01:21:30,751
wasn't our producer.

2259
01:21:31,054 --> 01:21:31,713
No way.

2260
01:21:31,738 --> 01:21:33,631
(Hot topic: the ghost's identity)

2261
01:21:33,656 --> 01:21:35,423
No way.

2262
01:21:35,424 --> 01:21:36,925
But wait.

2263
01:21:36,926 --> 01:21:38,327
I thought it was him over there.

2264
01:21:38,927 --> 01:21:40,496
- Right.
- Wasn't it you?

2265
01:21:41,063 --> 01:21:41,929
It really wasn't you?

2266
01:21:41,930 --> 01:21:43,765
If it really wasn't him...

2267
01:21:44,566 --> 01:21:46,233
- It really wasn't you?
- No way.

2268
01:21:46,501 --> 01:21:48,437
I thought you were the person
in the second-floor projection room.

2269
01:21:49,071 --> 01:21:51,172
This is so chilling. For real?

2270
01:21:52,141 --> 01:21:53,842
All four of us saw it.

2271
01:21:53,843 --> 01:21:56,210
It was definitely a person, not a ghost.

2272
01:21:56,211 --> 01:21:59,347
Come on, stop messing with us.

2273
01:21:59,348 --> 01:22:00,348
Won Ji, you saw it, right?

2274
01:22:00,349 --> 01:22:02,951
Was there even a projection room?

2275
01:22:03,185 --> 01:22:05,219
I guess so, since it was a theater.

2276
01:22:05,421 --> 01:22:06,955
"I guess so, since it was a theater."

2277
01:22:06,956 --> 01:22:08,356
I love answers like that.

2278
01:22:09,124 --> 01:22:10,993
So nobody went to the projection room?

2279
01:22:11,292 --> 01:22:12,593
I think they're telling the truth.

2280
01:22:12,594 --> 01:22:14,528
Really?

2281
01:22:14,529 --> 01:22:16,397
It really wasn't you guys?

2282
01:22:17,332 --> 01:22:19,500
I don't think I'm sleeping tonight.

2283
01:22:19,501 --> 01:22:20,803
Is that for real?

2284
01:22:20,828 --> 01:22:22,603
(Did we see a ghost?)

2285
01:22:22,604 --> 01:22:25,040
I'm sleeping in Gabee's bed tonight.

2286
01:22:25,808 --> 01:22:28,109
Can you wash your hair first, Won Ji?

2287
01:22:28,511 --> 01:22:30,145
(Can you wash your hair?)

2288
01:22:30,510 --> 01:22:33,010
(Hair smell scarier than a ghost)

2289
01:22:33,348 --> 01:22:35,916
It was so hard to get through that door.

2290
01:22:36,685 --> 01:22:38,086
Remember the wig dropping down on us?

2291
01:22:38,754 --> 01:22:40,122
And on the way back, there was a ghost.

2292
01:22:40,622 --> 01:22:42,223
- Wig ghost.
- Also, scorpion.

2293
01:22:43,158 --> 01:22:45,459
(Harimu: dancer and scorpion)

2294
01:22:45,460 --> 01:22:48,729
That pose just comes out
when I'm at death's door.

2295
01:22:48,964 --> 01:22:50,198
You mean when you're scared?

2296
01:22:50,199 --> 01:22:52,199
Have you ever almost died?

2297
01:22:52,200 --> 01:22:53,777
When did you do the scorpion pose?

2298
01:22:53,802 --> 01:22:55,603
Whenever I was scared.

2299
01:22:56,872 --> 01:22:58,506
(Scorpion mode)

2300
01:23:00,476 --> 01:23:01,976
(Touched)

2301
01:23:02,811 --> 01:23:04,845
We can see inside your shorts.

2302
01:23:06,315 --> 01:23:08,316
(Spicy underwear reveal)

2303
01:23:08,317 --> 01:23:10,018
But nobody else saw it.

2304
01:23:10,019 --> 01:23:11,052
I thought I might share it.

2305
01:23:11,053 --> 01:23:11,919
(Stronger bond forged)

2306
01:23:12,187 --> 01:23:13,754
But we really need some salt.

2307
01:23:13,889 --> 01:23:16,157
There definitely is a ghost.

2308
01:23:16,392 --> 01:23:17,926
Definitely there is.

2309
01:23:17,927 --> 01:23:18,493
(Clang)

2310
01:23:19,995 --> 01:23:20,561
(Clang)

2311
01:23:22,998 --> 01:23:26,801
(Rushing in)

2312
01:23:27,036 --> 01:23:28,803
(Screaming)

2313
01:23:28,804 --> 01:23:29,704
I can't!

2314
01:23:29,705 --> 01:23:31,739
What, what is it?

2315
01:23:32,074 --> 01:23:33,508
(Huddled)

2316
01:23:33,676 --> 01:23:35,377
What? Who was that?

2317
01:23:35,378 --> 01:23:36,510
Did someone go upstairs?

2318
01:23:36,712 --> 01:23:38,245
There's someone else here?

2319
01:23:38,246 --> 01:23:39,280
This is so chilling.

2320
01:23:39,281 --> 01:23:41,916
Stop messing with me.

2321
01:23:42,785 --> 01:23:43,819
That must have been the boiler.

2322
01:23:43,820 --> 01:23:46,287
No, it sounded like the toad instrument.

2323
01:23:46,288 --> 01:23:47,956
No, it sounded like a bell.

2324
01:23:48,358 --> 01:23:49,157
I thought it sounded like this.

2325
01:23:49,158 --> 01:23:50,025
(Slithering)

2326
01:23:50,026 --> 01:23:51,092
Yes, it sounded like this.

2327
01:23:51,193 --> 01:23:53,027
No, it was a bell.

2328
01:23:53,028 --> 01:23:54,762
I thought someone was going upstairs?

2329
01:23:54,763 --> 01:23:57,665
But there's nothing on the third floor.

2330
01:23:57,666 --> 01:23:59,233
I was just there.

2331
01:23:59,334 --> 01:24:00,968
How are we sleeping tonight?

2332
01:24:01,704 --> 01:24:02,971
Let's go.

2333
01:24:02,972 --> 01:24:03,638
Where?

2334
01:24:03,972 --> 01:24:05,373
- Upstairs.
- Good luck.

2335
01:24:05,374 --> 01:24:06,640
Be the first, Gabee.

2336
01:24:06,641 --> 01:24:08,109
Won Ji!

2337
01:24:08,110 --> 01:24:09,310
Come on, leader.

2338
01:24:09,311 --> 01:24:11,011
(Not listening)

2339
01:24:12,347 --> 01:24:13,614
Let me go.

2340
01:24:13,615 --> 01:24:14,648
I don't think there's anything.

2341
01:24:14,649 --> 01:24:16,416
It's so silly how we're all going.

2342
01:24:16,417 --> 01:24:19,053
Gabee, are you trying
to sneak to the back?

2343
01:24:19,054 --> 01:24:20,321
(Going to the back)

2344
01:24:20,322 --> 01:24:21,822
Let's have our scorpion lead the way.

2345
01:24:21,957 --> 01:24:23,291
Okay.

2346
01:24:23,358 --> 01:24:25,359
It was a bell.

2347
01:24:26,195 --> 01:24:27,562
I definitely heard a bell.

2348
01:24:27,763 --> 01:24:29,798
I thought it was a person going like this.

2349
01:24:30,799 --> 01:24:33,134
(Cracking up)

2350
01:24:33,403 --> 01:24:35,203
This is scary, just this.

2351
01:24:36,205 --> 01:24:38,273
(The scorpion crawls up.)

2352
01:24:38,740 --> 01:24:40,808
(Standing still)

2353
01:24:40,809 --> 01:24:42,110
Won Ji, why aren't you joining us?

2354
01:24:42,277 --> 01:24:43,544
(Howling)

2355
01:24:44,122 --> 01:24:45,022
Is anybody on the second floor?

2356
01:24:46,434 --> 01:24:48,225
(Come here, Won Ji.)

2357
01:24:48,250 --> 01:24:50,885
I think something is
in Gabee and Won Ji's room.

2358
01:24:51,620 --> 01:24:53,221
No way.

2359
01:24:53,655 --> 01:24:54,889
No way.

2360
01:24:54,890 --> 01:24:57,158
There's something up there.

2361
01:24:57,159 --> 01:24:59,326
I found this.

2362
01:24:59,327 --> 01:25:01,161
It's the QR code.

2363
01:25:01,162 --> 01:25:02,029
You found something.

2364
01:25:02,598 --> 01:25:04,165
(Scorpion express)

2365
01:25:04,300 --> 01:25:07,134
Let me scan the QR code.

2366
01:25:08,203 --> 01:25:09,370
Is that our plan for tomorrow?

2367
01:25:09,371 --> 01:25:10,237
I think so.

2368
01:25:12,674 --> 01:25:14,174
What?

2369
01:25:14,543 --> 01:25:15,343
What is it, Won Ji?

2370
01:25:15,577 --> 01:25:17,144
Can we be surprised together?

2371
01:25:17,145 --> 01:25:17,978
Okay.

2372
01:25:18,481 --> 01:25:21,683
Our second stop
for this one-suitcase trip is...

2373
01:25:23,452 --> 01:25:24,519
the mountain city of...

2374
01:25:24,887 --> 01:25:26,221
Chiang Mai.

2375
01:25:30,959 --> 01:25:34,361
(Shining 24 and 7 from day to night)

2376
01:25:34,630 --> 01:25:38,032
(The city of artists)

2377
01:25:38,567 --> 01:25:41,769
(Filled with colorful and unique charm)

2378
01:25:42,237 --> 01:25:44,205
(The jewel of Northern Thailand)

2379
01:25:44,840 --> 01:25:48,543
(Chiang Mai)

2380
01:25:49,711 --> 01:25:50,444
What is it?

2381
01:25:50,445 --> 01:25:51,612
I'm getting annoyed.

2382
01:25:51,613 --> 01:25:52,680
That's not good.

2383
01:25:52,681 --> 01:25:55,249
Don't annoy her. I hate you.

2384
01:25:55,250 --> 01:25:57,951
"For each gram you shed,

2385
01:25:57,952 --> 01:26:00,054
we'll offer extra funds."

2386
01:26:00,923 --> 01:26:03,424
They can't do this
after giving us a bigger bag.

2387
01:26:03,425 --> 01:26:05,693
I thought we had good fortune.

2388
01:26:05,694 --> 01:26:06,627
(Would this be good fortune?)

2389
01:26:06,628 --> 01:26:08,630
I think they're giving us a place to stay.

2390
01:26:09,243 --> 01:26:10,765
- Nice.
- Wait.

2391
01:26:11,233 --> 01:26:12,567
Sian, you'll like this.

2392
01:26:12,968 --> 01:26:13,701
What is it?

2393
01:26:13,702 --> 01:26:15,303
They have elephants there.

2394
01:26:15,837 --> 01:26:16,670
Oh!

2395
01:26:16,671 --> 01:26:17,404
(Squealing)

2396
01:26:20,108 --> 01:26:20,874
Really?

2397
01:26:21,136 --> 01:26:24,605
Our place is called
Chiang Mai Elephant something.

2398
01:26:25,013 --> 01:26:28,248
Maybe we get to feed the elephants.

2399
01:26:29,017 --> 01:26:31,752
It says, "a fantastic place
where you can play with elephants."

2400
01:26:31,753 --> 01:26:33,687
I never thought
we'd get to see an elephant.

2401
01:26:33,688 --> 01:26:34,521
This is so cool.

2402
01:26:34,522 --> 01:26:36,624
I never expected this.

2403
01:26:36,625 --> 01:26:38,225
I'm going to put him on my shoulder.

2404
01:26:38,226 --> 01:26:40,094
I'll put one on each side.

2405
01:26:40,095 --> 01:26:41,195
I'll also wear an elephant shirt...

2406
01:26:41,196 --> 01:26:42,796
and elephant shorts.

2407
01:26:42,797 --> 01:26:43,731
You have elephant shorts?

2408
01:26:43,732 --> 01:26:45,866
Mine are still intact.

2409
01:26:46,134 --> 01:26:47,801
(Certified elephant enthusiast)

2410
01:26:47,802 --> 01:26:50,639
They all told me
about how they want to see elephants.

2411
01:26:50,640 --> 01:26:53,540
Look, an elephant.

2412
01:26:53,541 --> 01:26:55,309
- They've never seen one before.
- Right.

2413
01:26:55,310 --> 01:26:56,376
Never.

2414
01:26:56,545 --> 01:26:58,713
- You've seen one before, Won Ji?
- Yes, I have.

2415
01:26:58,714 --> 01:27:00,815
I never touched one, though.

2416
01:27:00,816 --> 01:27:02,250
- I'm so happy right now.
- Me too.

2417
01:27:02,290 --> 01:27:03,085
Me too.

2418
01:27:03,719 --> 01:27:05,353
(Shake it if you love elephants.)

2419
01:27:05,354 --> 01:27:06,354
(Cheering)

2420
01:27:06,355 --> 01:27:08,189
(So happy just because of the elephant)

2421
01:27:08,190 --> 01:27:10,024
Are we going to shoot Reels
with the elephants?

2422
01:27:10,025 --> 01:27:11,159
- I'm in.
- Good.

2423
01:27:11,160 --> 01:27:12,326
Come on.

2424
01:27:12,327 --> 01:27:14,162
They're just so cute. I'm so excited.

2425
01:27:14,163 --> 01:27:15,363
I want to go to bed already.

2426
01:27:15,364 --> 01:27:17,065
Wait, we should pack first.

2427
01:27:17,299 --> 01:27:20,368
Our bag's over here.

2428
01:27:20,369 --> 01:27:21,669
Let's go.

2429
01:27:21,670 --> 01:27:22,703
(The new, bigger bag arrives.)

2430
01:27:23,038 --> 01:27:24,472
Okay, let's get packing.

2431
01:27:24,606 --> 01:27:26,307
We'll bring our stuff down.

2432
01:27:26,308 --> 01:27:27,374
(Sian and Harimu get their luggage.)

2433
01:27:27,677 --> 01:27:30,945
Let me put everything
in the elephant bag Harimu gave me.

2434
01:27:31,480 --> 01:27:33,381
Sian, do you have a spare elephant shirt?

2435
01:27:33,382 --> 01:27:34,449
- Do you want to borrow one?
- Can I?

2436
01:27:34,450 --> 01:27:35,349
Of course.

2437
01:27:35,884 --> 01:27:38,752
(Sharing clothes naturally)

2438
01:27:39,388 --> 01:27:41,923
I've never traveled this light before.

2439
01:27:42,624 --> 01:27:45,226
I think we can let go
of that curling iron.

2440
01:27:45,727 --> 01:27:46,760
Do you need it?

2441
01:27:46,761 --> 01:27:47,661
I don't know.

2442
01:27:47,863 --> 01:27:49,898
I'll leave the discussion
up to the curling iron users.

2443
01:27:49,899 --> 01:27:50,997
I'll talk to them about it.

2444
01:27:50,998 --> 01:27:52,400
Feel free to discuss it among yourselves.

2445
01:27:53,402 --> 01:27:54,769
About the curling iron...

2446
01:27:55,137 --> 01:27:56,437
Do you need it?

2447
01:27:56,438 --> 01:27:58,106
- I don't think so.
- Okay.

2448
01:27:58,107 --> 01:27:58,806
I can let it go.

2449
01:27:58,807 --> 01:27:59,941
What about the beauty device?

2450
01:28:00,208 --> 01:28:01,074
I can let it go.

2451
01:28:02,144 --> 01:28:03,245
You're letting a lot of things go.

2452
01:28:03,270 --> 01:28:04,412
(Detaching after just 3 days)

2453
01:28:04,613 --> 01:28:06,414
- Off goes the beauty device.
- I just don't have time.

2454
01:28:06,415 --> 01:28:07,481
(Curling iron and beauty device out)

2455
01:28:08,083 --> 01:28:09,451
Where's my toad?

2456
01:28:10,652 --> 01:28:12,286
A lot of things are getting shed.

2457
01:28:12,287 --> 01:28:13,454
(In curling iron
and beauty device's place,)

2458
01:28:13,455 --> 01:28:15,189
Three elephants, please.

2459
01:28:15,190 --> 01:28:16,156
(goes toad and elephant.)

2460
01:28:16,325 --> 01:28:17,925
We have to pack the shoes too.

2461
01:28:17,926 --> 01:28:18,960
Right.

2462
01:28:18,961 --> 01:28:19,960
The slippers.

2463
01:28:20,162 --> 01:28:21,028
Let me try.

2464
01:28:21,230 --> 01:28:22,430
You think they'll fit?

2465
01:28:22,731 --> 01:28:23,864
We have more than we thought.

2466
01:28:23,865 --> 01:28:25,099
(The bigger suitcase is soon full.)

2467
01:28:25,100 --> 01:28:25,900
Okay.

2468
01:28:26,668 --> 01:28:28,235
(Heavy)

2469
01:28:28,236 --> 01:28:29,670
It's definitely bigger.

2470
01:28:30,539 --> 01:28:31,739
(Pressing)

2471
01:28:31,740 --> 01:28:33,374
I can't close it.

2472
01:28:33,375 --> 01:28:34,542
(Full of greed)

2473
01:28:35,577 --> 01:28:36,644
Let's open it back up.

2474
01:28:36,645 --> 01:28:38,279
Let's take the slippers out.

2475
01:28:38,914 --> 01:28:39,947
We'll carry them to the car.

2476
01:28:40,588 --> 01:28:42,589
They're light, but bulky.

2477
01:28:42,617 --> 01:28:44,252
I don't like it.

2478
01:28:44,586 --> 01:28:46,420
This should be enough.

2479
01:28:46,955 --> 01:28:48,022
Okay.

2480
01:28:48,256 --> 01:28:49,457
I think we can close it.

2481
01:28:50,625 --> 01:28:51,725
(Successfully closed)

2482
01:28:51,726 --> 01:28:52,393
Okay.

2483
01:28:53,361 --> 01:28:54,861
Okay, let's get the scale.

2484
01:28:54,862 --> 01:28:56,663
(Bringing out the scale)

2485
01:28:57,332 --> 01:28:59,500
For every 100 grams we shed...

2486
01:29:00,035 --> 01:29:02,937
Wait, they'll give us 10 dollars.

2487
01:29:02,938 --> 01:29:04,171
(Every 100 gs are 10 dollars less.)

2488
01:29:04,440 --> 01:29:07,441
But if we go over, we have to pay a fine.

2489
01:29:08,210 --> 01:29:09,177
Can you try lifting it?

2490
01:29:09,344 --> 01:29:11,545
Let my brain calculate.

2491
01:29:12,114 --> 01:29:13,715
(Drumroll)

2492
01:29:13,716 --> 01:29:15,182
Wow.

2493
01:29:15,283 --> 01:29:17,885
I think this is over 20 kg.

2494
01:29:17,886 --> 01:29:18,685
Really?

2495
01:29:19,888 --> 01:29:21,021
Right.

2496
01:29:21,223 --> 01:29:22,357
We should take some out.

2497
01:29:22,491 --> 01:29:24,759
We have to. Because...

2498
01:29:25,827 --> 01:29:27,128
- Okay.
- The stakes are too high.

2499
01:29:27,596 --> 01:29:29,297
It's 10 dollars per 100 g.

2500
01:29:29,298 --> 01:29:31,365
(Not ready to lose even a cent)

2501
01:29:33,068 --> 01:29:35,302
Let's take out some non-essentials.

2502
01:29:35,470 --> 01:29:37,671
Sian, I think yours is a bit too big.

2503
01:29:38,407 --> 01:29:39,907
It is kind of big.

2504
01:29:40,242 --> 01:29:41,108
It's heavy too.

2505
01:29:41,176 --> 01:29:42,576
But I just have one.

2506
01:29:42,577 --> 01:29:43,410
(Thick)

2507
01:29:43,813 --> 01:29:45,079
What's in here?

2508
01:29:46,414 --> 01:29:47,147
It's big.

2509
01:29:47,449 --> 01:29:49,116
Let me just take out the heaviest thing.

2510
01:29:49,217 --> 01:29:50,684
This is super heavy.

2511
01:29:50,819 --> 01:29:52,286
These pants are heavy.

2512
01:29:52,287 --> 01:29:53,153
(Leopard print pants out)

2513
01:29:53,355 --> 01:29:54,288
What about this?

2514
01:29:55,390 --> 01:29:56,623
Oh, that one?

2515
01:29:57,392 --> 01:29:58,225
(Next candidate: wedding dress)

2516
01:29:58,250 --> 01:30:00,331
I don't think that one's too heavy.

2517
01:30:00,356 --> 01:30:01,563
Let's take this out.

2518
01:30:01,564 --> 01:30:02,330
Take it out?

2519
01:30:02,790 --> 01:30:04,549
- I don't think we'll wear it.
- You're not going to wear it?

2520
01:30:04,550 --> 01:30:05,563
Well.

2521
01:30:05,564 --> 01:30:06,434
Let's take it out.

2522
01:30:07,103 --> 01:30:08,994
You're taking it out
because you don't want to wear it, right?

2523
01:30:09,019 --> 01:30:10,306
How did you know?

2524
01:30:10,939 --> 01:30:12,040
Then I'm putting it back in.

2525
01:30:12,159 --> 01:30:13,675
Do you have anything you can wear?

2526
01:30:13,853 --> 01:30:15,076
The hair straightener is in there.

2527
01:30:15,077 --> 01:30:17,003
I took one out earlier,
but there's another one inside.

2528
01:30:17,004 --> 01:30:19,147
What is this? My last worldly possession?

2529
01:30:19,504 --> 01:30:20,649
Let's just put it in for now.

2530
01:30:20,650 --> 01:30:22,384
(We'll let this one slide
if you love it that much.)

2531
01:30:22,443 --> 01:30:23,351
All right.

2532
01:30:23,483 --> 01:30:24,753
What's this?

2533
01:30:25,120 --> 01:30:27,076
My clothes.

2534
01:30:27,077 --> 01:30:27,856
Hold on.

2535
01:30:28,750 --> 01:30:30,630
I think there's something in here.

2536
01:30:30,631 --> 01:30:32,060
- Show me.
- It's just clothes.

2537
01:30:32,061 --> 01:30:33,795
- What's in there?
- Take out whatever you can.

2538
01:30:33,894 --> 01:30:34,394
But...

2539
01:30:35,054 --> 01:30:37,265
These pants are heavy.
Aren't you going to wear them tomorrow?

2540
01:30:37,532 --> 01:30:39,739
- These are a bit heavy.
- Right.

2541
01:30:39,740 --> 01:30:41,770
Then I should set aside
what I'm going to wear tomorrow too.

2542
01:30:41,834 --> 01:30:43,405
I'm going to wear this tomorrow.

2543
01:30:43,860 --> 01:30:46,007
(Declaring that pajamas count
as getting dressed up)

2544
01:30:46,241 --> 01:30:48,241
If it's going to be too heavy,
I should wear the pants.

2545
01:30:48,242 --> 01:30:49,244
I should wear this tomorrow.

2546
01:30:49,245 --> 01:30:51,294
- It's much lighter now, right?
- It went down a lot.

2547
01:30:51,295 --> 01:30:52,247
It's totally flat now.

2548
01:30:52,721 --> 01:30:54,382
We really took out a lot.

2549
01:30:54,683 --> 01:30:56,618
This is so easy.

2550
01:30:56,728 --> 01:30:58,954
If we can get it down to about 19 kg,
we'll get 100 dollars.

2551
01:30:59,254 --> 01:31:01,923
Let me try lifting it.

2552
01:31:02,257 --> 01:31:04,592
I think it's about 18 kg.

2553
01:31:04,906 --> 01:31:06,906
Maybe 18.5 kg?

2554
01:31:07,419 --> 01:31:08,666
(Staring)

2555
01:31:09,364 --> 01:31:11,199
But you can't take this out, Sian.
Why did you take this out?

2556
01:31:11,406 --> 01:31:13,969
I have the bag Hye Rim bought me
yesterday.

2557
01:31:14,766 --> 01:31:15,870
Are you okay with this?

2558
01:31:16,338 --> 01:31:18,166
Hold on. I'll just check what's in there.

2559
01:31:18,333 --> 01:31:19,607
You don't need the sunglasses?

2560
01:31:19,941 --> 01:31:21,509
That was close.

2561
01:31:21,510 --> 01:31:23,130
My Gongjindan was in here.

2562
01:31:23,131 --> 01:31:24,946
- Gongjindan.
- Gongjindan.

2563
01:31:24,947 --> 01:31:26,014
- Passport.
- That's precious.

2564
01:31:26,190 --> 01:31:28,057
You were going to throw your passport out?

2565
01:31:28,058 --> 01:31:30,058
You almost couldn't go back to Korea.

2566
01:31:30,718 --> 01:31:32,745
You really have to keep
an eye on these kids.

2567
01:31:32,746 --> 01:31:34,255
I need looking after.

2568
01:31:34,598 --> 01:31:36,424
Okay, let me go.

2569
01:31:37,631 --> 01:31:40,178
(Time to weigh the suitcase)

2570
01:31:40,811 --> 01:31:43,251
(Celebrating prematurely)

2571
01:31:43,871 --> 01:31:45,371
(Even the expanded suitcase
is packed to the brim.)

2572
01:31:45,398 --> 01:31:46,334
Let's see!

2573
01:31:46,901 --> 01:31:48,503
Hold on.

2574
01:31:51,081 --> 01:31:52,340
Hold on.

2575
01:31:54,341 --> 01:31:56,041
(The suitcase weighs 19.65 kg.)

2576
01:31:56,455 --> 01:31:58,662
(Successfully shedding 350 g)

2577
01:31:59,555 --> 01:32:01,048
(The helicopter celebration)

2578
01:32:01,668 --> 01:32:03,088
(It catches on.)

2579
01:32:03,495 --> 01:32:06,048
Give me my money.

2580
01:32:08,900 --> 01:32:11,226
"You received 235 dollars per person..."

2581
01:32:11,366 --> 01:32:13,493
- "for each day of the trip."
- Nice!

2582
01:32:14,193 --> 01:32:15,430
Because of this?

2583
01:32:15,926 --> 01:32:19,667
If the suitcase got bigger
but weighs less,

2584
01:32:19,806 --> 01:32:21,970
that means we really did clear things out.

2585
01:32:22,246 --> 01:32:23,705
Did we really pack everything?

2586
01:32:25,473 --> 01:32:27,175
- I'm getting nervous.
- It does feel a little suspicious.

2587
01:32:27,260 --> 01:32:28,209
That's true.

2588
01:32:28,977 --> 01:32:31,446
Still, we got our spending money.

2589
01:32:31,920 --> 01:32:32,680
Let's sleep.

2590
01:32:32,681 --> 01:32:34,380
- Elephants.
- Elephants.

2591
01:32:34,473 --> 01:32:36,284
I can sleep with Gabee tonight.

2592
01:32:36,618 --> 01:32:38,586
Let's all sleep together tonight.
It's our last night in Bangkok.

2593
01:32:38,607 --> 01:32:39,587
- Sure.
- I love it.

2594
01:32:39,713 --> 01:32:41,222
Come down to this floor.

2595
01:32:41,397 --> 01:32:43,997
- Come down to this floor.
- I'm scared.

2596
01:32:43,998 --> 01:32:46,330
(Their final night in Bangkok
ends on a high note.)

2597
01:32:48,857 --> 01:32:50,899
Next, we're heading to Chiang Mai.

2598
01:32:50,924 --> 01:32:52,845
(To the second terrain, Chiang Mai)

2599
01:32:53,143 --> 01:32:54,503
Let's go.

2600
01:32:54,903 --> 01:32:57,223
(Maximum energy from the start)

2601
01:32:57,409 --> 01:32:58,976
(And the madness catches on.)

2602
01:32:59,289 --> 01:33:01,789
Honey. Babe.

2603
01:33:02,189 --> 01:33:03,247
(Don't leave me out.)

2604
01:33:03,474 --> 01:33:05,527
(The extroverts are having
the time of their lives.)

2605
01:33:05,800 --> 01:33:07,747
(Meanwhile, the introvert is slowly
running out of battery.)

2606
01:33:08,049 --> 01:33:09,319
Bring it up.

2607
01:33:09,507 --> 01:33:11,374
- Bring it up.
- Bring it up.

2608
01:33:12,020 --> 01:33:14,332
(You're too close.)

2609
01:33:14,545 --> 01:33:15,945
(Will she be able to adjust today?)

2610
01:33:16,258 --> 01:33:17,712
There are the elephants.

2611
01:33:17,885 --> 01:33:18,458
Wow.

2612
01:33:18,965 --> 01:33:19,512
Wow.

2613
01:33:19,778 --> 01:33:21,638
(The long-awaited encounter
with elephants)

2614
01:33:22,171 --> 01:33:23,705
This is amazing.

2615
01:33:23,931 --> 01:33:25,563
(Sian's dream comes true?)

2616
01:33:25,810 --> 01:33:28,350
(Starting with an up-close view
of an elephant feast)

2617
01:33:28,703 --> 01:33:31,656
When else would we ever get
to go for a walk with an elephant?

2618
01:33:31,916 --> 01:33:33,003
Look at that.

2619
01:33:33,436 --> 01:33:34,630
This is insane.

2620
01:33:34,850 --> 01:33:36,667
It feels so good.

2621
01:33:36,820 --> 01:33:37,494
(Kissing)

2622
01:33:38,367 --> 01:33:39,240
It really feels like you're connecting.

2623
01:33:39,261 --> 01:33:40,867
One more.

2624
01:33:43,153 --> 01:33:44,947
Hey, you're something else.

2625
01:33:45,201 --> 01:33:47,174
What's wrong with you?

2626
01:33:47,427 --> 01:33:49,485
That's not cool.

2627
01:33:49,891 --> 01:33:52,545
- What are you doing?
- It fell!

2628
01:33:52,712 --> 01:33:55,725
(Their affection grows more intense.)

2629
01:33:56,045 --> 01:33:58,879
(Looks like a fairy tale from afar,
but pure chaos up close)

2630
01:33:59,132 --> 01:34:00,490
It feels like a fairy tale.

2631
01:34:00,514 --> 01:34:02,012
I really can't handle this.

2632
01:34:02,429 --> 01:34:03,378
It's so cute.

2633
01:34:03,712 --> 01:34:05,252
But I'm scared.

2634
01:34:05,805 --> 01:34:09,057
(Will the romance last until the end?)

2635
01:34:09,082 --> 01:34:10,082
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
